serve source R7/R2 and all raw review/deferred evidence\\nreview: docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-review-1.md; complete Alice/Blake/Bob Claude Opus5.5/xhigh; three immutable receipts; Carl operator-skipped; no Eve; provider guard satisfied\\nresult: one confirmed HIGH R5: original-token word boundaries lost by strip-first redaction; original exact R2 cap input passes but repair is not complete; nine bounded fixes grouped into four tasks; five out-of-scope findings settled-deferred; preservation replay rows dismissed with evidence\\nnext: Phase 4 existing-review/unfinished-rework skip \\u2192 installed Phase 6 Dispatch rework and complete installed work pipeline for tasks 6\\u20139; task 6 first, tasks 7\\u20139 depend on it; logical sonnet maps to gpt-6.1-sol/medium, explicit isolated worker settings; retain full tests-first/gates/review/escalation obligations\\ncontract: task 6 must amend design recipe with original-boundary and post-cleanup redaction, preserving cap/classification/reset/control forms; no broad TUI or cyclic-guard expansion; all quoted findings retained verbatim in task bodies\\nverification: reviewed HEAD 4c84d4d; coordinator approved full suite 6884 passed/0 failed/0 skipped; sync, lint, format, mypy, build green; sandbox-failed run and approved retry archived; focused VERIFY queue runs in next work pass\\nprovenance: retain cycle-1 implementation-models.json fingerprint/snapshot through rework; regenerate from all contributing raw logs before cycle-2 review, then driver review-route; do not rewrite original attempt history or treat launcher as model origin\\nhandoff: after rework use canonical phase-done --outcome rework, increment to cycle 2, clear queue and STOP; fresh full opposite-company review next; do not finalize with the HIGH unresolved\\nscope: only 00051\\u201300054; all other held PRDs including 00010 remain held; no global binary/provisioning/publication/live inference/permission changes; final repair-readiness reassessment after all four remains pending\",\n  \"tasks_completed\": 5,\n  \"cycle\": 1,\n  \"review_lenses\": {\n    \"consensus\": \"done\",\n    \"blind\": \"done\",\n    \"doubt\": \"done\"\n  },\n  \"rework_task_ids\": [\n    \"6\",\n    \"7\",\n    \"8\",\n    \"9\"\n  ],\n  \"deferred_decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"issue\": \"`has_invalid_unicode_scalar` never stops on cyclic input. It keeps no record of containers it has already visited, so a payload like `d = {\\\"self\\\": d}` loops forever and its pending list grows without limit. I checked this: `Observation(payload=d)` was still running after 3 s. Before this change the recursive copier raised `RecursionError`, and `RawFirstDecoder` turned that into a `raw.unknown` gap. Now a driver bug that builds a cyclic payload freezes the supervisor's decode path, along with the timeout and cleanup steps that wait on it. Both design reviewers raised this as a non-blocker. Fix: track the `id()` of containers already visited, either skipping them or raising `ValueError`. That is about 3 lines and keeps the scan iterative\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/ovcaq/events/model.py:77\",\n      \"reason\": \"Settled limitation: the reviewed helper contract is explicitly acyclic JSON-like containers; native json.loads cannot create cycles. Preserve the witnessed hang; no cycle-guard scope expansion.\",\n      \"cycle\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"review-deferred\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue\": \"The R2 class of bug still exists at display time, outside this PRD's scope. `bounded_detail` strips only C0 controls and 7-bit CSI. The TUI's `display_text` drops all Cc/Cf/Cs/Zl/Zp characters (src/ovcaq/tui/model.py:57). Confirmed: `\\\"lane sk-abc\\\\u200b<36 chars>\\\"` (also with \\\\x85, \\\\x9b, \\\\u00ad, \\\\u2060 instead of \\\\u200b) passes redaction unchanged and the TUI shows the joined `sk-abcabcdef\\u2026` token. Activity text and tool details (src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:32, src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:127) strip nothing, so a NUL-split token also renders whole on screen. This needs a durable home (a PRD or issue)\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:59\",\n      \"reason\": \"Display-time character stripping/activity UI is excluded by this PRD. Preserve durable follow-up evidence; no implicit expansion of 00054.\",\n      \"cycle\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"review-deferred\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue\": \"The same strip-after-redact bug exists in the TUI. `display_text` drops Cc/Cf characters from already-sanitized activity and tool text without redacting again, so a stored `sk-abc\\\\x00defghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123` shows on screen as the rebuilt token\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"file\": \"src/ovcaq/tui/model.py:136\",\n      \"reason\": \"Same out-of-scope display-time defect as R6; preserve its separate citation and deferral.\",\n      \"cycle\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"review-deferred\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue\": \"The supervisor's catch-all handler builds `SessionSummary(..., str(error), ...)`. If the error text carries surrogateescape bytes (a non-UTF-8 path), the new `SessionSummary` check raises `ValueError` inside the handler and `_conclude` is skipped, so the failure record is lost. Not a regression: the strict encode in src/ovcaq/runtime/_session_io.py:19 already failed on such text\",\n      \"severity\": \"low\",\n      \"file\": \"src/ovcaq/runtime/supervisor.py:370\",\n      \"reason\": \"Pre-existing arbitrary exception/path surrogate handling; retain for later scoped runtime failure work.\",\n      \"cycle\": 1,\n      \"type\": \"review-deferred\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue\": \"The pre-decode check assumes every driver parses frames with plain `json.loads`. A plugin driver that unwraps a prefix or applies its own escapes skips the pre-mutation check. The model still rejects the bad strings, so nothing crashes