+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; print(Path(\\\"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-6.txt\\\").read_text())' \"","aggregated_output":"You are writing tests for a feature. You have NOT seen any implementation and must NOT think about how to implement it.\n\nTask: [D1] src/ovcaq/\n\nDescription:\nTask 6 only. Public behavior: bounded_detail(detail: str) -> str must retain redaction of tokens separated from a preceding word by any recognized C0/DEL/lone ESC control, and redact tokens reconstructed when recognized controls occur inside a token. Test bare sk- credentials and Bearer values independently through helper, native error and turn.failed payloads and saved normalized JSONL. Preserve the original R2 cap input and 4096-character final cap, formatting and original-text classification/reset. RawFirstDecoder must delegate deeply nested native JSON unchanged when preflight json.loads raises RecursionError: assert the native parser gap reason, unchanged adapter state, durable raw bytes and normalized evidence. No expanded control forms, cycles or TUI changes.\nAllowed tests to edit: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py and /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py. Read these two test files and /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/pyproject.toml only. Do not read production implementation. Reading budget: detail tests around lines 1-110 and 145-285; frame fixture lines 1-125 and delegation lines 275-320. Keep changes focused. Run only changed named tests -q --tb=line; do not commit or change state.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\nOriginal-boundary and reconstructed-token inputs are redacted exactly; deep JSON preserves native delegation. All original cases remain unchanged.\n\nExisting test patterns (follow these conventions):\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ovcaq.config import AgentSettings\nfrom ovcaq.drivers.codex import CodexDriver\nfrom ovcaq.drivers.codex_events import bounded_detail\nfrom ovcaq.events.model import Observation\nfrom ovcaq.events.tail import NormalizedEventWriter\n\nTOKEN = \"sk-\" + \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\"\nCAP_REPRODUCER = \"x\" * 4080 + \" sk-abc\\x1b[0mdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\"\nSPLIT_DETAILS = [\n    pytest.param(CAP_REPRODUCER, \"x\" * 4080 + \" [REDACTED]\", id=\"exact-cap\"),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Diagnostic sk-abc\\x1b[31mdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\",\n        \"Diagnostic [REDACTED]\",\n        id=\"ansi-split\",\n    ),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Diagnostic sk-abc\\x00defghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\",\n        \"Diagnostic [REDACTED]\",\n        id=\"nul-split\",\n    ),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Bearer \" + TOKEN,\n        \"Bearer [REDACTED]\",\n        id=\"bearer\",\n    ),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Diagnostic \\x1b]0;\" + TOKEN + \"\\x07 After\",\n        \"Diagnostic ]0;[REDACTED] After\",\n        id=\"osc-controls\",\n    ),\n    *[\n        pytest.param(\n            \"Before \" + token[:6] + control + token[6:] + \" After\",\n            \"Before [REDACTED] After\",\n            id=f\"alternate-{index}-{control_id}\",\n        )\n        for index, token in enumerate([\"sk-\" + \"Q7\" * 20, \"sk-\" + \"4bcD\" * 12])\n        for control_id, control in [\n            (\"plain\", \"\"),\n            (\"ansi\", \"\\x1b[0m\"),\n            (\"nul\", \"\\x00\"),\n        ]\n    ],\n]\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef driver() -> CodexDriver:\n    return CodexDriver(\n        AgentSettings(\n            name=\"codex\",\n            command=(\"fixture-wrapper\",),\n            tiers={\"standard\": \"fixture-model\"},\n            environment={},\n            options={},\n        ),\n        run_id=\"detail-safety-run\",\n    )\n\n\ndef decode_failure(\n    driver: CodexDriver, kind: str, detail: str\n) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\n    record = (\n        {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": detail}\n        if kind == \"error\"\n        else {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": detail}}\n    )\n    return driver.decode(json.dumps(record))\n\n\ndef assert_safe_details(\n    tmp_path: Path, observations: tuple[Observation, ...], expected: str\n) -> None:\n    assert observations\n    for observation in observations:\n        assert observation.payload[\"detail\"] == expected\n        assert len(observation.payload[\"detail\"]) <= 4096\n        assert \"\\x1b\" not in observation.payload[\"detail\"]\n        assert \"\\x00\" not in observation.payload[\"detail\"]\n        assert TOKEN not in expected\n        assert \"sk-abcdefghijkl\" not in expected\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    writer = NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=1 << 20, min_free_bytes=0)\n    try:\n        for observation in observations:\n            writer.write(observation)\n        writer.flush()\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n    saved = path.read_bytes()\n    assert TOKEN.encode() not in saved\n    assert b\"sk-abcdefghijkl\" not in saved\n    assert b\"\\\\u001b\" not in saved\n    assert b\"\\\\u0000\" not in saved\n    records = [json.loads(line) for line in saved.splitlines()]\n    assert len(records) == len(observations)\n    assert all(record[\"payload\"][\"detail\"] == expected for record in records)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"detail\", \"expected\"), SPLIT_DETAILS)\ndef test_bounded_detail_redacts_reconstructed_tokens_before_capping(\n    detail: str, expected: str\n) -> None:\n    actual = bounded_detail(detail)\n    assert actual == expected\n    assert len(actual) <= 4096\n    assert TOKEN not in actual\n    assert \"sk-abcdefghijkl\" not in actual\n    assert \"\\x1b\" not in actual\n    assert \"\\x00\" not in actual\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    (\"detail\", \"expected\"),\n    [\n        (\"\", \"\"),\n        (\"x\" * 4095, \"x\" * 4095),\n        (\"x\" * 4096, \"x\" * 4096),\n        (\"x\" * 4097, \"x\" * 4096),\n        (\"y\" * 4095, \"y\" * 4095),\n        (\"y\" * 4096, \"y\" * 4096),\n        (\"y\" * 4097, \"y\" * 4096),\n        (\"Diagnostic \" * 500, (\"Diagnostic \" * 500)[:4096]),\n        (\"OK\", \"OK\"),\n        (\"Warning!\", \"Warning!\"),\n        (\"First\\nSecond\", \"First\\nSecond\"),\n        (\"First\\tSecond\", \"First\\tSecond\"),\n        (\n            \"A\\x1b[31mB\\x1b[0m\\x00\\x08\\x0b\\x0c\\x0e\\x1f\\x7f\\t\\nC\",\n            \"AB\\t\\nC\",\n        ),\n        (\"\\x00\" * 4096 + \"Visible\", \"Visible\"),\n    ],\n)\ndef test_bounded_detail_preserves_printable_text_and_caps_after_control_removal(\n    detail: str, expected: str\n) -> None:\n    actual = bounded_detail(detail)\n    assert actual == expected\n    assert len(actual) <= 4096\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kind\", [\"error\", \"turn.failed\"])\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"detail\", \"expected\"), SPLIT_DETAILS)\ndef test_native_failure_redacts_diagnostic_payload_and_saved_jsonl(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n    tmp_path: Path,\n    kind: str,\n    detail: str,\n    expected: str,\n) -> None:\n    observations = decode_failure(driver, kind, detail)\n    assert [value.type for value in observations] == [\n        \"activity.message\" if kind == \"error\" else \"session.failed\"\n    ]\n    assert observations[0].payload[\"failure_class\"] == \"unknown\"\n    if kind == \"error\":\n        assert observations[0].payload[\"kind\"] == \"error\"\n        assert observations[0].payload[\"reset_at\"] is None\n    assert_safe_details(tmp_path, observations, expected)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kind\", [\"error\", \"turn.failed\"])\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"detail\", [\"OK\", \"Warning!\", \"First\\nSecond\", \"First\\tSecond\"])\ndef test_native_failure_preserves_short_and_formatted_saved_details(\n    driver: CodexDriver, tmp_path: Path, kind: str, detail: str\n) -> None:\n    observations = decode_failure(driver, kind, detail)\n    assert [value.type for value in observations] == [\n        \"activity.message\" if kind == \"error\" else \"session.failed\"\n    ]\n    assert observations[0].payload[\"failure_class\"] == \"unknown\"\n    assert_safe_details(tmp_path, observations, detail)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kind\", [\"error\", \"turn.failed\"])\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"seconds\", [30, 21600, -1, 21601])\ndef test_native_rate_limit_uses_full_text_for_reset_and_saves_bounded_redaction(\n    driver: CodexDriver, tmp_path: Path, kind: str, seconds: int\n) -> None:\n    detail = CAP_REPRODUCER + f\" HTTP 429; retry after {seconds} seconds\"\n    observations = decode_failure(driver, kind, detail)\n    if kind == \"error\":\n        assert [value.type for value in observations] == [\"activity.message\"]\n        failure = rate = observations[0]\n        assert failure.payload[\"kind\"] == \"error\"\n    else:\n        assert sorted(value.type for value in observations) == [\n            \"rate_limit.started\",\n            \"session.failed\",\n        ]\n        failure = next(\n            value for value in observations if value.type == \"session.failed\"\n        )\n        rate = next(\n            value for value in observations if value.type == \"rate_limit.started\"\n        )\n        assert rate.payload[\"window\"] is None\n    assert failure.payload[\"failure_class\"] == \"rate_limit\"\n    reset_at = rate.payload[\"reset_at\"]\n    if 0 <= seconds <= 21600:\n        assert isinstance(reset_at, str)\n        actual = datetime.fromisoformat(reset_at)\n        assert actual.utcoffset() == timedelta(0)\n        expected_reset = rate.timestamp + timedelta(seconds=seconds)\n        assert abs((actual - expected_reset).total_seconds()) < 1\n    else:\n        assert reset_at is None\n    expected_detail = (\n        \"x\" * 4080 + \" [REDACTED]\" + f\" HTTP 429; retry after {seconds} seconds\"\n    )[:4096]\n    assert_safe_details(tmp_path, observations, expected_detail)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kind\", [\"error\", \"turn.failed\"])\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    (\"native_suffix\", \"expected_class\"),\n    [\n        (\n            \"Unauthorized: HTTP 401; HTTP 429; retry after 30 seconds\",\n            \"authentication\",\n        ),\n        (\"Sandbox denied: HTTP 403\", \"permission\"),\n        (\"Connection reset: HTTP 503\", \"connectivity\"),\n        (\"Request timed out\", \"timeout\"),\n        (\"Unau\\x1b[0mthorized\", \"unknown\"),\n    ],\n)\ndef test_native_failure_preserves_full_original_classification_before_cleaning(\n    driver: CodexDriver, kind: str, native_suffix: str, expected_class: str\n) -> None:\n    detail = \"x\" * 4096 + \" \" + native_suffix\n    observations = decode_failure(driver, kind, detail)\n    failure = next(\n        value\n        for value in observations\n        if value.type == (\"activity.message\" if kind == \"error\" else \"session.failed\")\n    )\n    assert failure.payload[\"failure_class\"] == expected_class\n    assert failure.payload[\"detail\"] == \"x\" * 4096\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"detail\", \"expected\"), SPLIT_DETAILS)\ndef test_receiver_lane_redacts_message_payload_and_saved_jsonl(\n    driver: CodexDriver, tmp_path: Path, detail: str, expected: str\n) -> None:\n    driver.decode(json.dumps({\"type\": \"thread.started\", \"thread_id\": \"parent\"}))\n    observations = driver.decode(\n        json.dumps(\n            {\n                \"type\": \"item.started\",\n                \"item\": {\n                    \"id\": \"collab-1\",\n                    \"type\": \"collab_tool_call\",\n                    \"tool\": \"spawn_agent\",\n                    \"sender_thread_id\": \"parent\",\n                    \"receiver_thread_ids\": [\"child-1\"],\n                    \"prompt\": \"Inspect receiver\",\n                    \"agents_states\": {\n                        \"child-1\": {\"status\": \"running\", \"message\": detail}\n                    },\n                    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n                },\n            }\n        )\n    )\n    lanes = tuple(value for value in observations if value.lane_id == \"child-1\")\n    assert len(lanes) == 1\n    assert lanes[0].type == \"lane.started\"\n    lane_detail = lanes[0].payload[\"detail\"]\n    assert isinstance(lane_detail, str)\n    assert \"\\x1b\" not in lane_detail\n    assert \"\\x00\" not in lane_detail\n    if detail != CAP_REPRODUCER:\n        assert expected in lane_detail\n    assert_safe_details(tmp_path, lanes, lane_detail)\n\n\nPublic interfaces/types relevant to this task:\nbounded_detail(detail: str) -> str\nCodexDriver(AgentSettings(...), run_id: str); decode(frame: str) -> tuple[Observation, ...]\nRawFirstDecoder(raw=SessionEvidenceWriter(...), normalized=NormalizedEventWriter(...), driver=CodexDriver(...), run_id=..., session_id=...); feed(bytes) and finish() -> tuple[Observation,...]. Native malformed frame delegation produces RAW_UNKNOWN with driver-native reason, raw_sha256 and preview. Observation.payload is a mapping. Test fixture unicode_tail and detail driver fixtures are available in the listed test files.\n\nTest framework: pytest\n\nRules:\n1. Write tests from requirements only. You are a USER of this API, not its builder.\n2. Each test name describes a behavior: \"rejects empty email\", \"returns 404 for missing user\"\n3. Assert on outputs, return values, side effects, and errors. Never assert on mock existence.\n4. Cover edge cases: empty input, null/undefined, boundary values, error conditions\n5. Use real code paths. Mock only external dependencies (network, filesystem, databases).\n6. For EACH test, ask yourself: \"What wrong implementation would still pass this?\" If easy to answer, add constraints.\n7. Do not write implementation code. Do not modify non-test files.\n8. Do not add test-only methods to production classes. Use test utilities instead.\n9. SIMPLICITY FIRST: Test only the behavior in the acceptance criteria. Do not add tests for features nobody asked for. If you write 20 tests when 6 cover the spec, cut back.\n10. THINK BEFORE CODING: If the acceptance criteria are ambiguous (unclear input shape, unstated error behavior, multiple valid interpretations), STOP and report the ambiguity instead of picking an interpretation silently.\n10a. NEVER INVENT A CONTRACT: If the task names a data structure (JSON object, API response, enum, config schema, record type) but does not pin its EXACT field names, enum values, or types, STOP and report it as a blocker. Do not invent a plausible schema and test against it — a self-consistent wrong contract is worse than a reported gap, because the implementer will build to your tests and the mistake survives until PRD-level review. Likewise for \"which kind of thing\" choices the task leaves open (e.g. which hook event, which file location). The task description must hand you the exact strings; if it does not, that is a blocker, not a judgement call.\n11. SURGICAL: Only create/modify test files. Match the existing test file's style (quote style, import order, assertion library, naming). Do not reformat sample files you were given for reference.\n12. SIZE LIMITS: keep every test function under 50 lines and every test file under 800 lines; split by behavior into sibling files named after the test module (for example test_events_completion.py, test_events_usage.py) before you exceed either.\n\nDo NOT:\n- Think about how to implement the feature\n- Read or reference implementation files\n- Write stubs, placeholders, or TODO comments\n- Mock internal modules (only mock external boundaries)\n- Create tests that just check a function exists or returns truthy\n\nRead only the files listed above. If a file or symbol you need is not listed, stop and report it as a blocker — do not run broad `rg` sweeps to discover scope.\n\nAbort and report if you read more than 100K of total input. Return the partial result and an abort_reason: context_overrun field.\n\nRead every file before your first Edit to it. Never call bash `head`, `tail`, `cat`, `grep`, or `find` - a hook blocks them. Use the Read tool (offset/limit), `rg`, or `rg --files` instead. Never combine an inspection (read, list, search, diff) with a test, lint or build invocation in one Bash call - run them as two calls, because a combined command has two ways to hang and one exit code. Pass an explicit `timeout` on every Bash call: 60000 ms for an inspection, 300000 ms for a lint run or a narrow test run, 600000 ms for a full suite or a full build.\n\nRun only the test files this task names (the tests you wrote, or the\nfailing tests in your prompt), with `-q --tb=line`. Never run a whole test\ndirectory or `dev/bin/release-checks`: the orchestrator runs the full suite\nonce, after every task. Read the pass count and exit code from that one\nrun; never re-run a suite to recover a number.\n\nEnd your report with `ASSUMPTIONS:` - one line per assumption you made where the task, tests, or listed files were silent (guessed interface, data shape, resolved ambiguity, unstated behavior). Write `ASSUMPTIONS: none` if you made none.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
