+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_114","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\| R[0-9]+' docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-review-1.md\"","aggregated_output":"39:| R1 | [3/3] | 🟡 | The raw-first regressions (byte-exact raw output, gap digest/preview, unchanged adapter state, later healthy terminal) live in `tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py`. The PRD's Task 2 acceptance command (`pytest tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py tests/events/test_tail.py`) and its repository structure both name `test_unicode_safety.py`, so the PRD's own command does not run them. The full suite covers them, and the split keeps the file under 800 lines. Fix: record the file in the PRD or design acceptance text | tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py:1 | 2 | ALICE, BLAKE, BOB |\n40:| R2 | [2/3] | 🟡 | `has_invalid_unicode_scalar` never stops on cyclic input. It keeps no record of containers it has already visited, so a payload like `d = {\"self\": d}` loops forever and its pending list grows without limit. I checked this: `Observation(payload=d)` was still running after 3 s. Before this change the recursive copier raised `RecursionError`, and `RawFirstDecoder` turned that into a `raw.unknown` gap. Now a driver bug that builds a cyclic payload freezes the supervisor's decode path, along with the timeout and cleanup steps that wait on it. Both design reviewers raised this as a non-blocker. Fix: track the `id()` of containers already visited, either skipping them or raising `ValueError`. That is about 3 lines and keeps the scan iterative | src/ovcaq/events/model.py:77 | 1 | ALICE, BOB |\n41:| R3 | [2/3] | 🟡 | The receiver-lane test special-cases the exact cap input with `if detail != CAP_REPRODUCER`. It then calls `assert_safe_details(tmp_path, lanes, lane_detail)`, which compares the lane detail to itself, so the cap case never checks the exact redacted value or that `[REDACTED]` is present. I confirmed the actual lane detail equals the expected `\"x\"*4080 + \" [REDACTED]\"`. Simpler and stronger: drop the guard and call `assert_safe_details(tmp_path, lanes, expected)`. Related: `assert TOKEN not in expected` and `assert \"sk-abcdefghijkl\" not in expected` (lines 87-88) check fixed test data inside the loop. They should check `observation.payload[\"detail\"]` | tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py:281 | 3 | ALICE, BOB |\n42:| R4 | [2/3] | ⚪ | Hot-path scan cost. `_payload` scans the whole payload at line 224, then `sanitize_json` scans it again at line 252, and `_usage_payload` scans again through `sanitize_json`. Each scan uses a per-character Python generator: about 22 ms per MiB, against about 2.5 ms for a precompiled `re.compile(\"[\\ud800-\\udfff]\").search`. Every frame also gets re-validated by `replace()` in `_bind_observations` and by `observation_record` in the writer. Behavior-preserving fix: use the regex in the predicate, and call `_sanitize_json` inside `_payload` and `_usage_payload` once the up-front check has passed | src/ovcaq/events/model.py:224 | 1 | ALICE, BOB |\n43:| R5 | [1/3] | 🟠 | Removing controls before redaction now leaks tokens that the old order caught. When a bare C0 control, DEL or lone ESC sits between a word character and a token, removal glues them together: `\"x\\x00sk-\" + \"a\"*30` becomes `xsk-aaaa…` and `\"auth\\x00Bearer \" + \"a\"*26` becomes `authBearer …`. `_LIKELY_SECRET` needs `\\b` before `sk-`/`Bearer`, so neither `bounded_detail` nor the Observation's second sanitizer redacts them. The old order redacted both, because the control supplied the word boundary. Confirmed by tracing the regex by hand; not executed (read-only sandbox) | src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:64 | 3 | BOB |\n44:| R6 | [1/3] | 🟡 | The R2 class of bug still exists at display time, outside this PRD's scope. `bounded_detail` strips only C0 controls and 7-bit CSI. The TUI's `display_text` drops all Cc/Cf/Cs/Zl/Zp characters (src/ovcaq/tui/model.py:57). Confirmed: `\"lane sk-abc\\u200b<36 chars>\"` (also with \\x85, \\x9b, \\u00ad, \\u2060 instead of \\u200b) passes redaction unchanged and the TUI shows the joined `sk-abcabcdef…` token. Activity text and tool details (src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:32, src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:127) strip nothing, so a NUL-split token also renders whole on screen. This needs a durable home (a PRD or issue) | src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:59 | 3 | BLAKE |\n45:| R7 | [1/3] | 🟡 | The preflight's `except (ValueError, RecursionError)` branch, which hands the frame to the driver, has no test. No RawFirstDecoder test feeds a deeply nested frame. Narrowing it to `except ValueError` would still pass the suite: deep frames would then get \"driver failed to decode frame\" instead of the driver's own native gap, against the contract's \"ValueError or RecursionError → delegate unchanged\" | src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:119 | 2 | BOB |\n46:| R8 | [1/3] | 🟡 | The preflight parse and scan sit inside the tolerant driver catch, so the try blocks nest 4 levels deep (the limit). Hoist the `json.loads` try and the scalar check above it and wrap only `tuple(self._driver.decode(frame))` in `except Exception`. This also matches the contract's \"consume decode under the existing tolerant catch\" | src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:116 | 2 | BOB |\n47:| R9 | [1/3] | 🟡 | Duplicated test tables: the completion construct and record-decode tests repeat the same `additions` dict and body. Hoist it to one module constant or merge them into one test parametrized over construct vs decode | tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py:314 | 1 | BOB |\n48:| R10 | [1/3] | 🟡 | The same strip-after-redact bug exists in the TUI. `display_text` drops Cc/Cf characters from already-sanitized activity and tool text without redacting again, so a stored `sk-abc\\x00defghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123` shows on screen as the rebuilt token | src/ovcaq/tui/model.py:136 | general | BOB |\n49:| R11 | [1/3] | ⚪ | The same strip-after-redaction pattern survives outside `bounded_detail`. TUI `display_text` drops Cc/Cf characters after the sanitizer has already run. I checked that a NUL-split token in a Codex agent message (`codex_events.py:32`, where controls are never stripped) shows the full token on screen. So do ZWSP- and soft-hyphen-split tokens even in `bounded_detail` output, because format characters are not in its control regex. This is outside this PRD's scope (\"no speculative control forms\"), but the new doc sentence \"prevents controls inside a credential from hiding it from redaction\" claims more than the code delivers. Fix: narrow the wording to the recognized C0/DEL/CSI forms and file a follow-up PRD to re-sanitize at the display layer | docs/driver-protocol.md:224 | 5 | ALICE |\n50:| R12 | [1/3] | ⚪ | The `**runtime**` changelog entry claims a runtime fix, but no runtime production code changed (Task 4 added tests only). It repeats the `**events**` gap entry. Fix: fold the continuation and propagation wording into the events entry | CHANGELOG.md:43 | 4 | ALICE |\n51:| R13 | [1/3] | ⚪ | The supervisor's catch-all handler builds `SessionSummary(..., str(error), ...)`. If the error text carries surrogateescape bytes (a non-UTF-8 path), the new `SessionSummary` check raises `ValueError` inside the handler and `_conclude` is skipped, so the failure record is lost. Not a regression: the strict encode in src/ovcaq/runtime/_session_io.py:19 already failed on such text | src/ovcaq/runtime/supervisor.py:370 | general | BLAKE |\n52:| R14 | [1/3] | ⚪ | The pre-decode check assumes every driver parses frames with plain `json.loads`. A plugin driver that unwraps a prefix or applies its own escapes skips the pre-mutation check. The model still rejects the bad strings, so nothing crashes, but such a driver can change its state before the `Observation` constructor raises. Every frame (up to 1 MiB) is also parsed twice; the PRD sets no performance limit | src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:118 | 2 | BLAKE |\n53:| R15 | [1/3] | ⚪ | Cannot statically verify: focused and full suites pass at the review HEAD. The test gate was reused from 0961e40, and HEAD 4c84d4d adds chore commits on top | N/A | general | BOB |\n54:| R16 | [1/3] | 🟡 | 66 touched test(s) pass against the pre-change code: test_bounded_detail_redacts_reconstructed_tokens_before_capping, test_bounded_detail_preserves_printable_text_and_caps_after_control_removal +60 more | tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py | general | mech-check |\n55:| R17 | [1/3] | 🟡 | 5 touched test(s) pass against the pre-change code: test_valid_escaped_pair_remains_a_native_startup_record, test_malformed_and_non_json_frames_keep_native_delegation, test_real_writer_failures_propagate_from_unsafe_native_frames | tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py | general | mech-check |\n56:| R18 | [1/3] | 🟡 | 26 touched test(s) pass against the pre-change code: test_usage_and_completion_preserve_valid_unicode_scalars +20 more | tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py | general | mech-check |\n65:| R1 | fix | Correct design acceptance to include the approved frame-test split; preserve coverage and size limits. |\n66:| R2 | defer | Settled limitation: the reviewed helper contract is explicitly acyclic JSON-like containers; native json.loads cannot create cycles. Preserve the witnessed hang; no cycle-guard scope expansion. |\n67:| R3 | fix | Strengthen independent exact-value and redaction assertions for the receiver lane cap case. |\n68:| R4 | fix | Bounded scan optimization; preserve validation of all original strings before sensitive-key redaction, supported containers, and subclass semantics. |\n69:| R5 | fix | Confirmed on actual bounded_detail: C0 removal destroys regex word boundaries for bare and Bearer tokens; old order redacts both. Additional pre-cleanup redaction preserves required post-cleanup redaction and final cap, without interface changes. Amend the exact design contract from this review evidence. |\n70:| R6 | defer | Display-time character stripping/activity UI is excluded by this PRD. Preserve durable follow-up evidence; no implicit expansion of 00054. |\n71:| R7 | fix | Add independent deep-JSON RecursionError-delegation regression; preserve native fallback and adapter state. |\n72:| R8 | fix | Simplify only while preserving tolerant validation/decode failure behavior, ValueError/RecursionError delegation, raw-first ordering and fatal publication outside catches. Reject literal hoisting if it widens error escape; helper extraction within the existing boundary is acceptable. |\n73:| R9 | fix | Share the completion additions fixture while preserving independent construct/decode paths and assertions. |\n74:| R10 | defer | Same out-of-scope display-time defect as R6; preserve its separate citation and deferral. |\n75:| R11 | fix | Narrow protocol wording to recognized ANSI/control forms; broader TUI follow-up stays deferred. |\n76:| R12 | fix | Fold duplicate runtime wording into the events changelog entry, retaining continuity and fatal-writer guarantees. |\n77:| R13 | defer | Pre-existing arbitrary exception/path surrogate handling; retain for later scoped runtime failure work. |\n78:| R14 | defer | Prefix-unwrapping/custom-escape plugin drivers are outside this native JSON frame contract. Preserve malformed/non-JSON delegation; no generic rollback framework. |\n79:| R15 | verify | Route the exact focused command to the next mandatory work verification pass; current-HEAD full verification is separately recorded. |\n80:| R16 | discard | Verified preservation controls: valid Unicode/pairs, printable text, malformed delegation and genuine writer errors must pass before the change. The files also contain independent repair regressions; replay reports 1196 failures and 97 preservation passes with no uncollectable files. |\n81:| R17 | discard | Verified preservation controls: valid Unicode/pairs, printable text, malformed delegation and genuine writer errors must pass before th