+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'cycle.*1|contract card|Session handoff|record-store' /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/cli/review_stage.py\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/cli/review_stage.py:73:    \"review cycle — the diff is scoped to changes since then. Two jobs: (1) for \"\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:53:Review sessions run on opus at xhigh in cycle 1 and at high on cycle 2 and later; _AUTOPILOT_EFFORT_REVIEW forces one effort for every cycle and _AUTOPILOT_EFFORT_REVIEW_RERUN sets the rerun value. A rework resume (the cycle's review file exists and `rework_task_ids` names an unfinished task) runs on the queued tasks' own tier instead, sonnet unless one is opus or fable (`references/model-ladder.md` § Review sessions, PRD 00207).\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:97:**`statectl` is the sole writer of `state.json`.** Apply every field mutation with `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/run-autopilot/scripts/statectl.py <state.json> set|append|del <json-path> <json-value>` (read one field with `get`); it takes an advisory lock, backs up to `<state.json>.bak`, changes only the named path while preserving all siblings, and replaces the file atomically — so it cannot leave a half-written or unparseable state, and it never trips the \"not read yet\" / \"modified since read\" errors the editing tools hit. Since PRD 00089 it is a shim over `cli/state.transaction`, so every write is schema-validated too: a value that is malformed **for the field it targets** is rejected with exit 1 and the file left byte-unchanged (an unrelated pre-existing odd field blocks nothing). **Phase transitions are not field mutations** — use `autopilot phase-done --outcome <outcome>` (§ Session handoff procedure), never a hand-written `set phase` / `set next_phase` pair, so a transition cannot land without the effects it mandates. Resolve `<state.json>` by walking up from the resolved physical cwd to the autopilot dir (the `_walk_up.py` pattern in `/autopilot:work` step 2). The terse `set X` / `write field Y` / per-PRD-reset instructions throughout these skills and the gate files name the fields to change; each is applied with `statectl`, never by hand-editing the file.\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:103:Create `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/` and subdirectories if missing. Initialize state file at PRD selection. Update state at every phase transition. Autopilot also keeps a per-PRD **decision audit log** at `docs/dev/project-management/reviews/<prd-base>-audit.md`, **rendered once at Phase 9 finalize from the `state.json` decision arrays** (`autonomous_decisions`, `deferred_decisions`, `doubts`). `state.json` is the single in-run source of truth — decisions are NOT mirrored to `audit.md` incrementally per decision. Each rendered entry carries a **source** label (`autonomous`, `deferred`, or `doubt`); cycle/phase context goes in the entry body so the Phase 9 `decisions.md` projection can filter autonomous entries by label. The render is `autopilot render audit` (PRD 00107); the label set and the projection live in `references/audit-log-format.md`.\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:105:**Invariant:** every state mutation that advances `phase` SHOULD also set `next_phase` to the same value. The three gates are `build` | `review` | `done` (plus `paused`). `build` is ONE session: selection, catchup, design, planning, and work all run under `phase: \"build\"` with no mid-build handoff. The review surface runs in its own fresh session; blind and doubt scrutiny are LENSES inside every review cycle (Blake and Bob in `review-work-completion`'s roster), not separate phases — reviewers get isolated contexts by construction (subagent prompts, external CLIs). Legacy `blind`/`doubt` phase values in pre-00015 state files map to `review` on resume. Per-task implementor tiering inside `/autopilot:work` is unchanged. The authoritative resume signal is `phase` + `phases_completed`; build sub-step skipping is by ARTIFACT (capsule freshness, design-doc-exists, tasks-exist, all-done), not by `phases_completed` membership. This resume decision (phase + phases_completed + artifact checks → next step) is encoded canonically in `cli/resume.py` (`scripts/resume_target.py` re-exports it), which `scripts/test_autopilot_resume.py` imports — editing the resume logic there flips a test red rather than silently drifting from this prose. Run `autopilot resume-target` at Phase 0 to print what that encoding says the next action is, and reconcile it against the handler you are about to follow: a disagreement means the prose and the encoded contract have drifted, and the encoding wins. It also runs the schema-version preflight, so an old or future `state.json` is surfaced there rather than resumed blindly. It answers for the `build` and `review` gates; `phase: \"done\"` returns `unknown phase: done` by design — the done gate is routed by the table above, not by this function.\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:162:── AUTOPILOT ── handing off to fresh session for cycle {n+1} ───────\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:182:**Stand-down procedure (a peer session owns the PRD).** A headless session never works a PRD another session is already working: two writers on one `state.json` and one set of task artifacts corrupt both, and the one-loop-per-repo guard sees only wrappers, not a bare interactive session. Phase 0 asks before it pauses. A peer counts only when `ListAgents` shows a busy interactive session whose name starts with this repository's directory basename (`basename \"$PWD\"`, e.g. `agent-skills-`); a session named for another repository is never evidence, whatever it is busy with (the two 2026-09-14 false stand-downs in agent-skills each cited a `claude-autopilot-*` session, the other repo's own loop). When such a peer exists, send it one `SendMessage` naming the PRD and wait at most 120 s for a reply. Stand down only when the reply claims the PRD (condition `peer_claimed`), or when writer evidence is present: `autopilot dirty` prints at least one path (condition `dirty_tree`; store writes never count as this evidence), or the mtime of `state.json` or `contract-card.md`, truncated to whole seconds, is greater than the `at` of the most recent `kind: \"handoff\"` row with `edge: \"leave\"` and this PRD's `prd` in `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/dispatch-metrics.jsonl` (condition `state_after_leave`; the rows carry no batch id, so the `prd` filter is what keeps an older batch's row out; when no such `leave` row exists, skip the mtime test and let the dirty-tree test and the reply decide). That comparison holds only because every handoff site writes its `leave` row AFTER its last state and card write (§ Session handoff procedure orders step 1 before step 2; `/autopilot:work`'s task-boundary handoff must set `next_phase` before its row too): a site that touches `state.json` after its row makes every next session read its own hand-off as peer evidence. A bare recent mtime is not evidence (a reader that inspects state while the loop writes, or this batch's own per-PRD reset, satisfies it), commit trailers are not consulted (no commit here carries a session trailer), and a peer that only reads, or never answers, never pauses a batch. To stand down: do not select, move, or write anything else; write `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/pause-requested` with the Write tool as one JSON line, `{\"reason\": \"<peer session> owns <prd> (<evidence>)\", \"condition\": \"<peer_claimed | dirty_tree | state_after_leave>\"}`, and end the turn. The loop reads a marker written during the session as a stand-down (branch 5 above): it stops with state intact, burns no retry, writes no park marker, quotes the reason in its stop line and notification, and records `stood_down` and `stood_down_condition` in the session's `loop-metrics.jsonl` row; `autoclaude` alone resumes once the peer is done. Before this procedure existed (2026-09-02, agent-skills PRD 00010) four stand-downs read as deaths and parked a healthy PRD mid-task.\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:194:### Session handoff procedure (canonical — gate files invoke it by site name)\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:199:2. **Write the session brief, then the `leave` handoff row, then record the store, then print the site's banner** (shown at the invoking site in the gate file). The brief comes first, after the contract card (§ Contract card): `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/run-autopilot/scripts/statectl.py <state.json> write-brief docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/session-brief.md` renders `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/session-brief.md` from the state step 1 committed (where the batch stands, the card verbatim, the files the next gate needs), so the next session orients from one page (PRD 00201); the loop's launch prompt names it whenever it exists. A failed write is one stderr line, never a phase failure: carry on to the row. The row is `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/work/scripts/record_dispatch.py handoff --site <build|review|done> --edge leave --phase <state.phase> --prd <state.prd>`, best-effort (`work/references/subagent-dispatch.md` § Dispatch telemetry); `state.phase` already names the next session's phase because step 1 committed it. A new site row in the table below gets its row from this step, not from a per-site sentence. Under `$_AUTOPILOT_LOOP` the row is also the session's point of no return: `hooks/note_session_leave.py` records it, and `hooks/guard_skill_after_leave.py` denies any `autopilot:*` (or `git-ferry:catchup`) `Skill` call this session makes afterwards, so a session that prints its banner and then re-invokes a gate is stopped by the harness, not only by this prose (PRD 00211). After the row, and as the LAST write before STOP, record the store with `autopilot record-store`: `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/run-autopilot/cli/__main__.py record-store --state <state.json> --site <build|review|done> --prd <state.prd>`, best-effort like the row (a failure is one stderr line, never a reason to skip the row or the STOP). It runs at every site in the table below and comes after the row, never between the brief and the row: the row itself appends to the tracked `dispatch-metrics.jsonl`, so only a commit that follows it sweeps that append in.\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:215:Within-session compaction can drop this skill's text mid-procedure, after which the session drifts off-contract with nothing to re-anchor it. To survive that, **at each gate transition write a compact contract card** — the current step, the active invariants, and the next gate:\n/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md:224:The session brief (`write-brief`, § Session handoff procedure step 2) is rendered right after this call so it carries the card just loaded; `/autopilot:work`'s task-boundary handoff and `/autopilot:review-work-completion`'s cycle transition write the brief the same way where they write their cards.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
