+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_89","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Retention|Disposable|Trash|cleanup|clean up' /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/run-autopilot/SKILL.md\"","aggregated_output":"107:### Retention\n113:- **Disposable** (removed by their lifecycle transitions, by name): `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/last-session.log`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/wrapper.log`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/pause-requested`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/paused-by-operator`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/session-brief.md` (re-rendered at every handoff), `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/.session-left` (overwritten at every loop-mode handoff), `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/lanes/` (one marker per live CLI reviewer lane, removed when the lane exits), `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json` (at batch end only — in loop mode the wrapper archives it to `reports/{batch_id}-state-final.json`; see `references/phase-done.md`), `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/wave.json`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/wave-slots/` and `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/review-paths` (a wave's control file, its per-wave review-slot directory, and the review's path-scoping list — the last removed with the assembly worktree at wave end, same lifecycle as the other two — none is a durable PRD-lifecycle artifact; `references/waves.md`), `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/replan-context.md`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json.bak`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/**/*.lock` (the flock files beside `state.json` and beside each `deferred/*.json`), `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/.turn-counts.json`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/.handoff-requested`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/.cap-fired`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/contract-card.md`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/park-requested`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/last-verification.json`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/.review-gate-blocks`, `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/.review-gate-failed`, and `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/.lane-guard-blocks`.\n119:Batch end and cleanup steps enumerate lifecycle-owned runtime files explicitly; they never remove a directory wholesale. This keeps a completed PRD's complete review trail intact after the batch closes (`references/design-rationale.md` § Verified moves).\n152:`autoclaude` launches `tracon` (`scripts/tracon/`) in the foreground by default (PRD 00062), so the loop terminal shows the live dashboard with no extra step. It reads `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json` — no action needed from autopilot beyond keeping the state file updated. `q` detaches (loop keeps running, wrapper prints the reattach command), `p` pauses at the next session boundary, `Ctrl-C` stops the loop with full cleanup. When there is no tty, no `uv`, or `_AUTOPILOT_TRACON=0`, the loop terminal shows the `render_stream.py` fallback with per-lane subagent tags instead. Full operator surface: `references/dashboard-format.md`.\n236:**Loop sketch** (the real driver — `cli/loop.py`, invoked as `autopilot loop` — adds the memory circuit-breaker, the session wall-clock cap, orphan cleanup, metrics, notifications, and the operator-view renderer — `scripts/render_stream.py` turns the stream-json terminal output into one-line summaries while `last-session.log` keeps the raw events; the bash `autoclaude` wrapper keeps only the operator subcommands, the tracon presentation front-end, and the hand-off):\n261:Then, right after that `mkdir -p` and as its own Bash call, run `autopilot ensure-store`: `python3 ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/run-autopilot/cli/__main__.py ensure-store --state <state.json>`. It writes `docs/dev/project-management/.gitignore`, the machine form of the § Retention Disposable list, whenever that file is missing or differs from the list; it is idempotent, exits 0 either way, and needs no `state.json` to exist yet. The file is written by code, never with the Write or Edit tool: `hooks/enforce_prd_location.py` rejects a top-level store file outside its keeper list for editor tools, and that refusal is correct and stays. The patterns themselves live once, as `STORE_GITIGNORE` in `cli/store_tree.py`, and a test holds them against § Retention. `autopilot enter` runs this step itself.\n343:**Turn-ending PAUSE rows must set `state.phase = \"paused\"` (and `state.next_phase = \"paused\"`) before stopping, and must also write `state.pause_reason = {\"site\": \"<slug>\", \"detail\": \"<one-line human string>\"}`.** `pause_reason` is a durable marker so the loop halts even if the model forgets `phase=\"paused\"`; unlike `phase` it is not overwritten by normal progression, so it must be cleared on resume (see `### Resuming` cleanup). Without it the wrapper — seeing a non-empty `next_phase` — would take its continue branch and relaunch the failed phase instead of stopping for you to intervene; a paused state is the wrapper's stop-and-notify branch (Session Loop branch 1), and the wrapper surfaces `pause_reason.detail` in its notification. This applies to \"Sub-skill invocation fails outright\" (`pause_reason.site = \"sub_skill_fail\"`), \"Review produces no parseable output\" (`\"reviewer_fail\"`), \"All three reviewers fail\" (`\"reviewer_fail\"`), and \"statectl state-write fails\" (`\"statectl_fail\"`). Exceptions that need no `phase` change: \"State file corrupted\" (delete it and restart from Phase 0 in the same session; the freshly-written state is what the wrapper reads at turn end) and \"No PRDs anywhere\" (see its row — the drained state write covers the loop). PAUSE sites that ask via `AskUserQuestion` mid-turn (Phase 1.5 design gate, Phase 2 clarification, Phase 5 blocking escalation and scope alarm) do NOT end the turn and need no `phase` change — **but only outside the loop. When `$_AUTOPILOT_LOOP` is set there is no human to answer, and (post-00066) none of these pause the batch: each takes its per-PRD path instead. The design gate and a blocking escalation run the Loop-mode stall procedure (`references/recovery.md`; `site: \"design_gate\"` recording the design doc path, `site: \"blocking_escalation\"` recording the blocking issue in the deferred JSON `detail`); a scope alarm defers-and-continues (a `scope-overflow` deferred record — the top-10 fixes proceed); a Phase 2 ambiguity is resolved by the simplest safe assumption, or stalls (`site: \"clarification\"`) under `pause_on_ambiguity: true`. None writes `phase: \"paused\"` — the batch keeps draining and a human resolves the parked PRD on the next manual `/autopilot:run-autopilot` (see `references/decision-framework.md` → \"Autonomy in loop mode\"). A mid-turn question on the unattended path has stranded the loop for hours (`references/design-rationale.md` § No mid-turn questions).**\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
