ired lenses; catchup does not run that review or mutate phase state.\n\n## Related context\n\n- Topic queried: `UTF-8-safe normalized evidence` (one WIP PRD; master adds no useful topic). Review harvest attempted the canonical review Markdown files and exited 1 with `no_repo`; repo index/query also exited 1 because OVCAQ is not registered with engram. Portfolio query timed out after a bounded 12 seconds with no returned hits; this is a retrieval gap, not evidence that related work is absent.\n- Portfolio status at this catchup exited 1: memory 192 (23 stale, 1 dead), PRD 7,510 (5,259 dead), discovery 375 (112 dead), transcripts 17,713 (17,604 dead), code 50,424 (101 stale, 805 dead), findings 12,683 (0 stale/dead), decisions 25 (0 stale/dead), code skipped 4,230. Missing kind/repo coverage was also reported. This stamp covers the queried portfolio scope. Every subprocess had a 12-second deadline.\n\n## GitHub State\n\n- No git remote or tags are configured. Local `master` at `b3175de` and its primary worktree are the only branch/worktree. The latest commits on October 9 add task 1 scalar implementation (`b3175de`), regression strengthening/fixes (`3e2a46b`, `4719234`), and host loop state (`98056ff`); the reviewed repair batch was prepared on October 7. GitHub issues, PR overlaps, remote branches, releases and live CI remain unverified; GitHub gathering was skipped because there is no remote.\n- Recent 20 master commits and local dirty-file statistics were loaded. Feature-branch comparison and its full-file consumer trace are inapplicable on master. Initial dirty paths were two dispatch-metrics JSONL files, the repair-readiness report, the capsule, and two autocodex session JSONL/prompt/stderr sets. Preserve these workflow artifacts; catchup changes only this capsule.\n\n## Project Health\n\n- The October 10 readiness handoff records the batch stopped during task 1, the latest child stderr having a stdout Broken pipe panic; detached restart approval was aborted and 