+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_226","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; print(Path(\\\"docs/dev/tmp/ivan-4-context.txt\\\").read_text()); print(Path(\\\"/Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/work/scripts/record_dispatch.py\\\").read_text()[-6200:])'\"","aggregated_output":"# AGENTS.md — OVCAQ\n\nOVCAQ means **Orchestration, Visibility, and Control for Agent Queues**. It is\nan installable Python CLI/TUI that supervises a PRD-driven workflow through\nClaude Code, Codex, or another headless coding agent.\n\nThe global `AGENTS.md` remains in force. This file adds project-specific rules.\n\n## Current state\n\nThe repository is in planning/bootstrap. Until an implementation PRD replaces\nit, `docs/dev/project-management/plans/implementation-plan.md` is the architecture and sequencing\nauthority. Do not create production modules opportunistically outside that\nsequence.\n\n## Product boundary\n\nOVCAQ core owns state, lifecycle commands, process supervision, agent adapters,\nnormalized events, observability, the TUI, and launcher provisioning checks.\n\nOVCAQ core does **not** contain launcher-specific skills, agents, hooks, or\nplugins. Those live in external marketplaces. Core may carry declarative\nidentifiers and version requirements needed to reconcile them.\n\n## Architecture invariants\n\n1. **One state writer.** Every durable `state.json` mutation goes through the\n   state store. Agents mutate state only through `ovcaq state` or a higher-level\n   OVCAQ command. Never instruct an agent to edit `state.json` directly.\n2. **State decides; prose does not.** Session completion, phase handoff, pause,\n   drain, retry, and failure decisions derive from committed state plus a\n   normalized session result. A final agent message is never authoritative.\n3. **Provider code stays at the edge.** Claude/Codex argv, environment variables,\n   event formats, model names, rate-limit parsing, and connectivity checks live\n   under their adapter. Shared runtime and UI code must not parse provider-native\n   events.\n4. **Raw evidence survives normalization.** Preserve each session's raw output.\n   Normalizers are tolerant and must degrade to an unknown/raw observation\n   instead of crashing the supervisor.\n5. **The TUI observes shared models.** It reads state, registry, metrics, and\n   normalized observations. It does not implement lifecycle policy or maintain a\n   second liveness algorithm.\n6. **External capabilities stay external.** Provisioning invokes a launcher's\n   supported marketplace/plugin CLI and verifies the result. It does not copy\n   plugin contents into this package or hand-edit launcher caches.\n7. **No shell evaluation of configured commands.** Store agent commands as argv\n   arrays and spawn them without `shell=True`.\n\n## Target layout\n\n```text\nsrc/ovcaq/\n  state/        # schema, transactions, compound mutations\n  workflow/     # PRD selection, transitions, records, policy\n  runtime/      # supervisor, decisions, registry, process ownership\n  drivers/      # Claude, Codex, and generic command adapters\n  events/       # normalized event model and session reduction\n  tui/          # discovery and Textual/Rich presentation\n  provision/    # marketplace/plugin reconciliation\ntests/          # mirrors package boundaries; provider JSONL fixtures\ndocs/           # tracked architecture and operator documentation\n```\n\n## Toolchain\n\n- Python 3.12+ managed through `mise`.\n- `uv` for environments, locking, build, and command execution.\n- `pytest` for tests; `ruff` for formatting/linting; `mypy` for package types.\n- Keep the runtime dependency set small. Textual/Rich are justified by the TUI;\n  prefer the standard library for state, locking, configuration, and subprocesses.\n\nPlanned verification commands once the scaffold lands:\n\n```bash\nuv sync --all-groups\nuv run pytest\nuv run ruff check .\nuv run ruff format --check .\nuv run mypy src/ovcaq\nuv build\n```\n\n## Development rules\n\n- Characterize current behavior before moving it from `~/.claude`.\n- Extract state first, then pure workflow logic, runtime, adapters, TUI, and\n  provisioning in that order.\n- Sanitized Claude and Codex JSONL fixtures belong in `tests/fixtures/`; tests\n  never read live files from `~/.claude` or `~/.codex`.\n- Test process-group, lock, and signal behavior with real subprocesses in\n  addition to unit tests.\n- Documentation for commands comes from the same command registry/parser as the\n  implementation; do not maintain a second hand-written verb inventory.\n- Keep provider-neutral modules free of the strings `claude`, `anthropic`,\n  `codex`, and provider model identifiers except in tests that enforce this rule.\n- Use conventional commits. No compatibility shim, dual writer, or rollback\n  framework is required for the initial cutover.\n\n## Migration stance\n\nThis is a one-way early-stage extraction. Start a fresh OVCAQ batch/state tree;\ndo not build an importer for the current `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json` unless\na later requirement explicitly needs it. Temporary delegation during a local\ncanary is acceptable, but do not ship `autoclaude`, `autopilot`, `tracon`, or\n`statectl` aliases as permanent public APIs.\n\nRead-only context paths (anchored): tests/runtime/test_supervisor_process.py lines1–204 for ProcessDriver/Step/Harness/harness and lines250–288 for stopped/cleanup helpers; tests/runtime/test_supervisor.py lines381–412 run_once pattern; tests/runtime/test_supervisor_adapters.py lines1–65 if needed; tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py lines1–109 and203–243 for native fixture/API and healthy usage (cache_write_input_tokens=0 required). src/ovcaq/runtime/supervisor.py run_once lines263–267 and _attempt/_stream/_publish_summary anchors only; events.tail NormalizedEventWriter public write signature and events.model public Observation/SessionSummary signatures only. Do not read full large implementation modules. Complete total input limit100K, ordered plan: inspect harness, write continuity case, write genuine writer failure case, run only tests/runtime/test_unicode_continuity.py with -q --tb=line. UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/ovcaq-uv-cache. No network/provider probes; fixture Python children only. Avoid touching other test files. Use Python patterns/testing skills at /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md and python-testing/SKILL.md. No commits or state mutations.\n\nre: str,\n) -> tuple[list[dict[str, object]], bool]:\n    \"\"\"Parsed dict rows from the working file, and whether the file was read\n    successfully. A missing file is an empty ledger, silently, and counts as\n    read successfully; any other read failure (unreadable, not UTF-8) is also\n    treated as an empty ledger, but names itself on stderr as ``failure`` and\n    is reported as unsuccessful.\n    \"\"\"\n    ok = True\n    try:\n        lines = (autopilot_dir / FILENAME).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").splitlines()\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        lines = []  # no dispatch has been opened here yet: an empty ledger, not a failure\n    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError) as err:\n        print(f\"record_dispatch: {failure}: {err}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        lines = []\n        ok = False\n    rows: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n    skipped = 0\n    for line in lines:\n        try:\n            row = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError:\n            skipped += 1\n            continue\n        if isinstance(row, dict):\n            rows.append(row)\n    if skipped:\n        print(\n            f\"record_dispatch: skipped {skipped} unparseable line(s) in {FILENAME}\",\n            file=sys.stderr,\n        )\n    return rows, ok\n\n\ndef _queued_at(rows: list[dict[str, object]], dispatch_id: str) -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"The start row's ``queued_at`` for ``dispatch_id``, or None, said on stderr.\"\"\"\n    for row in rows:\n        if row.get(\"id\") == dispatch_id:\n            queued_at = row.get(\"queued_at\")\n            if isinstance(queued_at, int):\n                return queued_at\n    print(\n        f\"record_dispatch: no start row for {dispatch_id}, elapsed_s is null\",\n        file=sys.stderr,\n    )\n    return None\n\n\ndef _spans_handoff(\n    rows: list[dict[str, object]],\n    queued_at: int,\n    ended_at: int,\n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"True if a handoff row's ``at`` sits strictly inside (queued_at, ended_at):\n    part of the dispatch's window was spent away from the work, so its elapsed\n    time cannot be claimed.\n    \"\"\"\n    for row in rows:\n        if (\n            row.get(\"kind\") == \"handoff\"\n            and isinstance(row.get(\"at\"), int)\n            and queued_at < row[\"at\"] < ended_at\n        ):\n            return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef open_ids(autopilot_dir: Path) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Ids with a start row (``queued_at``) and no end row (``ended_at``)\n    anywhere in the file, in the order each id's start row was first seen.\n    \"\"\"\n    rows, _ = _read_rows(autopilot_dir, \"working file unreadable\")\n    started: list[str] = []\n    ended: set[str] = set()\n    for row in rows:\n        dispatch_id = row.get(\"id\")\n        if (\n            \"queued_at\" in row\n            and isinstance(dispatch_id, str)\n            and dispatch_id not in started\n        ):\n            started.append(dispatch_id)\n        if \"ended_at\" in row and isinstance(dispatch_id, str):\n            ended.add(dispatch_id)\n    return [dispatch_id for dispatch_id in started if dispatch_id not in ended]\n\n\ndef _handoff(autopilot_dir: Path, args: argparse.Namespace) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Close any dispatches still open at this handoff as lost, then stamp the edge.\"\"\"\n    at = int(time.time())\n    for dispatch_id in open_ids(autopilot_dir):\n        append_row(\n            autopilot_dir,\n            {\n                \"id\": dispatch_id,\n                \"ended_at\": at,\n                \"elapsed_s\": None,\n                \"outcome\": \"lost\",\n                \"detail\": f\"open at {args.site}/{args.edge} handoff\",\n            },\n        )\n    append_row(\n        autopilot_dir,\n        {\n            \"kind\": \"handoff\",\n            \"site\": args.site,\n            \"edge\": args.edge,\n            \"at\": at,\n            \"phase\": args.phase,\n            \"prd\": args.prd,\n        },\n    )\n\n\ndef parse_args(argv: list[str] | None) -> argparse.Namespace:\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Append dispatch timing rows.\")\n    verbs = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"verb\", required=True)\n\n    start = verbs.add_parser(\"start\", help=\"open a row for a hand-built dispatch\")\n    start.add_argument(\"--kind\", required=True)\n    start.add_argument(\"--task\", required=True)\n    start.add_argument(\n        \"--prompt-file\",\n        required=True,\n        help=\"the written prompt; its size is the count\",\n    )\n\n    end = verbs.add_parser(\"end\", help=\"close a dispatch row\")\n    end.add_argument(\"id\")\n    end.add_argument(\"--outcome\", required=True, choices=OUTCOMES)\n    end.add_argument(\"--detail\")\n\n    handoff = verbs.add_parser(\"handoff\", help=\"stamp one edge of a session handoff\")\n    handoff.add_argument(\"--site\", required=True, choices=SITES)\n    handoff.add_argument(\"--edge\", required=True, choices=EDGES)\n    handoff.add_argument(\"--phase\", required=True)\n    handoff.add_argument(\"--prd\", required=True)\n    return parser.parse_args(argv)\n\n\ndef main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n    args = parse_args(argv)\n    autopilot_dir = find_autopilot_dir(Path.cwd())\n    if args.verb == \"start\":\n        try:\n            prompt_bytes = len(Path(args.prompt_file).read_bytes())\n        except OSError as err:\n            print(f\"record_dispatch: prompt file unreadable: {err}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        print(prompt_bytes)\n        print(start_row(autopilot_dir, args.kind, args.task, prompt_bytes))\n    elif autopilot_dir is None:\n        return 0\n    elif args.verb == \"end\":\n        ended_at = int(time.time())\n        rows, ok = _read_rows(autopilot_dir, \"start row lookup failed\")\n        queued_at = _queued_at(rows, args.id) if ok else None\n        elapsed_s = None if queued_at is None else ended_at - queued_at\n        detail = args.detail\n        if queued_at is not None and _spans_handoff(rows, queued_at, ended_at):\n            elapsed_s = None\n            detail = f\"spans handoff; {args.detail or ''}\"\n        append_row(\n            autopilot_dir,\n            {\n                \"id\": args.id,\n                \"ended_at\": ended_at,\n                \"elapsed_s\": elapsed_s,\n                \"outcome\": args.outcome,\n                \"detail\": detail,\n            },\n        )\n    else:\n        _handoff(autopilot_dir, args)\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
