on tables are rebuilt per case across five or more tests. The same nested-location shapes are repeated in the observation, `sanitize_json` and record-decoder tests. At 500 lines the file is past the 200-400 line target. | Put the shared location builders (value, nested key, tuple, secret, deep) in one module-level helper keyed by name, and have each test pick from it.\n\n\nFILE tess-1-output.md\nTask 1: independent shared-model Unicode scalar regressions.\n\nChanged only tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py. No implementation or architecture files read; no production changes, commits, or state writes.\n\nPrecheck: direct Observation construction accepted a lone high surrogate in its payload.\n\nAdded seven behavior tests, expanded to 47 cases, covering lone high/low surrogates in identifiers, recursive payload values/keys, SessionSummary strings, sanitize_json including secret redaction, observation_from_record using generated records, ordinary Unicode and scalar boundaries, and valid escaped surrogate pairs. The record tests derive their shape from observation_record rather than guessing a serialization schema.\n\nRan only the named narrow test:\nenv UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/ovcaq-uv-cache mise exec -- uv run pytest -q --tb=line tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py -k scalar\n\nResult: 47 failed in 0.04s; exit code 1. Forty-two rejection cases failed because the existing public APIs accepted invalid scalars. Five acceptance cases exposed a test assumption: Observation freezes payload lists into tuples, so direct equality with input lists is unsuitable. The coordinator requested stopping further changes and deferring these defects, including broad raises(Exception), to the mandated quality-gate retry.\n\nRequested execution model: gpt-6.1-sol with high reasoning. Actual served-model metadata is not exposed; no served-model claim is made.\n\nASSUMPTIONS:\nRejected invalid strings would raise an Exception; the prompt did not specify an exception subclass.\nValid observation payloads would remain directly equal to their input lists; the narrow test disproved this container-representation assumption.\n\n# Project Capsule: OVCAQ\n\nGenerated: 2026-10-09T19:48:22.997221Z\nCatchup HEAD: `98056ff860f78868ab209cee07bc008d68e7b533` (`master`)\n\n## Key Invariants\n\n- `StateStore.transaction()` is the only durable `state.json` writer; commands and later workflow/runtime services share it.\n- State plus a normalized session result decides lifecycle progress. Agent prose and observational logs never do.\n- The clean v1 state is a one-way cutover: no legacy importer, dual writer, compatibility shim, or permanent `autoclaude`/`autopilot`/`tracon`/`statectl` aliases.\n- Provider-specific argv, environment, event, model, and rate-limit logic remains at driver edges; provider-neutral state/runtime/TUI modules must not parse native events.\n- Raw session evidence survives normalization, and configured commands are always argv arrays spawned without shell evaluation.\n- PRD sequencing follows `docs/dev/project-management/plans/implementation-plan.md`: state first, then workflow, runtime, adapters, TUI, and provisioning.\n\n## Architecture Decisions\n\n- OVCAQ is one Python 3.12+ installable package with an `ovcaq` console command and a small runtime dependency set (Rich/Textual plus stdlib-first internals).\n- State, workflow, runtime, events, both native adapters, supervisor, and TUI are implemented through PRD 00009. Codex includes native decoding, cumulative usage, lane/tool projection, state-only default prompts and fake-supervisor conformance. Provisioning and real launcher/plugin smoke remain later-phase work.\n- State v1 groups ownership under `batch`, `work`, `tasks`, `review`, `control`, and `recovery`, with a monotonic top-level `revision`.\n- Every transaction holds one advisory lock across read, optional revision compare, deep-copy mutation, full validation, revision increment, raw-byte backup publication, state publication, and supported directory fsync.\n- Generic JSON-path operations are recovery tools. Transition-owned paths require explicit `--unsafe`; normal skills use compound commands instead.\n- External launcher skills/plugins remain in their marketplaces. Core owns only declarative requirements and lifecycle state needed to reconcile them.\n\n## Component Boundaries\n\n- `ovcaq.state.schema`: clean v1 types/defaults, full nested validation, cross-field invariants, and future-version refusal.\n- `ovcaq.state.store`: locked load/init/transaction/restore, compare-and-set, backup, atomic replacement, and durability boundaries.\n- `ovcaq.state.paths`: generic JSON-path parsing/mutation only; no workflow ownership policy.\n- `ovcaq.state.commands`: compound task/attempt/contract-card operations and recovery commands; all writes call the store.\n- `ovcaq.cli`: the live parser and stable machine-output/error boundary; help and state documentation derive from it.\n- `ovcaq.workflow`: completed pure selection, frontmatter, resume, transition, policy, recoverable filesystem-record, and report services; it owns no process or launcher behavior.\n- `ovcaq.paths` and `ovcaq.config`: shared project/runtime discovery, containment, configuration precedence, agent tier settings, and phase routing; launcher-specific interpretation remains at the driver edge.\n- `ovcaq.runtime`: now owns runtime paths/configuration, the authoritative run lock, fleet registry, process groups, watchdog cleanup, raw session evidence, retention/purge, capabilities, and completion cleanup. `runtime_cli.py` projects those shared models into status/doctor/logs without becoming a second liveness authority.\n- `ovcaq.events` owns immutable protocol-1 observations, reduction and raw-first framing; `ovcaq.drivers` owns native decoding for both launchers under driver API 2. `runtime.session` owns private raw evidence and the decoder publishes normalized observations only afterward. The raw-first boundary must reject invalid native strings before a stateful adapter mutates identity/usage; genuine evidence writer failures must still propagate.\n- `ovcaq.tui` now projects the shared registry, state, metrics, normalized events,\n  and capability models; it owns presentation and exact-run controls but no\n  lifecycle policy or provider-native decoding. `ovcaq.provision` remains a\n  later-phase boundary.\n\n## Active Work\n\n- Current host batch `202610092123` names PRD `00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1.md`, phase/next phase `build`, full lane, review cap 2, and no completed PRDs. This host's `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json` is launcher orchestration state, distinct from the product's nested v1 state contract; catchup only read it.\n- Exactly one WIP PRD: **UTF-8-safe normalized evidence** (00051), four unchecked PRD tasks expanded into five canonical state tasks: task 1 in progress; tasks 2–5 pending. It owns shared Unicode scalar validation, rejection before adapter mutation, exact raw evidence plus safe gaps/continuation, and strip→sanitize→bound diagnostic details. No live model calls. `a537309` committed the 297-line `tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py` direct-model regressions; production scalar validation is still absent. Native-frame/detail/subprocess regression files remain to be completed. Catchup inspected source and committed tests; it did not rerun acceptance or treat the test commit as task completion.\n- Authorized repair batch order is 00051, 00052 (reviewed exact CLI evidence), 00053 (adapter policy/routing/probe behavior), 00054 (activity projection/rendering). Historical HOLD items remain HOLD. The October 7 repair triage and `reviews/repair-backlog-20261007.md` explain this split.\n- Previous batch `202609062243` completed 00004–00009 with cycles 16/2/5/2/2/2. PRD 00009 completed 30/30 tasks at review cap 2, leaving 33 cycle-2 findings deferred plus earlier deferrals and assumptions. Cap-deferred completion did not establish absence of defects.\n- Reviewed design `designs/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-design.md` fixes the contracts: one internal iterative scalar predicate, validation before redaction/usage early returns, JSON preflight before driver mutation, and strip→sanitize→bound diagnostics. Design reviewers reported no blockers; cycle/shared-container and duplicate-key questions remain recorded as non-blocking. The host contract card still describes task 1 test creation; the committed tests are newer evidence, while canonical status remains in progress.\n- All PRD tasks must finish before the mandated review handoff. Full review runs in a fresh session with all required lenses; catchup does not run that review or mutate phase state.\n\n## Related context\n\n- Topic queried: `UTF-8-safe normalized evidence` (master contributes no useful topic). Review harvest attempted 233 canonical review Markdown files; exited 1 with `no_repo`. Repo index and query also exited 1: OVCAQ is not registered with engram. An initial portfolio query was interrupted after hanging; a bounded 15-second retry timed out with no returned hits; this does not rule out related work.\n- Portfolio status collected during this catchup exited 1: memory 192 (23 stale, 1 dead), PRD 7,510 (5,259 dead), discovery 223 (112 dead), transcripts 17,713 (17,604 dead), code 50,308 (99 stale, 805 dead), findings 12,683 (0 stale/dead), code skipped 4,205. Missing kind/repo coverage was also reported. This stamp covers the queried portfolio scope.\n\n## GitHub State\n\n- No git remote or tags are configured. Local `master` at `98056ff` and its primary worktree are the only branch/worktree. The latest commits on October 9 add task 1 regression tests (`a537309`) and host loop state (`98056ff`); the reviewed repair batch was prepared on October 7. GitHub issues, PR overlaps, remote branches, releases and live CI remain unverified; GitHub gathering was skipped because there is no remote.\n- Recent 20 master commits and