pite implemented modules; the sequencing authority remains the implementation plan.\n- Retained raw evidence remains indefinite and private by default; purge is explicit, preview-first, cutoff-scoped, and active-session-safe. No canary, provisioning or launcher-global mutation is authorized by this catchup.\n- Host meta decisions/troubleshooting files and `agent_docs` were absent. Architecture, operator/protocol docs, source boundaries and fixture/test suites exist. Project memory loaded but reflects the August extraction inventory and legacy store paths; current files and PRDs supersede its historical status/version claims.\n- Task discovery returned `no_tasks_dir`, a benign restore skip. No prior launcher tasks were restored and no task-store schema drift was reported; the five canonical tasks remain available from read-only host state. Engram registration and unavailable GitHub state are context gaps; neither blocks the local fixture/fake repair acceptance.\n\n## Project Memories\n\n- The extraction source is the characterized personal `run-autopilot` implementation. Port proven behavior rather than redesigning it, while applying the accepted v1 nesting, deep-validation, revision, and directory-fsync changes.\n- Current legacy state has many flat operational fields, marker files, compound task verbs, a rotating raw-byte backup, and a recoverable stall saga. PRD 00003 owns their state-schema disposition; PRD 00004 owns workflow transitions and filesystem lifecycle sagas.\n- Codex/Claude launcher capabilities and marketplace work are later PRDs. PRD 00003 must not introduce launcher-specific content or hardcoded personal paths.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
