Always use `-f` with a temp file for prompts to avoid shell escaping issues.\n\n```bash\n# Write prompt to temp file, then run\necho 'Your prompt here (can contain \"quotes\", parens(), etc.)' > /tmp/model-prompt.txt\n~/.agents/skills/use-<backend>/scripts/<backend>-run.sh -f /tmp/model-prompt.txt\n```\n\nPrompts pass via argument or `-f` file, never stdin.\n\n## Child Stdin Policy\n\nEvery headless child CLI invocation (the `-p`/`--print`/`codex exec` dispatch paths, plus preflight probes and the `mise env` PATH lookup) redirects the child's stdin with `< /dev/null`, so an unattended background dispatch can never hang on a child reading the inherited stdin (the PRD 00040 hang class). Documented exception: interactive (`-i`), bare `-r`/`--resume`, and `-c`/`--continue` invocations keep stdin - they legitimately need the TTY. Never dispatch those modes unattended.\n\n## Error Stream Convention\n\nUsage and preflight errors (missing prompt, missing prompt file, backend CLI not found) print to stderr and exit non-zero. stdout is reserved for model output and the tee\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/work/scripts/check_style_limits.py --diff /private/tmp/test-diff-1.txt /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py'\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/work/scripts/check_style_limits.py --diff /private/tmp/test-diff-1.txt /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py'\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'git diff --shortstat HEAD~1..HEAD'\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'git diff --shortstat HEAD~1..HEAD'\n 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/work/scripts/check_style_limits.py --diff /private/tmp/task-diff-1.txt /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/events/model.py /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py'\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/work/scripts/check_style_limits.py --diff /private/tmp/task-diff-1.txt /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/events/model.py /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py'\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/work/scripts/check_split_hygiene.py /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py'\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc 'python3 /Users/bob/.claude/plugins/cache/buvis-plugins/autopilot/0.9.0/skills/work/scripts/check_split_hygiene.py /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py'\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
