+{"timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:38:40.391Z","ordinal":19,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1222c-bf87-7dc1-a83b-61853b6ba6c2","call_id":"call_4GHj5oh2wZlIdOB8PVoEg2Hs","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":0,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"45182f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002209,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1476,\"output\":\"Your tests have quality issues. Fix them.\\n\\nIssues found:\\n[MECH] 🟡 test_observation_rejects_invalid_scalar_identifiers accepts any exception via `raises(Exception)` | File: tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py:79 | Task: general\\n[MECH] 🟡 test_observation_rejects_invalid_scalars_recursively_in_payload accepts any exception via `raises(Exception)` | File: tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py:92 | Task: general\\n[MECH] 🟡 test_summary_rejects_invalid_scalar_strings accepts any exception via `raises(Exception)` | File: tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py:99 | Task: general\\n[MECH] 🟡 test_sanitize_json_rejects_invalid_scalars_before_redaction accepts any exception via `raises(Exception)` | File: tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py:113 | Task: general\\n[MECH] 🟡 test_observation_record_decoder_rejects_invalid_scalars accepts any exception via `raises(Exception)` | File: tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py:126 | Task: general\\nQuality checks: use ValueError with the documented static safe message Strings must contain only Unicode scalar values; never accepts any exception. Valid Observation payloads are deeply frozen; compare serialized observation_record payload or explicit tuple-shaped expected values rather than mutable list equality. Preserve valid Unicode semantics. Cover invalid scalars in usage.updated identity and session.completed payload with complete Usage fields, including hidden sensitive values before redaction. Cover tuple and nested mapping keys. No implementation reads. Type annotations on new test helpers/signatures per Python patterns.\\n\\n\\nOriginal requirements (unchanged):\\n\\nDescription:\\nOnly task 1: direct shared model scalar validation. Write only /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py. Test existing Observation, SessionSummary, sanitize_json, observation_record, observation_from_record and summary_record. No raw-first adapter tests in this task.\\n\\n- **Description**: Reject decoded strings containing lone UTF-16 surrogate code points.\\n- **Inputs**: Observation identifiers, payload values, nested mapping keys and native JSON records.\\n- **Outputs**: Valid observations or a bounded normalization gap.\\n- **Behavior**: Validate all strings recursively, including keys, before native-record semantic decoding and mutation. An invalid frame produces `raw.unknown` and no session/thread/lane/usage mutation; later frames see the pre-frame adapter state. Direct observation construction rejects invalid strings. Valid escaped surrogate pairs decode to their non-BMP scalar and remain supported. Preserve ordinary valid Unicode and existing malformed/non-JSON fallback behavior. Merely escaping invalid strings with `ensure_ascii=True`, replacing identifiers, or silently dropping characters does not satisfy this contract.\\n\\n\\n\\nAcceptance Criteria:\\n- Re-check that direct observations accept invalid scalars before editing; if already fixed, skip production edits and report while retaining independent tests. `mise exec -- uv run pytest tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py -k scalar` passes; cases cover lone high/low surrogates in identifiers, values and nested keys, ordinary Unicode and valid escaped pairs, with explicit rejected/accepted assertions.\\n\\nRewrite the tests addressing each issue above. Keep every test that is already\\nsound — this is a targeted fix, not a rewrite from scratch.\\n\\nThe original rules still apply. In particular:\\n\\n1. Write tests from requirements only. You are a USER of this API, not its builder.\\n2. Each test name describes a behavior, not an implementation detail.\\n3. Assert on outputs, return values, side effects, and errors. Never assert on mock existence.\\n4. For EACH test, ask yourself: \\\"What wrong implementation would still pass this?\\\" If easy to answer, add constraints.\\n5. SIMPLICITY FIRST: test only the behavior in the acceptance criteria. Strengthening a weak test does not mean adding tests nobody asked for.\\n6. NEVER INVENT A CONTRACT: if the requirements name a data structure but do not pin its exact field names, enum values, or types, STOP and report it as a blocker rather than inventing a plausible schema.\\n7. SURGICAL: only create/modify test files. Match the existing test file's style.\\n8. SIZE LIMITS: keep every test function under 50 lines and every test file under 800 lines; a style-gate line above naming a file or function over a limit is an issue to fix here, by splitting into sibling files named after the test module.\\n\\nRead only the files listed above. If a file or symbol you need is not listed, stop and report it as a blocker — do not run broad `rg` sweeps to discover scope.\\n\\nAbort and report if you read more than 100K of total input. Return the partial result and an abort_reason: context_overrun field.\\n\\nRead every file before your first Edit to it. Never call bash `head`, `tail`, `cat`, `grep`, or `find` - a hook blocks them. Use the Read tool (offset/limit), `rg`, or `rg --files` instead. Never combine an inspection (read, list, search, diff) with a test, lint or build invocation in one Bash call - run them as two calls, because a combined command has two ways to hang and one exit code. Pass an explicit `timeout` on every Bash call: 60000 ms for an inspection, 300000 ms for a lint run or a narrow test run, 600000 ms for a full suite or a full build.\\n\\nRun only the test files this task names (the tests you wrote, or the\\nfailing tests in your prompt), with `-q --tb=line`. Never run a whole test\\ndirectory or `dev/bin/release-checks`: the orchestrator runs the full suite\\nonce, after every task. Read the pass count and exit code from that one\\nrun; never re-run a suite to recover a number.\\n\\nEnd your report with `ASSUMPTIONS:` - one line per assumption you made where the task, tests, or listed files were silent (guessed interface, data shape, resolved ambiguity, unstated behavior). Write `ASSUMPTIONS: none` if you made none.\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":1,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"b07137\",\"wall_time_seconds\":7.08e-7,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1191,\"output\":\"Module: ovcaq.events (reexports model public names).\\nclass ObservationType(StrEnum):\\n    SESSION_STARTED = \\\"session.started\\\"\\n    ACTIVITY_MESSAGE = \\\"activity.message\\\"\\n    TOOL_STARTED = \\\"tool.started\\\"\\n    TOOL_COMPLETED = \\\"tool.completed\\\"\\n    TOOL_FAILED = \\\"tool.failed\\\"\\n    LANE_STARTED = \\\"lane.started\\\"\\n    LANE_PROGRESS = \\\"lane.progress\\\"\\n    LANE_COMPLETED = \\\"lane.completed\\\"\\n    LANE_FAILED = \\\"lane.failed\\\"\\n    USAGE_UPDATED = \\\"usage.updated\\\"\\n    RATE_LIMIT_STARTED = \\\"rate_limit.started\\\"\\n    RATE_LIMIT_CLEARED = \\\"rate_limit.cleared\\\"\\n    SESSION_COMPLETED = \\\"session.completed\\\"\\n    SESSION_FAILED = \\\"session.failed\\\"\\n    RAW_UNKNOWN = \\\"raw.unknown\\\"\\n\\nclass FailureClass(StrEnum):\\n    RATE_LIMIT = \\\"rate_limit\\\"\\n    CONNECTIVITY = \\\"connectivity\\\"\\n    PERMISSION = \\\"permission\\\"\\n    AUTHENTICATION = \\\"authentication\\\"\\n    TIMEOUT = \\\"timeout\\\"\\n    AGENT = \\\"agent\\\"\\n    UNKNOWN = \\\"unknown\\\"\\n\\nclass Usage:\\n    input_tokens: int | None = None\\n    output_tokens: int | None = None\\n    cache_creation_input_tokens: int | None = None\\n    cache_read_input_tokens: int | None = None\\n    tool_uses: int | None = None\\n    cost_usd: float | None = None\\n    estimated: bool = False\\n\\nclass Observation:\\n    protocol_version: int\\n    timestamp: datetime\\n    provider: str\\n    run_id: str\\n    session_id: str | None\\n    lane_id: str | None\\n    type: ObservationType\\n    payload: Mapping[str, JSONValue]\\n\\nclass SessionSummary:\\n    success: bool\\n    session_id: str | None\\n    failure_class: FailureClass | None\\n    failure_detail: str | None\\n    rate_limit_reset_at: datetime | None\\n    usage: Usage | None\\n\\ndef sanitize_text(text: str) -> str: ...\\n\\ndef sanitize_json(value: object) -> JSONValue: ...\\n\\ndef observation_record(observation: Observation) -> dict[str, JSONValue]: ...\\n\\ndef observation_from_record(record: Mapping[str, JSONValue]) -> Observation: ...\\n\\ndef summary_record(summary: SessionSummary) -> dict[str, JSONValue]: ...\\\"\\\"\\\"Public version-one observation contract, independent of agent drivers.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport json\\nfrom dataclasses import FrozenInstanceError, is_dataclass\\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta, timezone\\nfrom enum import StrEnum\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom ovcaq.events import (\\n    PROTOCOL_VERSION,\\n    FailureClass,\\n    Observation,\\n    ObservationType,\\n    SessionSummary,\\n    Usage,\\n    observation_from_record,\\n    observation_record,\\n    sanitize_json,\\n    sanitize_text,\\n    summary_record,\\n)\\n\\nNOW = datetime(2026, 9, 26, 12, 30, 15, 123456, tzinfo=UTC)\\nCOUNTERS = (\\n    \\\"input_tokens\\\",\\n    \\\"output_tokens\\\",\\n    \\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\",\\n    \\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\",\\n    \\\"tool_uses\\\",\\n)\\nUSAGE_DATA = dict.fromkeys(COUNTERS, 0) | {\\\"cost_usd\\\": 0.0, \\\"estimated\\\": False}\\nCLOSED_PAYLOADS = {\\n    \\\"usage.updated\\\": {\\\"usage\\\": USAGE_DATA, \\\"identity\\\": \\\"request-1\\\"},\\n    \\\"session.failed\\\": {\\\"failure_class\\\": \\\"agent\\\", \\\"detail\\\": \\\"request failed\\\"},\\n    \\\"rate_limit.started\\\": {\\n        \\\"reset_at\\\": \\\"2026-09-26T13:00:00Z\\\",\\n        \\\"window\\\": \\\"five_hour\\\",\\n        \\\"detail\\\": \\\"wait\\\",\\n    },\\n    \\\"raw.unknown\\\": {\\n        \\\"reason\\\": \\\"unrecognized\\\",\\n        \\\"raw_sha256\\\": \\\"a\\\" * 64,\\n        \\\"preview\\\": \\\"data\\\",\\n    },\\n}\\nCREDENTIAL_CASES = [\\n    (\\\"password=other-secret\\\", \\\"password=[REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"Authorization: Bearer Q7v-k9_42\\\", \\\"Authorization: Bearer [REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"authorization: bearer mN8p23\\\", \\\"authorization: bearer [REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"access_token=R4j-62_y\\\", \\\"access_token=[REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"X-Secret: another-value\\\", \\\"X-Secret: [REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"PASSWORD=Z8n4p2\\\", \\\"PASSWORD=[REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"api_key: key-73_B\\\", \\\"api_key: [REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"cookie=session-29\\\", \\\"cookie=[REDACTED]\\\"),\\n    (\\\"client_credential: c6D_8f\\\", \\\"client_credential: [REDACTED]\\\"),\\n]\\n\\n\\ndef make_observation(**changes):\\n    fields = {\\n        \\\"protocol_version\\\": 1,\\n        \\\"timestamp\\\": NOW,\\n        \\\"provider\\\": \\\"test-driver\\\",\\n        \\\"run_id\\\": \\\"run-1\\\",\\n        \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"session-1\\\",\\n        \\\"lane_id\\\": \\\"lane-1\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": ObservationType(\\\"activity.message\\\"),\\n        \\\"payload\\\": {\\\"message\\\": \\\"working\\\"},\\n    }\\n    fields.update(changes)\\n    return Observation(**fields)\\n\\n\\ndef make_summary(**changes):\\n    fields = {\\n        \\\"success\\\": False,\\n        \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"session-1\\\",\\n        \\\"failure_class\\\": FailureClass(\\\"agent\\\"),\\n        \\\"failure_detail\\\": \\\"request failed\\\",\\n        \\\"rate_limit_reset_at\\\": None,\\n        \\\"usage\\\": None,\\n    }\\n    fields.update(changes)\\n    return SessionSummary(**fields)\\n\\n\\ndef assert_ordinary_json(value):\\n    if type(value) is dict:\\n        assert all(type(key) is str for key in value)\\n        for child in value.values():\\n            assert_ordinary_json(child)\\n    elif type(value) is list:\\n        for child in value:\\n            assert_ordinary_json(child)\\n    else:\\n        assert type(value) in (str, int, float, bool, type(None))\\n\\n\"}}}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"result\":{\"status\":\"fulfilled\",\"value\":{\"chunk_id\":\"3a695e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":7.09e-7,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1335,\"output\":\"---\\nname: python-testing\\ndescription: Use when writing, fixing, or reviewing Python tests with pytest. Covers TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, coverage. Triggers on \\\"pytest\\\", \\\"python test\\\", \\\"conftest\\\", \\\"pytest.mark\\\", \\\"parametrize\\\", \\\"pytest fixture\\\", \\\"python mock\\\".\\ncompatibility: \\\"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Python Testing\\n\\nTDD: write the failing test (RED), make it pass (GREEN), refactor. One behavior per test. No logic in tests. Coverage target 80%, higher on critical paths.\\n\\n## Rulings\\n\\n**Mocking**\\n- Patch where the name is *used*, not where it's defined: `@patch(\\\"myapp.service.requests\\\")`, not `@patch(\\\"requests\\\")`.\\n- `autospec=True` so the mock rejects calls the real API would reject.\\n- Mock at the boundary (I/O, network, clock). Never mock the thing under test.\\n- Async: assert with `assert_awaited_once()`, not `assert_called_once()`.\\n\\n**Fixtures**\\n- `yield` for teardown; the line after `yield` is the cleanup.\\n- Default to function scope. Widen to `module`/`session` only for genuinely expensive resources.\\n- `autouse` hides dependencies — use sparingly; prefer explicit injection.\\n- `tmp_path` for temp files (auto-cleanup, `Path` API), not `tempfile`.\\n\\n**Parametrize**\\n- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` over loops — distinct test IDs, filterable with `-k`.\\n- Pass `ids=[...]` when params are objects or tuples; pytest already auto-names plain str/int/bool readably.\\n\\n**Config**\\n- One config in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.pytest.ini_options]`), not a separate `pytest.ini`.\\n- `--strict-markers` so a typo'd marker fails instead of silently passing.\\n- Register custom markers — e.g. `slow`, `@pytest.mark.unit`, `@pytest.mark.integration` — so `--strict-markers` catches a typo.\\n- Coverage locally: `pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing` — the missing-line report is the point; a bare percentage is not actionable.\\n\\n**Async (pytest-asyncio)**\\n- Default mode is `strict`: an async test with no `@pytest.mark.asyncio` is silently not collected. Set `asyncio_mode = \\\"auto\\\"` in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` to drop the per-test marker.\\n- Use `@pytest_asyncio.fixture` for async fixtures in strict mode.\\n---\\nname: python-patterns\\ndescription: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \\\"pythonic\\\", \\\"PEP 8\\\", \\\"python best practices\\\", \\\"python idioms\\\", \\\"bandit\\\".\\ncompatibility: \\\"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Python Patterns\\n\\nPick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\\n\\n## Idioms that earn their place\\n\\n| Rule | Why |\\n|------|-----|\\n| `X \\\\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\\n| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\\n| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\\n| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\\\"During handling...\\\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\\n| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\\n| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\\n\\n## Naming (PEP 8)\\n\\n`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\\n\\n**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\\n\\n## Traps\\n\\n```python\\n# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\\ndef bad(items=[]): ...\\ndef good(items=None):\\n    items = [] if items is None else items\\n\\n# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\\ntry: ...\\nexcept Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\\n\\n# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\\n# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\\n\\n# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\\n# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\\n\\nif value is None: ...             # never == None\\n```\\n\\nAvoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\\n\\n## Toolchain\\n\\n**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \\\"obvious\\\" returns.\\n\\n## Resources and laziness\\n\\nContext managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\\n\\n## Security\\n\\n- Read secrets with `os.environ[\\\"API_KEY\\\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\\n- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\\n- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\\n\"}}}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1222c-9ed0-73f1-9d0d-f846b680b016","create_time":1791574720.391105}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
