ate the negative oracle.\\n+3. strengthened: `test_observation_rejects_invalid_scalars_recursively_in_payload` and `test_sanitize_json_rejects_invalid_scalars_before_redaction` now place invalid values and mapping keys beneath 12 alternating dictionary/list/tuple containers, well beyond the demonstrated depth-four cutoff.\\n+4. strengthened: the identifier, summary, recursive payload, and sanitizer tests check exact start-position input, a middle position, and a surrogate after 96 valid prefix characters. Payload/sanitizer positions cover ordinary keys, sensitive-looking keys, and secret values as well as text values.\\n+5. strengthened: `test_shared_models_and_serializers_preserve_valid_unicode_scalars` and `test_usage_and_completion_preserve_valid_unicode_scalars` add U+00E9, Arabic/Devanagari/Korean text, combining marks, NUL and other control characters, and supplementary scalars. Shared positive tests now exercise all observation identifiers, payload keys/values, summaries, sanitization, and serialization/decoding with exact preservation assertions and strict UTF-8 checks.\\n+6. strengthened: `test_every_observation_type_rejects_invalid_scalar_payloads` parameterizes every public `ObservationType`, including `TOOL_STARTED`, with both value and key corruption. Each case first constructs and round-trips its valid control payload, then checks construction and native-record decoding reject the bad string with the scalar error. Key cases intentionally require recursive scalar validation before semantic rejection of a renamed mandatory field.\\n+7. strengthened: `test_text_subclasses_reject_invalid_scalars` wraps each invalid fixture in a genuine `str` subclass and exercises sanitizer root/value/key/sensitive-key locations, all four observation identifiers, summary session/failure text, and observation payload values/keys.\\n+8. strengthened: `test_sanitize_json_rejects_invalid_scalars_before_redaction`, `test_observation_rejects_invalid_scalars_recursively_in_payload`, `test_record_decoder_rejects_invalid_scalar_before_secret_redaction`, and the subclass test include sensitive-looking `password` keys containing surrogates with valid values. These must raise the same scalar error instead of retaining an invalid key with a redacted value.\\n+\\n+The orchestrator supplied verified public API contracts for previously unrepresented kinds: usage requires `usage`/`identity`; failure requires `failure_class`/`detail`; rate limits use `reset_at`/`window`/`detail`; raw unknown uses textual `reason`/`preview` and a 64-character lowercase hex `raw_sha256`; completion accepts full usage plus JSON extras; remaining kinds accept arbitrary mappings, with lane token totals represented by a nonnegative integer. These supplied contracts define the control fixtures; no production schema was inspected or invented.\\n+\\n+## Verification\\n+\\n+One narrow pytest run only, bounded to 300 seconds:\\n+\\n+```bash\\n+env UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/ovcaq-uv-cache mise exec -- uv run pytest -q --tb=line tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py\\n+```\\n+\\n+Result: `931 failed, 26 passed in 0.41s`; pytest exit code `1`. This is the expected red baseline while production scalar validation remains unimplemented. All 26 positive cases passed, including ordinary valid Unicode, controls, and decoded escaped pairs. No suite rerun or full-suite run occurred.\\n+\\n+Target-only Ruff formatting completed; target-only `ruff check` passed with exit code `0`. The file has 500 lines; its 15 test functions are each under 50 lines (largest: 31).\\n+\\n+Mutation verification was not rerun because this dispatch prohibits production edits. The added rejection/acceptance assertions directly distinguish each demonstrated exploit's behavior.\\n+\\n+Protocol note: the initial dispatch read used `cat` before the dispatch's embedded prohibition was known. Subsequent subprocess inspections and executions used explicit bounded timeouts; no further prohibited shell inspection commands were used.\\n+\\n+ASSUMPTIONS: none\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12236-c37a-7130-8980-ef8923edb138","create_time":1791575568.1374438}}}
