+{"timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:53:47.258Z","ordinal":15,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a1223a-835e-7452-99d7-f2de7a4239ff","turn_id":"01a1223a-83d0-7580-87e9-16cf2158ee62","session_id":"01a12232-fa5b-7120-a724-ea125be4783d","root_turn_id":"01a12232-fdfc-7282-a238-60d02bd08fb2","response_id":"resp_04a42ba97a869b67016ac946485b388191a66a39821a5b67a3","usage":{"input_tokens":23284,"cached_input_tokens":22912,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":85,"reasoning_output_tokens":19,"total_tokens":23369},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":23284,"cached_input_tokens":22912,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":85,"reasoning_output_tokens":19,"total_tokens":23369},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":23284,"cached_input_tokens":22912,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":85,"reasoning_output_tokens":19,"total_tokens":23369}}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:53:47.317Z","ordinal":16,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a1223a-835e-7452-99d7-f2de7a4239ff","turn_id":"01a1223a-83d0-7580-87e9-16cf2158ee62","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e1d77e39-e83f-46f5-844d-105f3af78dd8","process_id":"88228","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-1.txt"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-1.txt","name":"dispatch-ivan-1.txt","path":"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-1.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\nYou are Ivan, the implementor. Make all failing tests pass. Tests ARE the\nspec. Do NOT modify test files unless your allowlist below names them (a\ntest-only task lists them on purpose). Do NOT read the task's acceptance criteria —\nnone are provided to you on purpose.\n\n## Failing tests\n\n\"\"\"Unicode scalar contracts for shared observations, independent of drivers.\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ovcaq.events import (\n    FailureClass,\n    Observation,\n    ObservationType,\n    SessionSummary,\n    observation_from_record,\n    observation_record,\n    sanitize_json,\n    summary_record,\n)\n\nNOW = datetime(2026, 9, 26, 12, 30, 15, 123456, tzinfo=UTC)\nINVALID_SCALARS = (\n    \"\\ud800\",\n    \"\\ud801\",\n    \"\\udbff\",\n    \"\\udc00\",\n    \"\\udc01\",\n    \"\\udfff\",\n    \"\\ud83d\\ude80\",\n)\nSCALAR_IDS = [\n    \"high-start\",\n    \"high-interior\",\n    \"high-end\",\n    \"low-start\",\n    \"low-interior\",\n    \"low-end\",\n    \"uncombined-pair\",\n]\nVALID_SCALARS = (\n    \"\",\n    \"Žluťoučký 日本語\",\n    \"é\",\n    \"العربية हिन्दी 한국어\",\n    \"e\\u0301\",\n    \"\\x00\\t\\n\\x1f\\x7f\",\n    \"\\ud7ff\\ue000\",\n    \"\\U00010000\\U0010ffff\",\n    \"\\U0001f680\",\n)\nSCALAR_ERROR = r\"^Strings must contain only Unicode scalar values$\"\nUSAGE_DATA = {\n    \"input_tokens\": 1,\n    \"output_tokens\": 2,\n    \"cache_creation_input_tokens\": None,\n    \"cache_read_input_tokens\": None,\n    \"tool_uses\": None,\n    \"cost_usd\": None,\n    \"estimated\": False,\n}\n\n\ndef make_observation(**changes: Any) -> Observation:\n    fields = {\n        \"protocol_version\": 1,\n        \"timestamp\": NOW,\n        \"provider\": \"test-driver\",\n        \"run_id\": \"run-1\",\n        \"session_id\": \"session-1\",\n        \"lane_id\": \"lane-1\",\n        \"type\": ObservationType.ACTIVITY_MESSAGE,\n        \"payload\": {\"message\": \"working\"},\n    }\n    fields.update(changes)\n    return Observation(**fields)\n\n\ndef make_summary(**changes: Any) -> SessionSummary:\n    fields = {\n        \"success\": False,\n        \"session_id\": \"session-1\",\n        \"failure_class\": FailureClass.AGENT,\n        \"failure_detail\": \"request failed\",\n        \"rate_limit_reset_at\": None,\n        \"usage\": None,\n    }\n    fields.update(changes)\n    return SessionSummary(**fields)\n\n\ndef assert_scalar_json(value: object) -> None:\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        for key, child in value.items():\n            key.encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n            assert_scalar_json(child)\n    elif isinstance(value, list):\n        for child in value:\n            assert_scalar_json(child)\n    elif isinstance(value, str):\n        value.encode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"strict\")\n\n\ndef replace_record_string(value: Any, original: str, replacement: str) -> Any:\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        return {\n            replacement if key == original else key: replace_record_string(\n                child, original, replacement\n            )\n            for key, child in value.items()\n        }\n    if isinstance(value, list):\n        return [replace_record_string(child, original, replacement) for child in value]\n    return replacement if value == original else value\n\n\ndef positioned_scalar(scalar: str, position: str) -> str:\n    if position == \"middle\":\n        return f\"prefix{scalar}suffix\"\n    if position == \"long_prefix\":\n        return f\"{'a' * 96}{scalar}suffix\"\n    return scalar\n\n\ndef invalid_native_record(record: dict[str, Any], scalar: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    # JSON decoding combines adjacent high/low escapes into a valid scalar.\n    # A caller-supplied Python record still must reject uncombined code units.\n    if scalar == \"\\ud83d\\ude80\":\n        return record\n    return json.loads(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=True))\n\n\ndef nested_json(value: Any, depth: int) -> Any:\n    for index in range(depth):\n        if index % 3 == 0:\n            value = {\"nested\": value}\n        elif index % 3 == 1:\n            value = [value]\n        else:\n            value = (value,)\n    return value\n\n\ndef payload_for_type(event_type: ObservationType) -> dict[str, Any]:\n    if event_type is ObservationType.USAGE_UPDATED:\n        return {\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"identity\": \"valid\"}\n    if event_type is ObservationType.SESSION_COMPLETED:\n        return {\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"message\": \"valid\"}\n    if event_type is ObservationType.SESSION_FAILED:\n        return {\"failure_class\": FailureClass.AGENT.value, \"detail\": \"valid\"}\n    if event_type is ObservationType.RATE_LIMIT_STARTED:\n        return {\"reset_at\": None, \"window\": None, \"detail\": \"valid\"}\n    if event_type is ObservationType.RAW_UNKNOWN:\n        return {\"reason\": \"valid\", \"raw_sha256\": \"0\" * 64, \"preview\": \"valid\"}\n    return {\"message\": \"valid\", \"total_tokens\": 0}\n\n\nclass ScalarText(str):\n    \"\"\"An ordinary string subclass accepted by the public text interfaces.\"\"\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"field\", [\"provider\", \"run_id\", \"session_id\", \"lane_id\"])\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"position\", [\"start\", \"middle\", \"long_prefix\"])\ndef test_observation_rejects_invalid_scalar_identifiers(\n    field: str, scalar: str, position: str\n) -> None:\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        make_observation(**{field: positioned_scalar(scalar, position)})\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"location\",\n    [\n        \"value\",\n        \"nested_value\",\n        \"nested_key\",\n        \"tuple\",\n        \"tuple_key\",\n        \"secret\",\n        \"secret_key\",\n        \"deep_value\",\n        \"deep_key\",\n    ],\n)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"position\", [\"start\", \"middle\", \"long_prefix\"])\ndef test_observation_rejects_invalid_scalars_recursively_in_payload(\n    location: str, scalar: str, position: str\n) -> None:\n    scalar = positioned_scalar(scalar, position)\n    payloads = {\n        \"value\": {\"message\": scalar},\n        \"nested_value\": {\"message\": [\"valid\", {\"nested\": scalar}]},\n        \"nested_key\": {\"message\": [\"valid\", {scalar: \"valid\"}]},\n        \"tuple\": {\"message\": (\"valid\", {\"nested\": scalar})},\n        \"tuple_key\": {\"message\": (\"valid\", {scalar: \"valid\"})},\n        \"secret\": {\"message\": \"valid\", \"password\": scalar},\n        \"secret_key\": {\"message\": \"valid\", f\"password{scalar}\": \"valid\"},\n        \"deep_value\": {\"message\": nested_json(scalar, 12)},\n        \"deep_key\": {\"message\": nested_json({scalar: \"valid\"}, 12)},\n    }\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        make_observation(payload=payloads[location])\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"field\", [\"session_id\", \"failure_detail\"])\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"position\", [\"start\", \"middle\", \"long_prefix\"])\ndef test_summary_rejects_invalid_scalar_strings(\n    field: str, scalar: str, position: str\n) -> None:\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        make_summary(**{field: positioned_scalar(scalar, position)})\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"location\",\n    [\n        \"root\",\n        \"list\",\n        \"tuple\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"nested_key\",\n        \"tuple_key\",\n        \"secret\",\n        \"secret_key\",\n        \"deep_value\",\n        \"deep_key\",\n    ],\n)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"position\", [\"start\", \"middle\", \"long_prefix\"])\ndef test_sanitize_json_rejects_invalid_scalars_before_redaction(\n    location: str, scalar: str, position: str\n) -> None:\n    scalar = positioned_scalar(scalar, position)\n    values = {\n        \"root\": scalar,\n        \"list\": [\"valid\", scalar],\n        \"tuple\": (\"valid\", scalar),\n        \"value\": {\"message\": [\"valid\", {\"nested\": scalar}]},\n        \"nested_key\": {\"message\": [\"valid\", {scalar: \"valid\"}]},\n        \"tuple_key\": {\"message\": (\"valid\", {scalar: \"valid\"})},\n        \"secret\": {\"password\": scalar},\n        \"secret_key\": {f\"password{scalar}\": \"valid\"},\n        \"deep_value\": nested_json(scalar, 12),\n        \"deep_key\": nested_json({scalar: \"valid\"}, 12),\n    }\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        sanitize_json(values[location])\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"original\", [\"test-driver\", \"run-1\", \"session-1\", \"lane-1\", \"marker\", \"nested\"]\n)\ndef test_observation_record_decoder_rejects_invalid_scalars(\n    original: str, scalar: str\n) -> None:\n    valid = make_observation(payload={\"message\": [\"marker\", {\"nested\": \"valid\"}]})\n    record = replace_record_string(observation_record(valid), original, scalar)\n    decoded_record = invalid_native_record(record, scalar)\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        observation_from_record(decoded_record)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\ndef test_usage_observation_rejects_invalid_scalar_identity(scalar: str) -> None:\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        make_observation(\n            type=ObservationType.USAGE_UPDATED,\n            payload={\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"identity\": f\"request-{scalar}\"},\n        )\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\ndef test_usage_record_decoder_rejects_invalid_scalar_identity(scalar: str) -> None:\n    valid = make_observation(\n        type=ObservationType.USAGE_UPDATED,\n        payload={\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"identity\": \"request-1\"},\n    )\n    record = observation_record(valid)\n    record[\"payload\"] = {\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"identity\": f\"request-{scalar}\"}\n    decoded_record = invalid_native_record(record, scalar)\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        observation_from_record(decoded_record)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"location\", [\"secret_value\", \"secret_key\"])\ndef test_record_decoder_rejects_invalid_scalar_before_secret_redaction(\n    scalar: str,\n    location: str,\n) -> None:\n    record = observation_record(make_observation())\n    secret = (\n        {\"password\": scalar}\n        if location == \"secret_value\"\n        else {f\"password{scalar}\": \"valid\"}\n    )\n    record[\"payload\"] = {\"message\": \"valid\", **secret}\n    decoded_record = invalid_native_record(record, scalar)\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        observation_from_record(decoded_record)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"location\", [\"value\", \"nested_key\", \"secret\"])\ndef test_completion_observation_rejects_invalid_scalars_before_redaction(\n    location: str, scalar: str\n) -> None:\n    additions = {\n        \"value\": {\"extra\": {\"nested\": scalar}},\n        \"nested_key\": {\"extra\": {scalar: \"valid\"}},\n        \"secret\": {\"password\": scalar},\n    }\n    payload = {\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"message\": \"done\", **additions[location]}\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        make_observation(type=ObservationType.SESSION_COMPLETED, payload=payload)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"location\", [\"value\", \"nested_key\", \"secret\"])\ndef test_completion_record_decoder_rejects_invalid_scalars_before_redaction(\n    location: str, scalar: str\n) -> None:\n    valid = make_observation(\n        type=ObservationType.SESSION_COMPLETED,\n        payload={\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"message\": \"done\"},\n    )\n    additions = {\n        \"value\": {\"extra\": {\"nested\": scalar}},\n        \"nested_key\": {\"extra\": {scalar: \"valid\"}},\n        \"secret\": {\"password\": scalar},\n    }\n    record = observation_record(valid)\n    record[\"payload\"] = {\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"message\": \"done\", **additions[location]}\n    decoded_record = invalid_native_record(record, scalar)\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        observation_from_record(decoded_record)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"event_type\", list(ObservationType))\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"location\", [\"value\", \"key\"])\ndef test_every_observation_type_rejects_invalid_scalar_payloads(\n    event_type: ObservationType, location: str, scalar: str\n) -> None:\n    valid_payload = payload_for_type(event_type)\n    valid = make_observation(type=event_type, payload=valid_payload)\n    valid_record = observation_record(valid)\n    assert observation_from_record(valid_record) == valid\n    assert valid_record[\"payload\"] == valid_payload\n    if location == \"value\":\n        payload = replace_record_string(valid_payload, \"valid\", scalar)\n    else:\n        key = next(iter(valid_payload))\n        payload = {\n            f\"{key}{scalar}\" if name == key else name: value\n            for name, value in valid_payload.items()\n        }\n\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        make_observation(type=event_type, payload=payload)\n    valid_record[\"payload\"] = payload\n    decoded = invalid_native_record(valid_record, scalar)\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        observation_from_record(decoded)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"scalar\", INVALID_SCALARS, ids=SCALAR_IDS)\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"interface\",\n    [\n        \"root\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"key\",\n        \"secret_key\",\n        \"provider\",\n        \"run_id\",\n        \"session_id\",\n        \"lane_id\",\n        \"summary_session_id\",\n        \"failure_detail\",\n        \"payload_value\",\n        \"payload_key\",\n    ],\n)\ndef test_text_subclasses_reject_invalid_scalars(interface: str, scalar: str) -> None:\n    text = ScalarText(scalar)\n    values = {\n        \"root\": text,\n        \"value\": {\"value\": text},\n        \"key\": {text: \"valid\"},\n        \"secret_key\": {ScalarText(f\"password{scalar}\"): \"valid\"},\n    }\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError, match=SCALAR_ERROR):\n        if interface in values:\n            sanitize_json(values[interface])\n        elif interface == \"summary_session_id\":\n            make_summary(session_id=text)\n        elif interface == \"failure_detail\":\n            make_summary(failure_detail=text)\n        elif interface == \"payload_value\":\n            make_observation(payload={\"message\": text})\n        elif interface == \"payload_key\":\n            make_observation(payload={\"message\": {text: \"valid\"}})\n        else:\n            make_observation(**{interface: text})\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"text\", [text for text in VALID_SCALARS if text])\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"event_type\", [ObservationType.USAGE_UPDATED, ObservationType.SESSION_COMPLETED]\n)\ndef test_usage_and_completion_preserve_valid_unicode_scalars(\n    event_type: ObservationType, text: str\n) -> None:\n    payload = (\n        {\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"identity\": text}\n        if event_type is ObservationType.USAGE_UPDATED\n        else {\"usage\": USAGE_DATA, \"message\": text, \"extra\": {text: text}}\n    )\n    observation = make_observation(type=event_type, payload=payload)\n    record = observation_record(observation)\n    restored = observation_from_record(\n        json.loads(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=True))\n    )\n\n    assert record[\"payload\"] == payload\n    assert restored.type is event_type\n    assert observation_record(restored)[\"payload\"] == payload\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"text\", VALID_SCALARS)\ndef test_shared_models_and_serializers_preserve_valid_unicode_scalars(\n    text: str,\n) -> None:\n    payload = {\"message\": [text, {text: text}, None]}\n    observation = make_observation(\n        provider=text or \"test-driver\",\n        run_id=text or \"run-1\",\n        session_id=text or None,\n        lane_id=text or None,\n        payload=payload,\n    )\n    summary = make_summary(session_id=text or None, failure_detail=text)\n\n    assert sanitize_json(payload) == payload\n    assert sanitize_json(None) is None\n    assert sanitize_json(text) == text\n    record = observation_record(observation)\n    assert record[\"payload\"] == payload\n    for field in (\"provider\", \"run_id\", \"session_id\", \"lane_id\"):\n        assert record[field] == getattr(observation, field)\n    restored = observation_from_record(\n        json.loads(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=False))\n    )\n    assert observation_record(restored)[\"payload\"] == payload\n    assert restored.session_id == observation.session_id\n    assert restored == observation\n    assert summary.failure_detail == text\n    assert summary_record(summary)[\"session_id\"] == (text or None)\n    assert summary_record(summary)[\"failure_detail\"] == text\n    assert_scalar_json(record)\n    assert_scalar_json(summary_record(summary))\n\n\ndef test_valid_escaped_surrogate_pair_decodes_to_supported_scalar() -> None:\n    scalar = json.loads(r'\"\\ud83d\\ude80\"')\n    assert scalar == \"\\U0001f680\"\n    observation = make_observation(\n        provider=scalar,\n        run_id=scalar,\n        session_id=scalar,\n        lane_id=scalar,\n        payload={\"message\": [scalar, {scalar: scalar}]},\n    )\n    summary = make_summary(session_id=scalar, failure_detail=scalar)\n\n    assert sanitize_json({scalar: scalar}) == {scalar: scalar}\n    record = observation_record(observation)\n    restored = observation_from_record(\n        json.loads(json.dumps(record, ensure_ascii=True))\n    )\n    assert restored == observation\n    assert restored.provider == scalar\n    assert observation_record(restored)[\"payload\"] == {\n        \"message\": [scalar, {scalar: scalar}]\n    }\n    assert summary.session_id == scalar\n    assert summary.failure_detail == scalar\n    assert summary_record(summary)[\"session_id\"] == scalar\n    assert summary_record(summary)[\"failure_detail\"] == scalar\n    assert_scalar_json(record)\n    assert_scalar_json(summary_record(summary))\n\n\n## Architecture context\n\n# AGENTS.md — OVCAQ\n\nOVCAQ means **Orchestration, Visibility, and Control for Agent Queues**. It is\nan installable Python CLI/TUI that supervises a PRD-driven workflow through\nClaude Code, Codex, or another headless coding agent.\n\nThe global `AGENTS.md` remains in force. This file adds project-specific rules.\n\n## Current state\n\nThe repository is in planning/bootstrap. Until an implementation PRD replaces\nit, `docs/dev/project-management/plans/implementation-plan.md` is the architecture and sequencing\nauthority. Do not create production modules opportunistically outside that\nsequence.\n\n## Product boundary\n\nOVCAQ core owns state, lifecycle commands, process supervision, agent adapters,\nnormalized events, observability, the TUI, and launcher provisioning checks.\n\nOVCAQ core does **not** contain launcher-specific skills, agents, hooks, or\nplugins. Those live in external marketplaces. Core may carry declarative\nidentifiers and version requirements needed to reconcile them.\n\n## Architecture invariants\n\n1. **One state writer.** Every durable `state.json` mutation goes through the\n   state store. Agents mutate state only through `ovcaq state` or a higher-level\n   OVCAQ command. Never instruct an agent to edit `state.json` directly.\n2. **State decides; prose does not.** Session completion, phase handoff, pause,\n   drain, retry, and failure decisions derive from committed state plus a\n   normalized session result. A final agent message is never authoritative.\n3. **Provider code stays at the edge.** Claude/Codex argv, environment variables,\n   event formats, model names, rate-limit parsing, and connectivity checks live\n   under their adapter. Shared runtime and UI code must not parse provider-native\n   events.\n4. **Raw evidence survives normalization.** Preserve each session's raw output.\n   Normalizers are tolerant and must degrade to an unknown/raw observation\n   instead of crashing the supervisor.\n5. **The TUI observes shared models.** It reads state, registry, metrics, and\n   normalized observations. It does not implement lifecycle policy or maintain a\n   second liveness algorithm.\n6. **External capabilities stay external.** Provisioning invokes a launcher's\n   supported marketplace/plugin CLI and verifies the result. It does not copy\n   plugin contents into this package or hand-edit launcher caches.\n7. **No shell evaluation of configured commands.** Store agent commands as argv\n   arrays and spawn them without `shell=True`.\n\n## Target layout\n\n```text\nsrc/ovcaq/\n  state/        # schema, transactions, compound mutations\n  workflow/     # PRD selection, transitions, records, policy\n  runtime/      # supervisor, decisions, registry, process ownership\n  drivers/      # Claude, Codex, and generic command adapters\n  events/       # normalized event model and session reduction\n  tui/          # discovery and Textual/Rich presentation\n  provision/    # marketplace/plugin reconciliation\ntests/          # mirrors package boundaries; provider JSONL fixtures\ndocs/           # tracked architecture and operator documentation\n```\n\n## Toolchain\n\n- Python 3.12+ managed through `mise`.\n- `uv` for environments, locking, build, and command execution.\n- `pytest` for tests; `ruff` for formatting/linting; `mypy` for package types.\n- Keep the runtime dependency set small. Textual/Rich are justified by the TUI;\n  prefer the standard library for state, locking, configuration, and subprocesses.\n\nPlanned verification commands once the scaffold lands:\n\n```bash\nuv sync --all-groups\nuv run pytest\nuv run ruff check .\nuv run ruff format --check .\nuv run mypy src/ovcaq\nuv build\n```\n\n## Development rules\n\n- Characterize current behavior before moving it from `~/.claude`.\n- Extract state first, then pure workflow logic, runtime, adapters, TUI, and\n  provisioning in that order.\n- Sanitized Claude and Codex JSONL fixtures belong in `tests/fixtures/`; tests\n  never read live files from `~/.claude` or `~/.codex`.\n- Test process-group, lock, and signal behavior with real subprocesses in\n  addition to unit tests.\n- Documentation for commands comes from the same command registry/parser as the\n  implementation; do not maintain a second hand-written verb inventory.\n- Keep provider-neutral modules free of the strings `claude`, `anthropic`,\n  `codex`, and provider model identifiers except in tests that enforce this rule.\n- Use conventional commits. No compatibility shim, dual writer, or rollback\n  framework is required for the initial cutover.\n\n## Migration stance\n\nThis is a one-way early-stage extraction. Start a fresh OVCAQ batch/state tree;\ndo not build an importer for the current `docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json` unless\na later requirement explicitly needs it. Temporary delegation during a local\ncanary is acceptable, but do not ship `autoclaude`, `autopilot`, `tracon`, or\n`statectl` aliases as permanent public APIs.\n\nContract:\n — design Interfaces & contracts; target paths anchored to repository root):\n```python\n# /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/events/model.py — new module-level internal helper;\n# imported directly by events.tail, not re-exported from ovcaq.events.\ndef has_invalid_unicode_scalar(value: object) -> bool: ...\n\n# Existing public signature; validation wraps the existing recursive copier.\ndef sanitize_json(value: object) -> JSONValue: ...\n\n# New private recursive copier: existing sanitize_json body moves here,\n# and its recursion uses _sanitize_json rather than repeating root scans.\ndef _sanitize_json(value: object) -> JSONValue: ...\n\n# Existing boundaries; signatures retained.\ndef _identifier(value: object, *, optional: bool = False) -> None: ...\ndef _payload(\n    kind: ObservationType, payload: Mapping[str, JSONValue]\n) -> dict[str, JSONValue]: ...\ndef observation_record(observation: Observation) -> dict[str, JSONValue]: ...\ndef observation_from_record(record: Mapping[str, JSONValue]) -> Observation: ...\ndef summary_record(summary: SessionSummary) -> dict[str, JSONValue]: ...\n\n```\n\n`has_invalid_unicode_scalar(value)` is a side-effect-free predicate over strings,\n`Mapping` keys and values, and list/tuple elements. It returns `True` iff any\nreachable string contains a code point in the inclusive range\n`0xD800..0xDFFF`. Other scalar types are ignored; existing JSON/type/finite-number\nvalidation remains responsible for their acceptance. Scan supported acyclic\nJSON-like containers iteratively to avoid introducing a new recursion-depth\nfailure during preflight. It neither redacts nor modifies input. Ordinary\nUnicode, including non-BMP scalars, remains unchanged. `json.loads` decodes a\nvalid escaped high/low surrogate pair to one non-BMP scalar, which is accepted;\nunpaired decoded surrogates and Python strings still containing surrogate code\npoints are rejected. This is validation, never replacement or ASCII escaping.\n\n`sanitize_json` checks the complete original input with the predicate before\ncalling `_sanitize_json`; invalid input raises\n`ValueError(\"Strings must contain only Unicode scalar values\")`. Check nested\nkeys and every value, including values beneath sensitive keys which will later\nbe replaced by `[REDACTED]`. Preserve existing valid-container copying,\ncredential redaction, nonstring-key `TypeError`, nonfinite-number rejection and\nunsupported-type errors. `_sanitize_json` retains existing recursive behavior\nand uses its own name for recursion, so the complete scalar scan runs once per\npublic `sanitize_json` invocation rather than once for every subtree.\n\n`_identifier` retains its nonempty-string/optional-None rules, then rejects\ninvalid scalar strings with the same static `ValueError`. This protects\n`Observation.provider`, `run_id`, `session_id`, `lane_id`, and the existing\n`SessionSummary.session_id` caller. `_payload` checks the complete original\nmapping before inspecting payload shapes or taking the `_usage_payload` early\nreturn. Thus `usage.updated.identity`, nested usage keys/values and\n`session.completed`'s special usage branch cannot bypass scalar validation.\nInvalid strings fail before sanitization, truncation or freezing, even if those\noperations would have removed them. `SessionSummary.__post_init__` checks a\nnonnull string `failure_detail` before its existing sanitizer and 4096-character\ncap. Existing invalid-type checks stay in place. `observation_record`,\n`observation_from_record` and `summary_record` retain their signatures and field\nshapes and serialize only successfully constructed validated models. Error\nmessages never include the rejected string, mapping key, or credential.\n\n\n\n\nHost: use only named writable paths; tests listed in Failing tests are read-only unless on allowlist. UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/ovcaq-uv-cache. Reading budget: read the named module once, focus on named functions; implement in boundary order, run only the named narrow test file. Read /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md when editing Python. No commits or state edits. Save report to docs/dev/tmp/ivan-1-output.md.\n\n\n## Files you may read and modify\n\n/Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/src/ovcaq/events/model.py\n/Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/CHANGELOG.md\n\nRead only the files listed above. If a file or symbol you need is not\nlisted, stop and report it as a blocker — do not run broad `rg` sweeps to\ndiscover scope.\n\n\n\n### Code quality rules (mandatory)\n\nFollow these four rules. They override any instinct to \"improve\" the code\nbeyond what the failing tests require.\n\n**1. Think before coding.** Re-read the task and the failing tests. If scope,\ndata shape, target file, or success criteria are ambiguous - more than one\nreasonable implementation would pass the tests differently - STOP and report\nthe ambiguity as a blocker. Do not guess and proceed.\n\n**2. Simplicity.** Write the simplest code that makes the failing tests pass.\n\n- No abstractions, helpers, or interfaces built for a single caller.\n- No error handling, fallbacks, or validation for inputs the tests never\n  exercise. Validate at real system boundaries only.\n- No features, options, or configuration the task did not ask for.\n- If your draft runs long and the same behavior fits in far fewer lines,\n  rewrite it before returning.\n\n**3. Surgical changes.** Touch only what the task requires.\n\n- Do not refactor, reformat, or \"improve\" code outside the change.\n- Match the surro