29:            else None\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:330:        ),\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:331:        \"rate_limit_reset_at\": (\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:332:            _timestamp(summary.rate_limit_reset_at)\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:333:            if summary.rate_limit_reset_at is not None\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:334:            else None\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:335:        ),\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:336:        \"usage\": asdict(summary.usage) if summary.usage is not None else None,\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:337:    }\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:1:---\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:2:name: python-patterns\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:3:description: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \"pythonic\", \"PEP 8\", \"python best practices\", \"python idioms\", \"bandit\".\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:4:compatibility: \"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\"\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:5:---\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:6:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:7:# Python Patterns\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:8:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:9:Pick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:10:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:11:## Idioms that earn their place\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:12:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:13:| Rule | Why |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:14:|------|-----|\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:15:| `X \\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:16:| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:17:| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:18:| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\"During handling...\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:19:| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:20:| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:21:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:22:## Naming (PEP 8)\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:23:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:24:`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:25:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:26:**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:27:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:28:## Traps\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:29:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:30:```python\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:31:# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:32:def bad(items=[]): ...\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:33:def good(items=None):\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:34:    items = [] if items is None else items\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:35:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:36:# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:37:try: ...\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:38:except Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:39:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:40:# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:41:# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:42:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:43:# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:44:# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:45:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:46:if value is None: ...             # never == None\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:47:```\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:48:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:49:Avoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:50:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:51:## Toolchain\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:52:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:53:**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \"obvious\" returns.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:54:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:55:## Resources and laziness\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:56:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:57:Context managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:58:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:59:## Security\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:60:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:61:- Read secrets with `os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:62:- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:63:- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\n"},"started_at_ms":1791575635642,"completed_at_ms":1791575635642}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:53:55.645Z","ordinal":26,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1223a-b6bd-7c53-882e-4471fecca5a3","call_id":"call_455bcc09360d424bbede19c1e93ef07c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 11437)\nTotal output lines: 1\n\n{\"chunk_id\":\"1779d9\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":11204,\"output\":\"CHANGELOG.md:1:# Changelog\\nCHANGELOG.md:2:\\nCHANGELOG.md:3:All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\\nCHANGELOG.md:4:\\nCHANGELOG.md:5:The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).\\nCHANGELOG.md:6:\\nCHANGELOG.md:7:## [Unreleased]\\nCHANGELOG.md:8:\\nCHANGELOG.md:9:### Added\\nCHANGELOG.md:10:\\nCHANGELOG.md:11:- **drivers**: run supervised workflows with Codex, configured models and effort, verified version/authentication checks, and state-based phase handoffs.\\nCHANGELOG.md:12:- **drivers**: show Codex activity, tools, receiver lanes and cache-aware usage with retained raw evidence; conflicting native threads fail safely even after supervisor ownership binding.\\nCHANGELOG.md:13:- **tui**: add `ovcaq attach`, TTY-default attachment for `ovcaq run`, detachable interactive controls with plain fallback, and interactive `resume` that attaches to a live supervisor or launches once after a boundary pause.\\nCHANGELOG.md:14:- **runtime**: run batch capabilities as durable provider-neutral attempts with private session evidence, final metrics, stale-owner reconciliation, and explicit one-attempt retry of failed capabilities.\\nCHANGELOG.md:15:- **state**: add guarded compound supervisor mutations for pause/resume, progress fingerprints, capability attempts, failure attention, and empty-drain completion.\\nCHANGELOG.md:16:- **runtime**: publish one immutable canonical metric row per phase or capability session, reconcile interrupted evidence deterministically, and project versioned metrics through legacy-compatible reports.\\nCHANGELOG.md:17:- **config**: resolve provider-neutral build, review, and done routes with validated effort, timeout, model-tier, retry-policy, and literal prompt configuration; drivers now expose the version-two default-prompt contract.\\nCHANGELOG.md:18:- **config**: load immutable per-agent argv, tier, environment, and JSON option settings with user/project merging and credential-shaped value rejection.\\nCHANGELOG.md:19:- **drivers**: define the immutable provider-neutral launch, health, plugin, and discovery contracts with exact-version, duplicate-name, and fail-closed probe validation.\\nCHANGELOG.md:20:- **drivers**: add the shell-free Claude launch adapter with explicit unattended permissions, configured tier and fallback resolution, isolated environment construction, executable health checks, and neutral summary reduction.\\nCHANGELOG.md:21:- **drivers**: normalize Claude init, activity, tool, lane, usage, rate-limit, and terminal stream records with bounded replay-safe identity tracking and closed failure classification.\\nCHANGELOG.md:22:- **events**: define the immutable version-one observation, usage, failure, summary, redaction, validation, and JSON record contract.\\nCHANGELOG.md:23:- **events**: deterministically reduce normalized sessions, fold cumulative usage without double counting, preserve typed completion usage, and synthesize sanitized failure observations.\\nCHANGELOG.md:24:- **events**: persist private normalized JSONL and decode bounded newline frames only after exact raw bytes are durably recorded, with observable sanitized fallbacks for oversized or failing frames.\\nCHANGELOG.md:25:- **runtime**: resolve secure project, runtime, fleet, and evidence paths with validated limits and stable documented field order; probe required macOS process and durability capabilities; and publish, observe, prune, and conditionally remove identity-pinned fleet records behind inode-stable run locks without launch contention.\\nCHANGELOG.md:26:- **runtime**: own shell-free process groups through persistent anchors, preserve descendant ownership and validated cleanup ancestry without mutating substituted paths, escalate timed-out groups from TERM to KILL through serialized bounded watchdogs, map supervisor signals to exit statuses, and durably remove matching ownership records while retaining evidence and lock files.\\nCHANGELOG.md:27:- **runtime**: persist complete bounded raw session bytes; publish private metadata and summaries that reject unsafe identifiers, mismatches, non-UTC timestamps, and empty required fields; inventory retained evidence; and apply explicit active-safe purge plans with verified ancestry, locks, bounded malformed-row preservation, and durable deletion.\\nCHANGELOG.md:28:- **runtime**: gate launches on durable emergency state-write evidence, preserve concurrent evidence, reject malformed or deeply nested records, revalidate evidence before acknowledgement, archive the exact acknowledged record, and restore the gate after failed acknowledgement.\\nCHANGELOG.md:29:- **cli**: expose runtime status, actionable doctor resource checks, retained-log lookup/follow, non-applying purge previews, and explicit purge application; reject conflicting parent log options, omit internal path metadata, and reuse validated state for emergency acknowledgement.\\nCHANGELOG.md:30:- Import-only package boundaries and a help-only `ovcaq` command.\\nCHANGELOG.md:31:- Versioned v1 state schema/defaults and the exhaustive legacy-field crosswalk.\\nCHANGELOG.md:32:- Closed v1 state validation with nested, resource, and cross-field invariants.\\nCHANGELOG.md:33:- Locked state-store transactions with canonical publication, raw backups, and restore.\\nCHANGELOG.md:34:- Monotonic revisions and locked compare-and-set conflict checks for transactions and restores.\\nCHANGELOG.md:35:- Create-only initialization requires an existing runtime directory and repairs failed publications.\\nCHANGELOG.md:36:- Pure JSON-path parsing and in-memory get/set/append/delete recovery operations.\\nCHANGELOG.md:37:- Atomic StateService task, attempt, metadata, count, and contract-card commands.\\nCHANGELOG.md:38:- Parsed-token protection for generic state recovery, with explicit unsafe override.\\nCHANGELOG.md:39:- P01-T10 state CLI dispatch, stable errors, root discovery, and parser-derived command documentation.\\nCHANGELOG.md:40:\\nCHANGELOG.md:41:### Fixed\\nCHANGELOG.md:42:\\nCHANGELOG.md:43:- **cli**: reject unhealthy adapters before foreground agent execution using sanitized health diagnostics.\\nCHANGELOG.md:44:- **tui**: show bounded normalized tool, message and plan activity alongside selected-session lanes with literal markup.\\nCHANGELOG.md:45:\\nCHANGELOG.md:46:- **tui**: surface selected-run observation read errors as gaps while preserving ownership checks and process-control exceptions.\\nCHANGELOG.md:47:- **runtime**: keep standalone `run_once()` usable without full-loop ownership metadata while preserving supervisor identity across full-run sessions.\\nCHANGELOG.md:48:- **runtime**: preserve unknown numeric usage in final metrics while retaining exact fields and strict validation of known values.\\nCHANGELOG.md:49:- **tui**: fall back after ordinary interactive-view failures, detach plain viewers on real EOF, and print only changed frames while preserving terminal results.\\nCHANGELOG.md:50:- **tui**: persist theme changes from both views, honor trusted XDG aliases, and use private no-follow theme I/O with replacement checks that tolerate concurrent readers.\\nCHANGELOG.md:51:- **tui**: sanitize both fleet selectors and show stale/malformed registry counts and empty-fleet status without selecting a run.\\nCHANGELOG.md:52:- **launcher**: recognize verified fast completion and attachment cleanup races, preserve bounded private startup diagnostics, honor configured runtime roots, and guide duplicate-owner failures to attach even while the new child is still starting.\\nCHANGELOG.md:53:- **cli**: require explicit foreground mode for JSON runs and load viewer dependencies only for interactive commands.\\nCHANGELOG.md:54:- **tui**: guard selected-run pause/resume through durable publication, reuse those controls for interactive resume, and honor the injected fleet registry for stop.\\nCHANGELOG.md:55:- **runtime**: provide shared ownership exclusion for guarded state mutations, preserving state and backup bytes when a selected owner becomes stale during publication.\\nCHANGELOG.md:56:- **tui**: keep controls responsive during observation reads and show elapsed selected-run duration instead of summed session times; terminal duration uses durable end evidence so late polls cannot inflate it.\\nCHANGELOG.md:57:- **runtime**: bind terminal observations to the exact supervisor and revalidate evidence reads without competing for the launch lock or discarding ordinary active state progress.\\nCHANGELOG.md:58:- **tui**: display normalized lane descriptions when an explicit lane label is absent.\\nCHANGELOG.md:59:- **events**: bind normalized observations to the owning supervisor run and session while retaining exact native raw evidence.\\nCHANGELOG.md:60:- **tui**: retain selected final state and telemetry after supervisor cleanup, reject replacement evidence, and render terminal outcomes before viewers exit.\\nCHANGELOG.md:61:- **tui**: follow active session telemetry across rollover, retain stream damage diagnostics, preserve live usage and numeric costs, show the latest capability attempt's evidence path, and distinguish raw-only content without changing evidence presence flags.\\nCHANGELOG.md:62:- **paths**: align workflow, runtime, report, launcher, and test defaults on the\\nCHANGELOG.md:63:  `docs/dev/project-management` store tree.\\nCHANGELOG.md:64:- **runtime**: keep supervisor session collection within style limits while preserving timeout evidence and classification.\\nCHANGELOG.md:65:- **runtime**: honor supplied phase settings on every workflow launch while preserving agent overrides and literal prompts.\\nCHANGELOG.md:66:- **workflow**: include canonical phase metrics in reports when usage is missing or malformed while excluding capability attempts from workflow totals.\\nCHANGELOG.md:67:- **runtime**: share capability execution and failure evidence across pending runs and retries, honor bounded capability timeout precedence, and defer aggregate publication until completion.\\nCHANGELOG.md:68:- **runtime**: persist operator stops until resume and halt state failures behind sanitized durable attention or an emergency restart barrier, preserving existing attention notices.\\nCHANGELOG.md:69:- **runtime**: bound unchanged attempts across failure classes while preserving terminal halts, honor committed controls before capabilities and drain completion, and preserve phase-pause reasons on resume.\\nCHANGELOG.md:70:- **runtime**: initialize batch identity before sessions, preserve capability failure and retry attention, and archive completed batches using the supervisor clock.\\nCHANGELOG.md:71:\\nCHANGELOG.md:72:- **events**: normalized evidence redacts `x-api-key`, `apiKey`, and other separator or case variants of API-key names, and raw fallback previews redact before truncating so no secret prefix survives the cut.\\nCHANGELOG.md:73:- **events**: redaction stays linear on long unbroken text, and raw fallback previews read a bounded head of the frame, so one bad frame can no longer stall decoding or expose a secret cut at the frame limit.\\nCHANGELOG.md:74:- **events**: credential assignments behind sensitive key names longer than 64 characters are redacted again.\\nCHANGELOG.md:75:- **events**: raw fallback previews of a cut-off frame with no whitespace come out empty whenever an `sk-` token is in view, and short CRLF frames no longer carry the trailing CR.\\nCHANGELOG.md:76:- **drivers**: a dated limit banner whose date does not exist in its year (such as Feb 29 in a non-leap year) yields no reset instead of jumping to a later leap year.\\nCHANGELOG.md:77:- **drivers**: rate-limit warnings no longer clear a live limit, a rejected event's reset wins over the terminal banner, real clock-and-zone banners such as `resets 8:10pm (Europe/Prague)` yield a reset, and the limit window is structured payload data.\\nCHANGELOG.md:78:- **drivers**: dated limit banners such as `resets Sep 20 at 11am (Europe/Prague)` yield a multi-day reset, and a terminal banner reset now applies after a rejected event that carried no credible future reset.\\nCHANGELOG.md:79:- Agent configuration applies command defaults and shared validation; normalized text redacts bare credential tokens while preserving usage counters.\\nCHANGELOG.md:80:- Deferred directory setup diagnostics report the full configured path while preserving the originating OS error.\\nCHANGELOG.md:81:- Deferred publication revalidates the complete confirmed runtime ancestry before returning success.\\nCHANGELOG.md:82:- Deferred ancestry confirmation detects replaced ancestors on reopen, supports search-only access, and avoids redundant ancestor creation and root confirmation.\\nCHANGELOG.md:83:- Shared publication contention reports `publication busy; retry: <path>` for both reports and deferred ledgers.\\nCHANGELOG.md:84:- Deferred retries and replays confirm existing runtime ancestry after abrupt exits and preserve directories created by concurrent callers when confirmation fails.\\nCHANGELOG.md:85:- Deferred publication validates the complete prospective ledger and persists newly created runtime ancestors; overlapping report renders no longer lose successful sections.\\nCHANGELOG.md:86:- Report JSON returns the complete published batch text after PRD updates and exact rerenders.\\nCHANGELOG.md:87:- Deferred ledgers reject duplicate keys and excessive nesting; replaced sidecar locks refuse publication without losing competing appends.\\nCHANGELOG.md:88:- Park/stall recovery retains the original PRD's filesystem identity through restart and preserves unfinished work on substitution.\\nCHANGELOG.md:89:- Batch reports reconstruct all deferred details with PRD attribution; report, audit, and archive retries complete directory durability.\\nCHANGELOG.md:90:- Blank decision content is omitted consistently from counts and audits; named payload and configuration files reject nonregular inputs promptly.\\nCHANGELOG.md:91:- PRD moves atomically refuse concurrent held work; filesystem evidence remains checked through saga state publication.\\nCHANGELOG.md:92:- Recovery validates batch identity and operation inputs before creating lifecycle directories or durable intent.\\nCHANGELOG.md:93:- Installed workflow commands honor configured roots and active abstract tier keys, with explicit path and tier overrides.\\nCHANGELOG.md:94:- Metric inputs reject FIFO/nonregular files promptly; systemic park pauses return a distinct halt status and actionable output.\\nCHANGELOG.md:95:- Workflow orchestration, render sections, and installed/saga tests are split by responsibility while retaining failpoints and acceptance coverage.\\nCHANGELOG.md:96:\\nCHANGELOG.md:97:- Drained workflows remain terminal, and stall refuses conflicting recovery intents while park retains reconciliation behavior.\\nCHANGELOG.md:98:- Workflow reports preserve unknown legacy totals, order equal-key metric rows deterministically, and reject nonregular output targets without blocking.\\nCHANGELOG.md:99:- Deferred ledger publication and saga commit now verify the configured directory identity through durable writes and recovery.\\nCHANGELOG.md:100:- State validation now uses canonical persisted-byte sizing, precise nested diagnostics, and cached type metadata.\\nCHANGELOG.md:101:- CLI task payloads now reject non-object JSON, option abbreviations are disabled at every parser level, and resource limits use typed errors.\\nCHANGELOG.md:102:- State transactions now overwrite mutator-supplied revisions before validation and close lock descriptors on every setup failure.\\nCHANGELOG.md:103:- The installed state service now owns restore routing, and the protocol documents the complete schema, durability, and error contracts.\\nCHANGELOG.md:104:- Project initialization now preserves existing config metadata and remains retryable when config creation fails.\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:1:\\\"\\\"\\\"Immutable, sanitized version-one observations and session summaries.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:2:\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:3:import math\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:4:import re\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:5:from collections.abc import Mapping\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:6:from dataclasses import asdict, dataclass, fields\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:7:from datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:8:from enum import StrEnum\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:9:from types import MappingProxyType\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:10:\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:11:PROTOCOL_VERSION = 1\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:12:type JSONValue = (\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:13:    str\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:14:    | int\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:15:    | float\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:16:    | bool\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:17:    | None\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:18:    | list[\\\"JSONValue\\\"]\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:19:    | tuple[\\\"JSONValue\\\", ...]\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:20:    | Mapping[str, \\\"JSONValue\\\"]\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:21:)\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:22:_SENSITIVE = r\\\"token|secret|password|authorization|api[_-]?key|cookie|credential\\\"\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:23:_SENSITIVE_KEY = re.compile(_SENSITIVE, re.IGNORECASE)\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:24:# A key is a whole `[\\\\w-]` run, entered only at a run start, so each run is\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:25:# scanned a constant number of times: li