+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:32:18.472Z","ordinal":16,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a124ba-014b-7f22-85be-580a1695d453","turn_id":"01a124ba-01aa-7d90-b51d-a27099219213","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-73ae1483-ad69-4728-adb1-7397e5b73d90","process_id":"11625","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-2.txt"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-2.txt","name":"dispatch-tess-2.txt","path":"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-2.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"You are writing tests for a feature. You have NOT seen any implementation and must NOT think about how to implement it.\n\nTask: Reject unsafe native frames before adapter mutation\n\nDescription:\nWrite independent raw-first regression tests in /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py only. Do not change existing scalar tests. Requirement: any bounded native JSON frame with an invalid Unicode scalar anywhere (including ignored fields and nested keys) produces exactly one raw.unknown with reason frame contains invalid Unicode scalar value, sha256 of original frame without newline or one framing CR, sanitized preview capped 512; no semantic observations or actual adapter state mutation (_session_id, _usage, _thread_conflict, _identities). Cover startup, completion and collaboration records and invalid high/low scalars; exact durable raw bytes, session ownership binding, healthy later identity/usage/terminal completion, valid escaped pair, malformed/non-JSON unchanged delegation, and genuine writer exceptions propagating. Public types and signatures are supplied. Existing tests supplied as sample define actual Codex native record shapes. Only the listed test file may be changed; read only sample tests and supplied interfaces, never implementation.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n\n- Re-check R7 before edits; if already safely recovered without adapter mutation, skip production edits and report while retaining independent tests. `mise exec -- uv run pytest tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py tests/events/test_tail.py` passes; byte-exact raw, gap digest/preview, unchanged adapter identity/usage and later healthy terminal are asserted; existing genuine writer failures still raise.\n\nVerify: mise exec -- uv run pytest -q --tb=line tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py\n\nExisting test patterns (follow these conventions):\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport errno\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport os\nimport stat\nimport time\nimport tracemalloc\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterable\nfrom dataclasses import replace\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ovcaq.events import (\n    PROTOCOL_VERSION,\n    Observation,\n    ObservationType,\n    observation_from_record,\n    observation_record,\n)\nfrom ovcaq.events.tail import NormalizedEventWriter, RawFirstDecoder\nfrom ovcaq.runtime.session import EvidenceLimitError, SessionEvidenceWriter\n\n\ndef _observation(message: str) -> Observation:\n    return Observation(\n        protocol_version=1,\n        timestamp=datetime(2026, 1, 1, tzinfo=UTC),\n        provider=\"fake\",\n        run_id=\"run-1\",\n        session_id=None,\n        lane_id=None,\n        type=ObservationType.ACTIVITY_MESSAGE,\n        payload={\"message\": message},\n    )\n\n\ndef _read_observations(path: Path) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\n    return tuple(\n        observation_from_record(json.loads(line))\n        for line in path.read_bytes().splitlines()\n    )\n\n\ndef _assert_unknown_evidence(\n    observation: Observation, frame: bytes, ordinary: str\n) -> None:\n    assert observation.type == ObservationType.RAW_UNKNOWN\n    assert observation.payload[\"raw_sha256\"] == hashlib.sha256(frame).hexdigest()\n    reason = observation.payload[\"reason\"]\n    assert isinstance(reason, str) and reason.strip()\n    preview = observation.payload[\"preview\"]\n    assert isinstance(preview, str)\n    assert ordinary in preview\n\n\nclass RecordingDriver:\n    name = \"fake\"\n\n    def __init__(self, before_decode: Callable[[], None] | None = None) -> None:\n        self.lines: list[str] = []\n        self.before_decode = before_decode\n\n    def decode(self, raw_line: str) -> Iterable[Observation]:\n        if self.before_decode is not None:\n            self.before_decode()\n        self.lines.append(raw_line)\n        return (_observation(raw_line), _observation(\"second observation\"))\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef evidence(tmp_path: Path):\n    raw = SessionEvidenceWriter(\n        tmp_path / \"raw.jsonl\", max_bytes=4 << 20, min_free_bytes=0\n    )\n    normalized = NormalizedEventWriter(\n        tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\", max_bytes=4 << 20, min_free_bytes=0\n    )\n    try:\n        yield raw, normalized\n    finally:\n        normalized.close()\n        raw.close()\n\n\ndef test_normalized_lines_are_private_sanitized_and_round_trip(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    previous_umask = os.umask(0)\n    try:\n        writer = NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=4096, min_free_bytes=0)\n    finally:\n        os.umask(previous_umask)\n    observations = (_observation(\"token=hidden-value\\nhello é\"), _observation(\"next\"))\n    try:\n        assert stat.S_ISREG(path.stat().st_mode)\n        assert stat.S_IMODE(path.stat().st_mode) == 0o600\n        previous_size = 0\n        for observation in observations:\n            accepted = writer.write(observation)\n            content = path.read_bytes()\n            assert accepted == len(content) - previous_size\n            assert content.endswith(b\"\\n\")\n            assert b\"hidden-value\" not in content\n            previous_size = len(content)\n        lines = path.read_bytes().splitlines()\n        assert len(lines) == len(observations)\n        assert [json.loads(line) for line in lines] == [\n            observation_record(observation) for observation in observations\n        ]\n        assert _read_observations(path) == observations\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"obstacle\", [\"file\", \"symlink\", \"dangling\", \"directory\", \"fifo\"]\n)\ndef test_normalized_creation_preserves_existing_paths(\n    tmp_path: Path, obstacle: str\n) -> None:\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    target = tmp_path / \"target\"\n    target.write_bytes(b\"preserve\")\n    if obstacle == \"file\":\n        path.write_bytes(b\"prior evidence\")\n    elif obstacle == \"symlink\":\n        path.symlink_to(target)\n    elif obstacle == \"dangling\":\n        path.symlink_to(tmp_path / \"missing\")\n    elif obstacle == \"directory\":\n        path.mkdir()\n    else:\n        os.mkfifo(path)\n    before = path.lstat()\n    with pytest.raises(OSError):\n        NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=4096, min_free_bytes=0)\n    assert os.path.samestat(before, path.lstat())\n    assert target.read_bytes() == b\"preserve\"\n    assert not (tmp_path / \"missing\").exists()\n    if obstacle == \"file\":\n        assert path.read_bytes() == b\"prior evidence\"\n\n\ndef test_normalized_ceiling_rejects_whole_record_without_damaging_prior_line(\n    tmp_path: Path,\n) -> None:\n    observation = _observation(\"bounded\")\n    reference = tmp_path / \"reference.jsonl\"\n    writer = NormalizedEventWriter(reference, max_bytes=4096, min_free_bytes=0)\n    try:\n        length = writer.write(observation)\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    writer = NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=length, min_free_bytes=0)\n    try:\n        assert writer.write(observation) == length\n        with pytest.raises(EvidenceLimitError):\n            writer.write(observation)\n        assert path.read_bytes() == reference.read_bytes()\n        assert _read_observations(path) == (observation,)\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"obstacle\", [\"symlink\", \"world-writable\"])\ndef test_normalized_writer_rejects_unsafe_parent(tmp_path: Path, obstacle: str) -> None:\n    target = tmp_path / \"target\"\n    target.mkdir(mode=0o700)\n    parent = tmp_path / \"session\"\n    if obstacle == \"symlink\":\n        parent.symlink_to(target, target_is_directory=True)\n    else:\n        parent.mkdir(mode=0o700)\n        parent.chmod(0o777)\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        NormalizedEventWriter(\n            parent / \"normalized.jsonl\", max_bytes=4096, min_free_bytes=0\n        )\n    assert not (parent / \"normalized.jsonl\").exists()\n    assert list(target.iterdir()) == []\n\n\ndef test_normalized_records_respect_space_floor_and_finish_partial_writes(\n    tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch\n) -> None:\n    available = 10000\n\n    def filesystem_space(_location: object) -> os.statvfs_result:\n        return os.statvfs_result((1, 1, 10000, 10000, available, 1, 1, 1, 0, 255))\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(os, \"statvfs\", filesystem_space)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(os, \"fstatvfs\", filesystem_space)\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    writer = NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=4096, min_free_bytes=128)\n    real_write = os.write\n    calls = 0\n\n    def partial_write(descriptor: int, payload: bytes) -> int:\n        nonlocal calls\n        calls += 1\n        if calls % 3 == 1:\n            raise InterruptedError(errno.EINTR, \"interrupted\")\n        return real_write(descriptor, payload[:17])\n\n    observation = _observation(\"partial é\")\n    try:\n        with monkeypatch.context() as patch:\n            patch.setattr(os, \"write\", partial_write)\n            length = writer.write(observation)\n        assert length == len(path.read_bytes())\n        available = 128 + length - 1\n        with pytest.raises(EvidenceLimitError):\n            writer.write(observation)\n        assert _read_observations(path) == (observation,)\n        available = 128 + length\n        assert writer.write(observation) == length\n        assert _read_observations(path) == (observation, observation)\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n\n\ndef test_normalized_write_failure_preserves_prior_line_and_partial_new_bytes(\n    tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch\n) -> None:\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    writer = NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=4096, min_free_bytes=0)\n    observation = _observation(\"partial failure\")\n    real_write = os.write\n    accepted = False\n\n    def failing_write(descriptor: int, payload: bytes) -> int:\n        nonlocal accepted\n        if not accepted:\n            accepted = True\n            return real_write(descriptor, payload[:7])\n        raise OSError(errno.ENOSPC, \"injected disk full\")\n\n    try:\n        writer.write(observation)\n        previous = path.read_bytes()\n        with monkeypatch.context() as patch:\n            patch.setattr(os, \"write\", failing_write)\n            with pytest.raises(OSError):\n                writer.write(observation)\n        assert path.read_bytes() == previous + previous[:7]\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n    assert path.read_bytes() == previous + previous[:7]\n\n\ndef test_normalized_close_syncs_and_closes_once(\n    tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch\n) -> None:\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    writer = NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=4096, min_free_bytes=0)\n    observation = _observation(\"durable\")\n    writer.write(observation)\n    information = path.stat()\n    real_fsync, real_close = os.fsync, os.close\n    events: list[str] = []\n\n    def sync(descriptor: int) -> None:\n        is_evidence = os.path.samestat(information, os.fstat(descriptor))\n        real_fsync(descriptor)\n        if is_evidence:\n            events.append(\"sync\")\n\n    def close(descriptor: int) -> None:\n        is_evidence = os.path.samestat(information, os.fstat(descriptor))\n        real_close(descriptor)\n        if is_evidence:\n            events.append(\"close\")\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(os, \"fsync\", sync)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(os, \"close\", close)\n    try:\n        writer.close()\n        writer.close()\n        assert events == [\"sync\", \"close\"]\n        with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n            writer.write(observation)\n        assert _read_observations(path) == (observation,)\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"chunk_size\", [1, 3, 4096])\ndef test_frames_decode_only_after_exact_raw_bytes_are_synced(\n    tmp_path: Path, evidence, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, chunk_size: int\n) -> None:\n    raw, normalized = evidence\n    path = tmp_path / \"raw.jsonl\"\n    information = path.stat()\n    real_fsync = os.fsync\n    durable = b\"\"\n    expected = b\"\"\n\n    def sync(descriptor: int) -> None:\n        nonlocal durable\n        real_fsync(descriptor)\n        if os.path.samestat(information, os.fstat(descriptor)):\n            durable = path.read_bytes()\n\n    def before_decode() -> None:\n        assert path.read_bytes() == expected\n        assert durable == expected\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(os, \"fsync\", sync)\n    driver = RecordingDriver(before_decode)\n    decoder = RawFirstDecoder(\n        raw=raw, normalized=normalized, driver=driver, run_id=\"run-1\"\n    )\n    payload = b\"first\\r\\n\\n\\xc3\\xa9\\nlast\"\n    emitted: tuple[Observation, ...] = ()\n    assert decoder.feed(b\"\") == ()\n    for offset in range(0, len(payload), chunk_size):\n        chunk = payload[offset : offset + chunk_size]\n        expected += chunk\n        emitted += decoder.feed(chunk)\n        assert path.read_bytes() == expected\n        assert _read_observations(tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\") == emitted\n    assert driver.lines == [\"first\", \"\", \"é\"]\n    emitted += decoder.finish()\n    assert import hashlib\nimport json\nfrom collections.abc import Iterable, Iterator\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ovcaq.config import AgentSettings\nfrom ovcaq.drivers.codex import CodexDriver\nfrom ovcaq.drivers.codex_events import classify_failure\nfrom ovcaq.events.model import FailureClass, Observation\nfrom ovcaq.events.reducer import reduce_session, session_failure_observation\n\nFIXTURES = Path(__file__).parents[1] / \"fixtures\" / \"codex\" / \"v1\"\nFAKE_CREDENTIAL = \"sk-\" + \"SyntheticCredentialForDecoderTestOnly123456789012\"\nNOW = datetime.now(UTC)\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef driver() -> CodexDriver:\n    settings = AgentSettings(\n        name=\"codex\",\n        command=(\"fixture-wrapper\",),\n        tiers={\"standard\": \"fixture-model\"},\n        environment={},\n        options={},\n    )\n    return CodexDriver(settings, run_id=\"terminal-run\")\n\n\ndef decode(driver: CodexDriver, record: dict[str, object]) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\n    return driver.decode(json.dumps(record))\n\n\ndef supplied(kind: str, payload: dict[str, object]) -> Observation:\n    return Observation(\n        protocol_version=1,\n        timestamp=NOW,\n        provider=\"codex\",\n        run_id=\"supplied-run\",\n        session_id=\"supplied-thread\",\n        lane_id=None,\n        type=kind,\n        payload=payload,\n    )\n\n\nclass SingleUse:\n    def __init__(self, observations: Iterable[Observation]) -> None:\n        self.observations = tuple(observations)\n        self.iterations = 0\n\n    def __iter__(self) -> Iterator[Observation]:\n        self.iterations += 1\n        assert self.iterations == 1, \"summarize consumed its iterable more than once\"\n        yield from self.observations\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    (\"detail\", \"failure_class\"),\n    [\n        (\"Unauthorized: HTTP 401\", \"authentication\"),\n        (\"Sandbox denied: HTTP 403\", \"permission\"),\n        (\"Quota limit reached: HTTP 429\", \"rate_limit\"),\n        (\"Connection reset: HTTP 503\", \"connectivity\"),\n        (\"Request timed out\", \"timeout\"),\n        (\"Unexpected diagnostic\", \"unknown\"),\n    ],\n)\ndef test_native_failure_emits_classified_terminal_with_receipt_identity(\n    driver: CodexDriver, detail: str, failure_class: str\n) -> None:\n    decode(driver, {\"type\": \"thread.started\", \"thread_id\": \"failure-thread\"})\n    before = datetime.now(UTC)\n    observations = decode(driver, {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": detail}})\n    after = datetime.now(UTC)\n    expected = [\"session.failed\"]\n    if failure_class == \"rate_limit\":\n        expected.append(\"rate_limit.started\")\n    assert sorted(o.type for o in observations) == sorted(expected)\n    terminal = next(o for o in observations if o.type == \"session.failed\")\n    assert dict(terminal.payload) == {\"failure_class\": failure_class, \"detail\": detail}\n    for observation in observations:\n        assert observation.protocol_version == 1\n        assert observation.provider == \"codex\"\n        assert observation.run_id == \"terminal-run\"\n        assert observation.session_id == \"failure-thread\"\n        assert observation.timestamp.utcoffset() == timedelta(0)\n        assert before <= observation.timestamp <= after\n    summary = driver.summarize(observations, 1)\n    assert summary == reduce_session(observations, 1).summary\n    assert not summary.success\n    assert summary.failure_class == FailureClass(failure_class)\n    assert summary.failure_detail == detail\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"fixture\",\n    [\n        \"rate-limited\",\n        \"authentication-failed\",\n        \"connectivity-failed\",\n        \"permission-failed\",\n    ],\n)\ndef test_fixture_error_then_identical_failure_has_one_terminal_and_rate_start(\n    driver: CodexDriver, fixture: str\n) -> None:\n    records = (FIXTURES / f\"{fixture}.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines()\n    observations = tuple(o for line in records for o in driver.decode(line))\n    failures = [o for o in observations if o.type == \"session.failed\"]\n    provisional = [\n        o\n        for o in observations\n        if o.payload.get(\"kind\") == \"error\" and \"failure_class\" in o.payload\n    ]\n    assert len(failures) == len(provisional) == 1\n    detail = json.loads(records[-1])[\"error\"][\"message\"]\n    classification = classify_failure(detail)\n    assert failures[0].payload[\"failure_class\"] == classification.value\n    assert provisional[0].payload[\"failure_class\"] == classification.value\n    assert provisional[0].type == \"activity.message\"\n    rates = [o for o in observations if o.type == \"rate_limit.started\"]\n    assert len(rates) == int(classification == FailureClass(\"rate_limit\"))\n    for rate in rates:\n        assert dict(rate.payload) == {\n            \"reset_at\": None,\n            \"window\": None,\n            \"detail\": detail,\n        }\n    stream = SingleUse(observations)\n    assert driver.summarize(stream, 1) == reduce_session(observations, 1).summary\n    assert stream.iterations == 1\n\n\ndef test_top_level_error_is_sanitized_provisional_activity(driver: CodexDriver) -> None:\n    detail = f\"Unauthorized {FAKE_CREDENTIAL}\\x1b[31m\"\n    observations = decode(driver, {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": detail})\n    assert len(observations) == 1\n    activity = observations[0]\n    assert activity.type == \"activity.message\"\n    assert activity.payload[\"kind\"] == \"error\"\n    assert activity.payload[\"failure_class\"] == \"authentication\"\n    assert activity.payload[\"reset_at\"] is None\n    assert activity.payload[\"detail\"] == \"Unauthorized [REDACTED]\"\n    assert FAKE_CREDENTIAL not in activity.payload[\"detail\"]\n    assert \"[REDACTED]\" in activity.payload[\"detail\"]\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"reset\", [\"retry after 30 seconds\", \"retry after 21600 seconds\"]\n)\ndef test_native_rate_failure_preserves_explicit_bounded_reset(\n    driver: CodexDriver, reset: str\n) -> None:\n    detail = f\"Rate limit reached; {reset}\"\n    observations = decode(driver, {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": detail}})\n    failure = next(o for o in observations if o.type == \"session.failed\")\n    rate = next(o for o in observations if o.type == \"rate_limit.started\")\n    seconds = int(reset.split()[2])\n    expected = rate.timestamp + timedelta(seconds=seconds)\n    actual = datetime.fromisoformat(rate.payload[\"reset_at\"])\n    assert actual.utcoffset() == timedelta(0)\n    assert abs((actual - expected).total_seconds()) < 1\n    assert dict(failure.payload) == {\"failure_class\": \"rate_limit\", \"detail\": detail}\n    assert rate.payload[\"window\"] is None\n    assert rate.payload[\"detail\"] == detail\n    assert driver.summarize(observations, 1).rate_limit_reset_at == actual\n\n\ndef test_provisional_rate_error_preserves_explicit_utc_reset_without_terminal(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n) -> None:\n    reset = datetime.now(UTC) + timedelta(seconds=120)\n    detail = f\"Rate limit reached; reset at {reset.isoformat()}\"\n    observations = decode(driver, {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": detail})\n    assert len(observations) == 1\n    activity = observations[0]\n    assert activity.type == \"activity.message\"\n    assert activity.payload[\"kind\"] == \"error\"\n    assert activity.payload[\"failure_class\"] == \"rate_limit\"\n    assert activity.payload[\"detail\"] == detail\n    assert datetime.fromisoformat(activity.payload[\"reset_at\"]) == reset\n    summary = driver.summarize(SingleUse(observations), 1)\n    assert summary.failure_class == FailureClass(\"rate_limit\")\n    assert summary.rate_limit_reset_at == reset\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"reset\",\n    [\n        \"try again in 60 seconds\",\n        \"retry after -1 seconds\",\n        \"retry after 21601 seconds\",\n        \"retry after nan seconds\",\n        \"retry after 1e999 seconds\",\n        \"reset at 2020-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n        \"reset at 2099-01-01T00:00:00\",\n        \"reset at 3:00 PM\",\n        \"\",\n    ],\n)\ndef test_native_rate_failure_keeps_missing_or_invalid_reset_unknown(\n    driver: CodexDriver, reset: str\n) -> None:\n    detail = f\"Rate limit reached; {reset}\"\n    observations = decode(driver, {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": detail}})\n    rate = next(o for o in observations if o.type == \"rate_limit.started\")\n    assert dict(rate.payload) == {\"reset_at\": None, \"window\": None, \"detail\": detail}\n    assert driver.summarize(observations, 1).rate_limit_reset_at is None\n\n\ndef test_recovered_provisional_error_has_no_failure_or_rate_observations(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n) -> None:\n    lines = (FIXTURES / \"healthy.jsonl\").read_text().splitlines()\n    observations = tuple(o for line in lines for o in driver.decode(line))\n    assert not any(\n        o.type in {\"session.failed\", \"rate_limit.started\"} for o in observations\n    )\n    assert any(o.payload.get(\"kind\") == \"error\" for o in observations)\n    stream = SingleUse(observations)\n    summary = driver.summarize(stream, 0)\n    assert summary == reduce_session(observations, 0).summary\n    assert summary.success\n    assert summary.failure_class is None\n    assert summary.failure_detail is None\n    assert stream.iterations == 1\n\n\ndef test_nonfatal_item_error_never_supplies_provisional_failure_metadata(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n) -> None:\n    observations = decode(\n        driver,\n        {\n            \"type\": \"item.completed\",\n            \"item\": {\n                \"id\": \"warning-429\",\n                \"type\": \"error\",\n                \"message\": \"Rate limit reached\",\n            },\n        },\n    )\n    assert observations\n    assert all(o.type == \"activity.message\" for o in observations)\n    for observation in observations:\n        assert \"failure_class\" not in observation.payload\n        assert \"reset_at\" not in observation.payload\n    assert driver.summarize(observations, 0) == reduce_session(observations, 0).summary\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"failure_class\", [value.value for value in FailureClass])\ndef test_supplied_provisional_metadata_is_authoritative_without_prior_decode(\n    driver: CodexDriver, failure_class: str\n) -> None:\n    reset = NOW + timedelta(seconds=90) if failure_class == \"rate_limit\" else None\n    activity = supplied(\n        \"activity.message\",\n        {\n            \"kind\": \"error\",\n            \"detail\": \"Opaque normalized diagnostic\",\n            \"failure_class\": failure_class,\n            \"reset_at\": reset.isoformat() if reset else None,\n        },\n    )\n    stream = SingleUse([activity])\n    summary = driver.summarize(stream, 0)\n    assert not summary.success\n    assert summary.session_id == \"supplied-thread\"\n    assert summary.failure_class == FailureClass(failure_class)\n    assert summary.failure_detail == \"Opaque normalized diagnostic\"\n    assert summary.rate_limit_reset_at == reset\n    assert stream.iterations == 1\n    assert activity.payload[\"kind\"] == \"error\"\n\n\ndef test_latest_provisional_error_supersedes_earlier_normalized_metadata(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n) -> None:\n    first = supplied(\n        \"activity.message\",\n        {\n            \"kind\": \"error\",\n            \"detail\": \"First\",\n            \"failure_class\": \"rate_limit\",\n            \"reset_at\": (NOW + timedelta(seconds=30)).isoformat(),\n        },\n    )\n    last = supplied(\n        \"activity.message\",\n        {\n            \"kind\": \"error\",\n            \"detail\": \"Last\",\n            \"failure_class\": \"authentication\",\n            \"reset_at\": None,\n        },\n    )\n    summary = driver.summarize(SingleUse([first, last]), 1)\n    assert not summary.success\n    assert summary.failure_class == FailureClass(\"authentication\")\n    assert summary.failure_detail == \"Last\"\n    assert summary.rate_limit_reset_at is None\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"exit_code\", [0, 1])\ndef test_empty_or_nonprovisional_input_preserves_shared_reducer_result(\n    driver: CodexDriver, exit_code: int\n) -> None:\n    for observations in [\n        [],\n        [\n            supplied(\n                \"activity.message\",\n                {\"kind\": \"message\", \"detail\": \"Quoted example: HTTP 429; rate limit\"},\n            )\n        ],\n    ]:\n        stream = SingleUse(observations)\n        summary = driver.summarize(stream, exit_code)\n        assert summary == reduce_session(observations, exit_code).summary\n        assert not summary.success\n        assert stream.iterations == 1\n\n\ndef test_reused_driver_never_applies_stale_provisional_error(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n) -> None:\n    old = decode(driver, {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": \"Unauthorized\"})\n    assert driver.summarize(old, 1).failure_class == FailureClass(\"authentication\")\n    fresh = [supplied(\"activity.message\", {\"kind\": \"message\", \"detail\": \"Fresh input\"})]\n    assert driver.summarize(SingleUse(fresh), 0) == reduce_session(fresh, 0).summary\n    assert driver.summarize(SingleUse([]), 1) == reduce_session([], 1).summary\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"runtime_class\", [FailureClass(\"timeout\"), FailureClass(\"agent\")]\n)\ndef test_runtime_terminal_preserves_reducer_precedence_over_provisional_error(\n    driver: CodexDriver, runtime_class: FailureClass\n) -> None:\n    provisional = supplied(\n        \"activity.message\",\n        {\n            \"kind\": \"error\",\n            \"detail\": \"Quota limit\",\n            \"failure_class\": \"rate_limit\",\n            \"reset_at\": (NOW + timedelta(seconds=90)).isoformat(),\n        },\n    )\n    runtime = session_failure_observation(\n        timestamp=NOW,\n        provider=\"runtime\",\n        run_id=\"supplied-run\",\n        session_id=\"supplied-thread\",\n        failure_class=runtime_class,\n        detail=\"Runtime terminal\",\n    )\n    observations = [provisional, runtime]\n    assert (\n        driver.summarize(SingleUse(observations), 1)\n        == reduce_session(observations, 1).summary\n    )\n\n\ndef test_multiple_turn_terminals_preserve_shared_reducer_result(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n) -> None:\n    decode(driver, {\"type\": \"thread.started\", \"thread_id\": \"multi-turn\"})\n    first = decode(\n        driver, {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": \"Unauthorized\"}}\n    )\n    second = decode(\n        driver,\n        {\n            \"type\": \"turn.completed\",\n            \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 3, \"cached_input_tokens\": 0, \"output_tokens\": 2},\n        },\n    )\n    observations = [*first, *second]\n    assert (\n        driver.summarize(SingleUse(observations), 0)\n        == reduce_session(observations, 0).summary\n    )\n\n\ndef test_conflicting_terminal_identities_preserve_shared_reducer_result(\n    driver: CodexDriver,\n) -> None:\n    first = supplied(\n        \"session.failed\", {\"failure_class\": \"permission\", \"detail\": \"Denied\"}\n    )\n    second = Observation(\n        protocol_version=1,\n        timestamp=NOW,\n        provider=\"codex\",\n        run_id=\"supplied-run\",\n        session_id=\"other-thread\",\n        lane_id=None,\n        type=\"session.failed\",\n        payload={\"failure_class\": \"authentication\", \"detail\": \"Login\"},\n    )\n    observations = [first, second]\n    expected = reduce_session(observations, 1).summary\n    assert driver.summarize(SingleUse(observations), 1) == expected\n    assert expected.failure_class == FailureClass(\"unknown\")\n    assert expected.failure_detail is None\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\n    \"record\",\n    [\n        {\"type\": \"turn.failed\"},\n        {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": None},\n        {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": []},\n        {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": 429}},\n        {\"type\": \"error\"},\n        {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": None},\n        {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": [\"Unauthorized\"]},\n    ],\n)\ndef test_malformed_failure_records_degrade_to_hashed_raw_without_state_changes(\n    driver: CodexDriver, record: dict[str, object]\n) -> None:\n    decode(driver, {\"type\": \"thread.started\", \"thread_id\": \"valid-thread\"})\n    raw_line = json.dumps(record)\n    observations = driver.decode(raw_line)\n    assert observations\n    assert all(o.type == \"raw.unknown\" for o in observations)\n    for observation in observations:\n        assert set(observation.payload) == {\"reason\", \"raw_sha256\", \"preview\"}\n        assert (\n            observation.payload[\"raw_sha256\"]\n            == hashlib.sha256(raw_line.encode()).hexdigest()\n        )\n        assert isinstance(observation.payload[\"reason\"], str)\n        assert observation.payload[\"reason\"]\n        assert len(observation.payload[\"preview\"]) <= 512\n        assert observation.session_id == \"valid-thread\"\n    terminal = decode(\n        driver, {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": \"Unauthorized\"}}\n    )\n    assert (\n        next(o for o in terminal if o.type == \"session.failed\").session_id\n        == \"valid-thread\"\n    )\n\n\nPublic interfaces/types relevant to this task:\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py\nclass NormalizedEventWriter:\n    def __init__(self, path: Path, *, max_bytes: int, min_free_bytes: int) -> None: ...\n    def write(self, observation: Observation) -> int: ...\n    def flush(self) -> None: ...\n    def close(self) -> None: ...\nclass RawFirstDecoder:\n    def __init__(self, *, raw: SessionEvidenceWriter, normalized: NormalizedEventWriter, driver: AgentDriver, run_id: str, session_id: str | None=None, max_frame_bytes: int=1024 * 1024) -> None: ...\n    def feed(self, chunk: bytes) -> tuple[Observat