n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:9:Pick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:10:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:11:## Idioms that earn their place\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:12:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:13:| Rule | Why |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:14:|------|-----|\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:15:| `X \\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:16:| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:17:| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:18:| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\"During handling...\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:19:| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:20:| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:21:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:22:## Naming (PEP 8)\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:23:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:24:`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:25:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:26:**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:27:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:28:## Traps\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:29:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:30:```python\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:31:# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:32:def bad(items=[]): ...\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:33:def good(items=None):\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:34:    items = [] if items is None else items\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:35:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:36:# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:37:try: ...\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:38:except Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:39:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:40:# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:41:# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:42:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:43:# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:44:# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:45:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:46:if value is None: ...             # never == None\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:47:```\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:48:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:49:Avoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:50:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:51:## Toolchain\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:52:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:53:**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \"obvious\" returns.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:54:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:55:## Resources and laziness\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:56:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:57:Context managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:58:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:59:## Security\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:60:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:61:- Read secrets with `os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:62:- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:63:- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:1:\"\"\"Provider-neutral driver records, protocol, and plugin discovery.\"\"\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:2:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:3:from collections.abc import Callable, Iterable, Mapping\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:4:from dataclasses import dataclass\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:5:from importlib import metadata\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:6:from pathlib import Path\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:7:from types import MappingProxyType\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:8:from typing import Protocol\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:9:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:10:from ovcaq.events import Observation, SessionSummary\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:11:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:12:DRIVER_API_VERSION = 2\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:13:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:14:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:15:def _require_string(value: object, field: str) -> None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:16:    if not isinstance(value, str):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:17:        raise TypeError(f\"{field} must be a string\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:18:    if not value:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:19:        raise ValueError(f\"{field} must not be empty\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:20:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:21:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:22:@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:23:class LaunchRequest:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:24:    root: Path\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:25:    phase: str\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:26:    prompt: str\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:27:    model: str | None\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:28:    effort: str | None\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:29:    timeout_seconds: int\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:30:    session_dir: Path\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:31:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:32:    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:33:        for field in (\"root\", \"session_dir\"):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:34:            if not isinstance(getattr(self, field), Path):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:35:                raise TypeError(f\"{field} must be a Path\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:36:        for field in (\"phase\", \"prompt\"):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:37:            _require_string(getattr(self, field), field)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:38:        for field in (\"model\", \"effort\"):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:39:            value = getattr(self, field)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:40:            if value is not None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:41:                _require_string(value, field)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:42:        if type(self.timeout_seconds) is not int:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:43:            raise TypeError(\"timeout_seconds must be an integer\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:44:        if self.timeout_seconds <= 0:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:45:            raise ValueError(\"timeout_seconds must be positive\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:46:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:47:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:48:@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:49:class LaunchSpec:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:50:    argv: tuple[str, ...]\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:51:    env: Mapping[str, str]\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:52:    cwd: Path\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:53:    raw_format: str\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:54:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:55:    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:56:        if not isinstance(self.argv, tuple):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:57:            raise TypeError(\"argv must be a tuple\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:58:        if not self.argv:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:59:            raise ValueError(\"argv must not be empty\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:60:        for argument in self.argv:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:61:            _require_string(argument, \"argv argument\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:62:        if not isinstance(self.env, Mapping):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:63:            raise TypeError(\"env must be a mapping\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:64:        for key, value in self.env.items():\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:65:            _require_string(key, \"env key\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:66:            _require_string(value, \"env value\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:67:        object.__setattr__(self, \"env\", MappingProxyType(dict(self.env)))\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:68:        if not isinstance(self.cwd, Path):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:69:            raise TypeError(\"cwd must be a Path\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:70:        _require_string(self.raw_format, \"raw_format\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:71:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:72:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:73:@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:74:class DriverHealth:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:75:    healthy: bool\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:76:    detail: str\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:77:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:78:    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:79:        if type(self.healthy) is not bool:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:80:            raise TypeError(\"healthy must be a boolean\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:81:        if not isinstance(self.detail, str):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:82:            raise TypeError(\"detail must be a string\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:83:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:84:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:85:class AgentDriver(Protocol):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:86:    name: str\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:87:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:88:    def default_prompt(self, phase: str) -> str: ...\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:89:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:90:    def probe(self) -> DriverHealth: ...\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:91:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:92:    def build_launch(self, request: LaunchRequest) -> LaunchSpec: ...\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:93:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:94:    def decode(self, raw_line: str) -> Iterable[Observation]: ...\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:95:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:96:    def summarize(\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:97:        self, observations: Iterable[Observation], exit_code: int\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:98:    ) -> SessionSummary: ...\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:99:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:100:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:101:DriverFactory = Callable[[], AgentDriver]\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:102:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:103:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:104:@dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:105:class DriverPlugin:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:106:    api_version: int\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:107:    factory: DriverFactory\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:108:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:109:    def __post_init__(self) -> None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:110:        if type(self.api_version) is not int:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:111:            raise TypeError(\"api_version must be an integer\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:112:        if not callable(self.factory):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:113:            raise TypeError(\"factory must be callable\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:114:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:115:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:116:class DriverDiscoveryError(RuntimeError):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:117:    \"\"\"A driver could not be loaded, constructed, or verified.\"\"\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:118:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:119:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:120:class IncompatibleDriverError(DriverDiscoveryError):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:121:    \"\"\"A plugin declares an unsupported driver API version.\"\"\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:122:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:123:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:124:class DuplicateDriverError(DriverDiscoveryError):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:125:    \"\"\"More than one plugin declares the same driver name.\"\"\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:126:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:127:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:128:def _register_driver(\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:129:    discovered: dict[str, AgentDriver],\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:130:    candidate: object,\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:131:    source: str,\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:132:    advertised_name: str | None = None,\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:133:) -> None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:134:    if not isinstance(candidate, DriverPlugin):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:135:        raise DriverDiscoveryError(f\"{source} must provide a DriverPlugin\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:136:    if candidate.api_version != DRIVER_API_VERSION:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:137:        raise IncompatibleDriverError(\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:138:            f\"{source} uses driver API {candidate.api_version}; \"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:139:            f\"expected {DRIVER_API_VERSION}\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:140:        )\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:141:    try:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:142:        driver = candidate.factory()\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:143:    except Exception as exc:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:144:        raise DriverDiscoveryError(f\"{source} factory failed: {exc}\") from exc\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:145:    name = driver.name\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:146:    if not isinstance(name, str) or not name:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:147:        raise DriverDiscoveryError(f\"{source} has an invalid driver name: {name!r}\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:148:    if advertised_name is not None and name != advertised_name:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:149:        raise DriverDiscoveryError(\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:150:            f\"{source} advertises {advertised_name!r} but returned {name!r}\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:151:        )\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:152:    if name in discovered:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:153:        raise DuplicateDriverError(f\"Duplicate driver name: {name!r} ({source})\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:154:    try:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:155:        health = driver.probe()\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:156:    except Exception as exc:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:157:        raise DriverDiscoveryError(\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:158:            f\"Driver {name!r} from {source} probe failed: {exc}\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:159:        ) from exc\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:160:    if not health.healthy:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:161:        raise DriverDiscoveryError(\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:162:            f\"Driver {name!r} from {source} is unhealthy: {health.detail}\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:163:        )\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:164:    discovered[name] = driver\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:165:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:166:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:167:def discover_drivers(\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:168:    builtins: Iterable[DriverPlugin],\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:169:    *,\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:170:    entry_points: Iterable[metadata.EntryPoint] | None = None,\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:171:) -> Mapping[str, AgentDriver]:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:172:    \"\"\"Construct and probe each plugin, returning an immutable ordered registry.\"\"\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:173:    discovered: dict[str, AgentDriver] = {}\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:174:    for index, candidate in enumerate(builtins):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:175:        _register_driver(discovered, candidate, f\"builtin {index}\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:176:    if entry_points is None:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:177:        entry_points = metadata.entry_points(group=\"ovcaq.drivers\")\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:178:    for entry_point in sorted(entry_points, key=lambda entry: entry.name):\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:179:        source = f\"entry point {entry_point.name!r}\"\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:180:        try:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:181:            loaded = entry_point.load()\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:182:        except Exception as exc:\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:183:            raise DriverDiscoveryError(f\"Could not load {source}: {exc}\") from exc\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:184:        _register_driver(discovered, loaded, source, entry_point.name)\nsrc/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:185:    return MappingProxyType(discovered)\nCHANGELOG.md:1:# Changelog\nCHANGELOG.md:2:\nCHANGELOG.md:3:All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\nCHANGELOG.md:4:\nCHANGELOG.md:5:The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).\nCHANGELOG.md:6:\nCHANGELOG.md:7:## [Unreleased]\nCHANGELOG.md:8:\nCHANGELOG.md:9:### Added\nCHANGELOG.md:10:\nCHANGELOG.md:11:- **drivers**: run supervised workflows with Codex, configured models and effort, verified version/authentication checks, and state-based phase handoffs.\nCHANGELOG.md:12:- **drivers**: show Codex activity, tools, receiver lanes and cache-aware usage with retained raw evidence; conflicting native threads fail safely even after supervisor ownership binding.\nCHANGELOG.md:13:- **tui**: add `ovcaq attach`, TTY-default attachment for `ovcaq run`, detachable interactive controls with plain fallback, and interactive `resume` that attaches to a live supervisor or launches once after a boundary pause.\nCHANGELOG.md:14:- **runtime**: run batch capabilities as durable provider-neutral attempts with private session evidence, final metrics, stale-owner reconciliation, and explicit one-attempt retry of failed capabilities.\nCHANGELOG.md:15:- **state**: add guarded compound supervisor mutations for pause/resume, progress fingerprints, capability attempts, failure attention, and empty-drain completion.\nCHANGELOG.md:16:- **runtime**: publish one immutable canonical metric row per phase or capability session, reconcile interrupted evidence deterministically, and project versioned metrics through legacy-compatible reports.\nCHANGELOG.md:17:- **config**: resolve provider-neutral build, review, and done routes with validated effort, timeout, model-tier, retry-policy, and literal prompt configuration; drivers now expose the version-two default-prompt contract.\nCHANGELOG.md:18:- **config**: load immutable per-agent argv, tier, environment, and JSON option settings with user/project merging and credential-shaped value rejection.\nCHANGELOG.md:19:- **drivers**: define the immutable provider-neutral launch, health, plugin, and discovery contracts with exact-version, duplicate-name, and fail-closed probe validation.\nCHANGELOG.md:20:- **drivers**: add the shell-free Claude launch adapter with explicit unattended permissions, configured tier and fallback resolution, isolated environment construction, executable health checks, and neutral summary reduction.\nCHANGELOG.md:21:- **drivers**: normalize Claude init, activity, tool, lane, usage, rate-limit, and terminal stream records with bounded replay-safe identity tracking and closed failure classification.\nCHANGELOG.md:22:- **events**: define the immutable version-one observation, usage, failure, summary, redaction, validation, and JSON record contract.\nCHANGELOG.md:23:- **events**: deterministically reduce normalized sessions, fold cumulative usage without double counting, preserve typed completion usage, and synthesize sanitized failure observations.\nCHANGELOG.md:24:- **events**: persist private normalized JSONL and decode bounded newline frames only after exact raw bytes are durably recorded, with observable sanitized fallbacks for oversized or failing frames.\nCHANGELOG.md:25:- **runtime**: resolve secure project, runtime, fleet, and evidence paths with validated limits and stable documented field order; probe required macOS process and durability capabilities; and publish, observe, prune, and conditionally remove identity-pinned fleet records behind inode-stable run locks without launch contention.\nCHANGELOG.md:26:- **runtime**: own shell-free process groups through persistent anchors, preserve descendant ownership and validated cleanup ancestry without mutating substituted paths, escalate timed-out groups from TERM to KILL through serialized bounded watchdogs, map supervisor signals to exit statuses, and durably remove matching ownership records while retaining evidence and lock files.\nCHANGELOG.md:27:- **runtime**: persist complete bounded raw session bytes; publish private metadata and summaries that reject unsafe identifiers, mismatches, non-UTC timestamps, and empty required fields; inventory retained evidence; and apply explicit active-safe purge plans with verified ancestry, locks, bounded malformed-row preservation, and durable deletion.\nCHANGELOG.md:28:- **runtime**: gate launches on durable emergency state-write evidence, preserve concurrent evidence, reject malformed or deeply nested records, revalidate evidence before acknowledgement, archive the exact acknowledged record, and restore the gate after failed acknowledgement.\nCHANGELOG.md:29:- **cli**: expose runtime status, actionable doctor resource checks, retained-log lookup/follow, non-applying purge previews, and explicit purge application; reject conflicting parent log options, omit internal path metadata, and reuse validated state for emergency acknowledgement.\nCHANGELOG.md:30:- Import-only package boundaries and a help-only `ovcaq` command.\nCHANGELOG.md:31:- Versioned v1 state schema/defaults and the exhaustive legacy-field crosswalk.\nCHANGELOG.md:32:- Closed v1 state validation with nested, resource, and cross-field invariants.\nCHANGELOG.md:33:- Locked state-store transactions with canonical publication, raw backups, and restore.\nCHANGELOG.md:34:- Monotonic revisions and locked compare-and-set conflict checks for transactions and restores.\nCHANGELOG.md:35:- Create-only initialization requires an existing runtime directory and repairs failed publications.\nCHANGELOG.md:36:- Pure JSON-path parsing and in-memory get/set/append/delete recovery operations.\nCHANGELOG.md:37:- Atomic StateService task, attempt, metadata, count, and contract-card commands.\nCHANGELOG.md:38:- Parsed-token protection for generic state recovery, with explicit unsafe override.\nCHANGELOG.md:39:- P01-T10 state CLI dispatch, stable errors, root discovery, and parser-derived command documentation.\nCHANGELOG.md:40:\nCHANGELOG.md:41:### Fixed\nCHANGELOG.md:42:\nCHANGELOG.md:43:- **events**: reject surrogate code points in shared observation and summary text before redaction or truncation while preserving valid Unicode scalars.\nCHANGELOG.md:44:- **cli**: reject unhealthy adapters before foreground agent execution using sanitized health diagnostics.\nCHANGELOG.md:45:- **tui**: show bounded normalized tool, message and plan activity alongside selecte