+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:44:42.764Z","ordinal":28,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a124c5-258a-77e0-a3ed-c37cff37bc64","turn_id":"01a124c5-25ff-7982-97ca-3dde672209d8","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-21e78fd8-07af-4fbf-88c8-8b4f941df82e","process_id":"80320","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import subprocess; paths=[\"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\", \"src/ovcaq/events/tail.py\", \"CHANGELOG.md\", \"src/ovcaq/events/model.py\", \"src/ovcaq/drivers/base.py\", \"src/ovcaq/drivers/codex.py\", \"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-2.txt\"]; print([(p,Path(p).stat().st_size) for p in paths]); subprocess.run([\"rg\", \"-n\", \"^\", \"src/ovcaq/events/tail.py\", \"CHANGELOG.md\"],timeout=60,check=True)'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import subprocess; paths=[\"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\", \"src/ovcaq/events/tail.py\", \"CHANGELOG.md\", \"src/ovcaq/events/model.py\", \"src/ovcaq/drivers/base.py\", \"src/ovcaq/drivers/codex.py\", \"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-2.txt\"]; print([(p,Path(p).stat().st_size) for p in paths]); subprocess.run([\"rg\", \"-n\", \"^\", \"src/ovcaq/events/tail.py\", \"CHANGELOG.md\"],timeout=60,check=True)'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"CHANGELOG.md:1:# Changelog\nCHANGELOG.md:2:\nCHANGELOG.md:3:All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\nCHANGELOG.md:4:\nCHANGELOG.md:5:The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).\nCHANGELOG.md:6:\nCHANGELOG.md:7:## [Unreleased]\nCHANGELOG.md:8:\nCHANGELOG.md:9:### Added\nCHANGELOG.md:10:\nCHANGELOG.md:11:- **drivers**: run supervised workflows with Codex, configured models and effort, verified version/authentication checks, and state-based phase handoffs.\nCHANGELOG.md:12:- **drivers**: show Codex activity, tools, receiver lanes and cache-aware usage with retained raw evidence; conflicting native threads fail safely even after supervisor ownership binding.\nCHANGELOG.md:13:- **tui**: add `ovcaq attach`, TTY-default attachment for `ovcaq run`, detachable interactive controls with plain fallback, and interactive `resume` that attaches to a live supervisor or launches once after a boundary pause.\nCHANGELOG.md:14:- **runtime**: run batch capabilities as durable provider-neutral attempts with private session evidence, final metrics, stale-owner reconciliation, and explicit one-attempt retry of failed capabilities.\nCHANGELOG.md:15:- **state**: add guarded compound supervisor mutations for pause/resume, progress fingerprints, capability attempts, failure attention, and empty-drain completion.\nCHANGELOG.md:16:- **runtime**: publish one immutable canonical metric row per phase or capability session, reconcile interrupted evidence deterministically, and project versioned metrics through legacy-compatible reports.\nCHANGELOG.md:17:- **config**: resolve provider-neutral build, review, and done routes with validated effort, timeout, model-tier, retry-policy, and literal prompt configuration; drivers now expose the version-two default-prompt contract.\nCHANGELOG.md:18:- **config**: load immutable per-agent argv, tier, environment, and JSON option settings with user/project merging and credential-shaped value rejection.\nCHANGELOG.md:19:- **drivers**: define the immutable provider-neutral launch, health, plugin, and discovery contracts with exact-version, duplicate-name, and fail-closed probe validation.\nCHANGELOG.md:20:- **drivers**: add the shell-free Claude launch adapter with explicit unattended permissions, configured tier and fallback resolution, isolated environment construction, executable health checks, and neutral summary reduction.\nCHANGELOG.md:21:- **drivers**: normalize Claude init, activity, tool, lane, usage, rate-limit, and terminal stream records with bounded replay-safe identity tracking and closed failure classification.\nCHANGELOG.md:22:- **events**: define the immutable version-one observation, usage, failure, summary, redaction, validation, and JSON record contract.\nCHANGELOG.md:23:- **events**: deterministically reduce normalized sessions, fold cumulative usage without double counting, preserve typed completion usage, and synthesize sanitized failure observations.\nCHANGELOG.md:24:- **events**: persist private normalized JSONL and decode bounded newline frames only after exact raw bytes are durably recorded, with observable sanitized fallbacks for oversized or failing frames.\nCHANGELOG.md:25:- **runtime**: resolve secure project, runtime, fleet, and evidence paths with validated limits and stable documented field order; probe required macOS process and durability capabilities; and publish, observe, prune, and conditionally remove identity-pinned fleet records behind inode-stable run locks without launch contention.\nCHANGELOG.md:26:- **runtime**: own shell-free process groups through persistent anchors, preserve descendant ownership and validated cleanup ancestry without mutating substituted paths, escalate timed-out groups from TERM to KILL through serialized bounded watchdogs, map supervisor signals to exit statuses, and durably remove matching ownership records while retaining evidence and lock files.\nCHANGELOG.md:27:- **runtime**: persist complete bounded raw session bytes; publish private metadata and summaries that reject unsafe identifiers, mismatches, non-UTC timestamps, and empty required fields; inventory retained evidence; and apply explicit active-safe purge plans with verified ancestry, locks, bounded malformed-row preservation, and durable deletion.\nCHANGELOG.md:28:- **runtime**: gate launches on durable emergency state-write evidence, preserve concurrent evidence, reject malformed or deeply nested records, revalidate evidence before acknowledgement, archive the exact acknowledged record, and restore the gate after failed acknowledgement.\nCHANGELOG.md:29:- **cli**: expose runtime status, actionable doctor resource checks, retained-log lookup/follow, non-applying purge previews, and explicit purge application; reject conflicting parent log options, omit internal path metadata, and reuse validated state for emergency acknowledgement.\nCHANGELOG.md:30:- Import-only package boundaries and a help-only `ovcaq` command.\nCHANGELOG.md:31:- Versioned v1 state schema/defaults and the exhaustive legacy-field crosswalk.\nCHANGELOG.md:32:- Closed v1 state validation with nested, resource, and cross-field invariants.\nCHANGELOG.md:33:- Locked state-store transactions with canonical publication, raw backups, and restore.\nCHANGELOG.md:34:- Monotonic revisions and locked compare-and-set conflict checks for transactions and restores.\nCHANGELOG.md:35:- Create-only initialization requires an existing runtime directory and repairs failed publications.\nCHANGELOG.md:36:- Pure JSON-path parsing and in-memory get/set/append/delete recovery operations.\nCHANGELOG.md:37:- Atomic StateService task, attempt, metadata, count, and contract-card commands.\nCHANGELOG.md:38:- Parsed-token protection for generic state recovery, with explicit unsafe override.\nCHANGELOG.md:39:- P01-T10 state CLI dispatch, stable errors, root discovery, and parser-derived command documentation.\nCHANGELOG.md:40:\nCHANGELOG.md:41:### Fixed\nCHANGELOG.md:42:\nCHANGELOG.md:43:- **events**: reject surrogate code points in shared observation and summary text before redaction or truncation while preserving valid Unicode scalars.\nCHANGELOG.md:44:- **cli**: reject unhealthy adapters before foreground agent execution using sanitized health diagnostics.\nCHANGELOG.md:45:- **tui**: show bounded normalized tool, message and plan activity alongside selected-session lanes with literal markup.\nCHANGELOG.md:46:\nCHANGELOG.md:47:- **tui**: surface selected-run observation read errors as gaps while preserving ownership checks and process-control exceptions.\nCHANGELOG.md:48:- **runtime**: keep standalone `run_once()` usable without full-loop ownership metadata while preserving supervisor identity across full-run sessions.\nCHANGELOG.md:49:- **runtime**: preserve unknown numeric usage in final metrics while retaining exact fields and strict validation of known values.\nCHANGELOG.md:50:- **tui**: fall back after ordinary interactive-view failures, detach plain viewers on real EOF, and print only changed frames while preserving terminal results.\nCHANGELOG.md:51:- **tui**: persist theme changes from both views, honor trusted XDG aliases, and use private no-follow theme I/O with replacement checks that tolerate concurrent readers.\nCHANGELOG.md:52:- **tui**: sanitize both fleet selectors and show stale/malformed registry counts and empty-fleet status without selecting a run.\nCHANGELOG.md:53:- **launcher**: recognize verified fast completion and attachment cleanup races, preserve bounded private startup diagnostics, honor configured runtime roots, and guide duplicate-owner failures to attach even while the new child is still starting.\nCHANGELOG.md:54:- **cli**: require explicit foreground mode for JSON runs and load viewer dependencies only for interactive commands.\nCHANGELOG.md:55:- **tui**: guard selected-run pause/resume through durable publication, reuse those controls for interactive resume, and honor the injected fleet registry for stop.\nCHANGELOG.md:56:- **runtime**: provide shared ownership exclusion for guarded state mutations, preserving state and backup bytes when a selected owner becomes stale during publication.\nCHANGELOG.md:57:- **tui**: keep controls responsive during observation reads and show elapsed selected-run duration instead of summed session times; terminal duration uses durable end evidence so late polls cannot inflate it.\nCHANGELOG.md:58:- **runtime**: bind terminal observations to the exact supervisor and revalidate evidence reads without competing for the launch lock or discarding ordinary active state progress.\nCHANGELOG.md:59:- **tui**: display normalized lane descriptions when an explicit lane label is absent.\nCHANGELOG.md:60:- **events**: bind normalized observations to the owning supervisor run and session while retaining exact native raw evidence.\nCHANGELOG.md:61:- **tui**: retain selected final state and telemetry after supervisor cleanup, reject replacement evidence, and render terminal outcomes before viewers exit.\nCHANGELOG.md:62:- **tui**: follow active session telemetry across rollover, retain stream damage diagnostics, preserve live usage and numeric costs, show the latest capability attempt's evidence path, and distinguish raw-only content without changing evidence presence flags.\nCHANGELOG.md:63:- **paths**: align workflow, runtime, report, launcher, and test defaults on the\nCHANGELOG.md:64:  `docs/dev/project-management` store tree.\nCHANGELOG.md:65:- **runtime**: keep supervisor session collection within style limits while preserving timeout evidence and classification.\nCHANGELOG.md:66:- **runtime**: honor supplied phase settings on every workflow launch while preserving agent overrides and literal prompts.\nCHANGELOG.md:67:- **workflow**: include canonical phase metrics in reports when usage is missing or malformed while excluding capability attempts from workflow totals.\nCHANGELOG.md:68:- **runtime**: share capability execution and failure evidence across pending runs and retries, honor bounded capability timeout precedence, and defer aggregate publication until completion.\nCHANGELOG.md:69:- **runtime**: persist operator stops until resume and halt state failures behind sanitized durable attention or an emergency restart barrier, preserving existing attention notices.\nCHANGELOG.md:70:- **runtime**: bound unchanged attempts across failure classes while preserving terminal halts, honor committed controls before capabilities and drain completion, and preserve phase-pause reasons on resume.\nCHANGELOG.md:71:- **runtime**: initialize batch identity before sessions, preserve capability failure and retry attention, and archive completed batches using the supervisor clock.\nCHANGELOG.md:72:\nCHANGELOG.md:73:- **events**: normalized evidence redacts `x-api-key`, `apiKey`, and other separator or case variants of API-key names, and raw fallback previews redact before truncating so no secret prefix survives the cut.\nCHANGELOG.md:74:- **events**: redaction stays linear on long unbroken text, and raw fallback previews read a bounded head of the frame, so one bad frame can no longer stall decoding or expose a secret cut at the frame limit.\nCHANGELOG.md:75:- **events**: credential assignments behind sensitive key names longer than 64 characters are redacted again.\nCHANGELOG.md:76:- **events**: raw fallback previews of a cut-off frame with no whitespace come out empty whenever an `sk-` token is in view, and short CRLF frames no longer carry the trailing CR.\nCHANGELOG.md:77:- **drivers**: a dated limit banner whose date does not exist in its year (such as Feb 29 in a non-leap year) yields no reset instead of jumping to a later leap year.\nCHANGELOG.md:78:- **drivers**: rate-limit warnings no longer clear a live limit, a rejected event's reset wins over the terminal banner, real clock-and-zone banners such as `resets 8:10pm (Europe/Prague)` yield a reset, and the limit window is structured payload data.\nCHANGELOG.md:79:- **drivers**: dated limit banners such as `resets Sep 20 at 11am (Europe/Prague)` yield a multi-day reset, and a terminal banner reset now applies after a rejected event that carried no credible future reset.\nCHANGELOG.md:80:- Agent configuration applies command defaults and shared validation; normalized text redacts bare credential tokens while preserving usage counters.\nCHANGELOG.md:81:- Deferred directory setup diagnostics report the full configured path while preserving the originating OS error.\nCHANGELOG.md:82:- Deferred publication revalidates the complete confirmed runtime ancestry before returning success.\nCHANGELOG.md:83:- Deferred ancestry confirmation detects replaced ancestors on reopen, supports search-only access, and avoids redundant ancestor creation and root confirmation.\nCHANGELOG.md:84:- Shared publication contention reports `publication busy; retry: <path>` for both reports and deferred ledgers.\nCHANGELOG.md:85:- Deferred retries and replays confirm existing runtime ancestry after abrupt exits and preserve directories created by concurrent callers when confirmation fails.\nCHANGELOG.md:86:- Deferred publication validates the complete prospective ledger and persists newly created runtime ancestors; overlapping report renders no longer lose successful sections.\nCHANGELOG.md:87:- Report JSON returns the complete published batch text after PRD updates and exact rerenders.\nCHANGELOG.md:88:- Deferred ledgers reject duplicate keys and excessive nesting; replaced sidecar locks refuse publication without losing competing appends.\nCHANGELOG.md:89:- Park/stall recovery retains the original PRD's filesystem identity through restart and preserves unfinished work on substitution.\nCHANGELOG.md:90:- Batch reports reconstruct all deferred details with PRD attribution; report, audit, and archive retries complete directory durability.\nCHANGELOG.md:91:- Blank decision content is omitted consistently from counts and audits; named payload and configuration files reject nonregular inputs promptly.\nCHANGELOG.md:92:- PRD moves atomically refuse concurrent held work; filesystem evidence remains checked through saga state publication.\nCHANGELOG.md:93:- Recovery validates batch identity and operation inputs before creating lifecycle directories or durable intent.\nCHANGELOG.md:94:- Installed workflow commands honor configured roots and active abstract tier keys, with explicit path and tier overrides.\nCHANGELOG.md:95:- Metric inputs reject FIFO/nonregular files promptly; systemic park pauses return a distinct halt status and actionable output.\nCHANGELOG.md:96:- Workflow orchestration, render sections, and installed/saga tests are split by responsibility while retaining failpoints and acceptance coverage.\nCHANGELOG.md:97:\nCHANGELOG.md:98:- Drained workflows remain terminal, and stall refuses conflicting recovery intents while park retains reconciliation behavior.\nCHANGELOG.md:99:- Workflow reports preserve unknown legacy totals, order equal-key metric rows deterministically, and reject nonregular output targets without blocking.\nCHANGELOG.md:100:- Deferred ledger publication and saga commit now verify the configured directory identity through durable writes and recovery.\nCHANGELOG.md:101:- State validation now uses canonical persisted-byte sizing, precise nested diagnostics, and cached type metadata.\nCHANGELOG.md:102:- CLI task payloads now reject non-object JSON, option abbreviations are disabled at every parser level, and resource limits use typed errors.\nCHANGELOG.md:103:- State transactions now overwrite mutator-supplied revisions before validation and close lock descriptors on every setup failure.\nCHANGELOG.md:104:- The installed state service now owns restore routing, and the protocol documents the complete schema, durability, and error contracts.\nCHANGELOG.md:105:- Project initialization now preserves existing config metadata and remains retryable when config creation fails.\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:1:\"\"\"Persist raw evidence before decoding bounded newline-delimited frames.\"\"\"\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:2:\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:3:import hashlib\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:4:import json\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:5:import os\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:6:import stat\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:7:from collections.abc import Callable, Mapping\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:8:from dataclasses import dataclass, replace\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:9:from datetime import UTC, datetime\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py:10:from pathlib 