+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T08:24:19.838Z","ordinal":23,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a124e9-ba7e-75e2-be34-73cf439d2001","call_id":"call_V8isGE2Qz9l7ejqF7tHhKv0X","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"996357\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002334,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2646,\"output\":\"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\\n1: ---\\n2: name: python-patterns\\n3: description: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \\\"pythonic\\\", \\\"PEP 8\\\", \\\"python best practices\\\", \\\"python idioms\\\", \\\"bandit\\\".\\n4: compatibility: \\\"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\\\"\\n5: ---\\n6: \\n7: # Python Patterns\\n8: \\n9: Pick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\\n10: \\n11: ## Idioms that earn their place\\n12: \\n13: | Rule | Why |\\n14: |------|-----|\\n15: | `X \\\\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\\n16: | `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\\n17: | `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\\n18: | `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\\\"During handling...\\\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\\n19: | `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\\n20: | `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\\n21: \\n22: ## Naming (PEP 8)\\n23: \\n24: `snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\\n25: \\n26: **Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\\n27: \\n28: ## Traps\\n29: \\n30: ```python\\n31: # Mutable default argument — shared across calls\\n32: def bad(items=[]): ...\\n33: def good(items=None):\\n34:     items = [] if items is None else items\\n35: \\n36: # Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\\n37: try: ...\\n38: except Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\\n39: \\n40: # __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\\n41: # memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\\n42: \\n43: # __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\\n44: # Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\\n45: \\n46: if value is None: ...             # never == None\\n47: ```\\n48: \\n49: Avoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\\n50: \\n51: ## Toolchain\\n52: \\n53: **black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \\\"obvious\\\" returns.\\n54: \\n55: ## Resources and laziness\\n56: \\n57: Context managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\\n58: \\n59: ## Security\\n60: \\n61: - Read secrets with `os.environ[\\\"API_KEY\\\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\\n62: - `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\\n63: - `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/tail.py\\n1: \\\"\\\"\\\"Persist raw evidence before decoding bounded newline-delimited frames.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n2: \\n3: import hashlib\\n4: import json\\n5: import os\\n6: import stat\\n7: from collections.abc import Callable, Mapping\\n8: from dataclasses import dataclass, replace\\n9: from datetime import UTC, datetime\\n10: from pathlib import Path\\n11: from typing import Literal, cast\\n12: \\n13: from ovcaq.drivers.base import AgentDriver\\n14: from ovcaq.events import (\\n15:     PROTOCOL_VERSION,\\n16:     Observation,\\n17:     ObservationType,\\n18:     observation_record,\\n19:     sanitize_text,\\n20: )\\n21: from ovcaq.events.model import has_invalid_unicode_scalar\\n22: from ovcaq.runtime.session import SessionEvidenceWriter\\n23: from ovcaq.state.schema import MAX_STATE_BYTES, JSONValue\\n24: \\n25: _PREVIEW_WINDOW_BYTES = 4096\\n26: \\n27: \\n28: class NormalizedEventWriter:\\n29:     \\\"\\\"\\\"Write sanitized observations as private, bounded JSONL evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n30: \\n31:     def __init__(self, path: Path, *, max_bytes: int, min_free_bytes: int) -> None:\\n32:         self._writer = SessionEvidenceWriter(\\n33:             path, max_bytes=max_bytes, min_free_bytes=min_free_bytes\\n34:         )\\n35: \\n36:     def write(self, observation: Observation) -> int:\\n37:         payload = json.dumps(\\n38:             observation_record(observation), ensure_ascii=False, allow_nan=False\\n39:         )\\n40:         return self._writer.write((payload + \\\"\\\\n\\\").encode(\\\"utf-8\\\"))\\n41: \\n42:     def flush(self) -> None:\\n43:         self._writer.flush()\\n44: \\n45:     def close(self) -> None:\\n46:         self._writer.close()\\n47: \\n48: \\n49: class RawFirstDecoder:\\n50:     \\\"\\\"\\\"Frame only durable raw bytes, retaining bounded previews on decode failure.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n51: \\n52:     def __init__(\\n53:         self,\\n54:         *,\\n55:         raw: SessionEvidenceWriter,\\n56:         normalized: NormalizedEventWriter,\\n57:         driver: AgentDriver,\\n58:         run_id: str,\\n59:         session_id: str | None = None,\\n60:         max_frame_bytes: int = 1024 * 1024,\\n61:     ) -> None:\\n62:         self._raw = raw\\n63:         self._normalized = normalized\\n64:         self._driver = driver\\n65:         self._run_id = run_id\\n66:         self._session_id = session_id\\n67:         self._bind_identity = session_id is not None\\n68:         self._max_frame_bytes = max_frame_bytes\\n69:         self._buffer = bytearray()\\n70:         self._length = 0\\n71:         self._digest = hashlib.sha256()\\n72:         self._last = b\\\"\\\"\\n73: \\n74:     def feed(self, chunk: bytes) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\\n75:         self._raw.write(chunk)\\n76:         self._raw.flush()\\n77:         emitted: list[Observation] = []\\n78:         offset = 0\\n79:         view = memoryview(chunk)\\n80:         while offset < len(chunk):\\n81:             newline = chunk.find(b\\\"\\\\n\\\", offset)\\n82:             end = len(chunk) if newline < 0 else newline\\n83:             segment = view[offset:end]\\n84:             if segment:\\n85:                 # Defer the last byte so CRLF framing excludes its CR from the\\n86:                 # digest, even when the CR and LF arrive in separate chunks.\\n87:                 self._digest.update(self._last)\\n88:                 self._digest.update(segment[:-1])\\n89:                 self._last = bytes(segment[-1:])\\n90:                 self._length += len(segment)\\n91:                 capacity = max(self._max_frame_bytes + 1, 512) - len(self._buffer)\\n92:                 self._buffer.extend(segment[:capacity])\\n93:             if newline < 0:\\n94:                 break\\n95:             emitted.extend(self._complete(terminated=True))\\n96:             offset = newline + 1\\n97:         return tuple(emitted)\\n98: \\n99:     def finish(self) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\\n100:         self._raw.flush()\\n101:         return self._complete(terminated=False) if self._length else ()\\n102: \\n103:     def _complete(self, *, terminated: bool) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\\n104:         trim_cr = terminated and self._last == b\\\"\\\\r\\\"\\n105:         length = self._length - int(trim_cr)\\n106:         if not trim_cr:\\n107:             self._digest.update(self._last)\\n108:         reason = \\\"frame exceeds byte limit\\\"\\n109:         observations: tuple[Observation, ...] | None = None\\n110:         if length <= self._max_frame_bytes:\\n111:             try:\\n112:                 frame = self._buffer[:length].decode(\\\"utf-8\\\")\\n113:             except UnicodeDecodeError:\\n114:                 reason = \\\"frame contains invalid UTF-8\\\"\\n115:             else:\\n116:                 try:\\n117:                     try:\\n118:                         record = json.loads(frame)\\n119:                     except json.JSONDecodeError:\\n120:                         record = None\\n121:                     if has_invalid_unicode_scalar(record):\\n122:                         reason = \\\"frame contains invalid Unicode scalar value\\\"\\n123:                     else:\\n124:                         # Consume lazy iterables before publishing any part of a frame.\\n125:                         observations = tuple(self._driver.decode(frame))\\n126:                 except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 - provider failures become observations\\n127:                     reason = \\\"driver failed to decode frame\\\"\\n128:         if observations is None:\\n129:             observations = (\\n130:                 Observation(\\n131:                     protocol_version=PROTOCOL_VERSION,\\n132:                     timestamp=datetime.now(UTC),\\n133:                     provider=self._driver.name,\\n134:                     run_id=self._run_id,\\n135:                     session_id=self._session_id,\\n136:                     lane_id=None,\\n137:                     type=ObservationType.RAW_UNKNOWN,\\n138:                     payload={\\n139:                         \\\"reason\\\": reason,\\n140:                         \\\"raw_sha256\\\": self._digest.hexdigest(),\\n141:                         \\\"preview\\\": self._preview(length),\\n142:                     },\\n143:                 ),\\n144:             )\\n145:         observations = self._bind_observations(observations)\\n146:         self._buffer.clear()\\n147:         self._length = 0\\n148:         self._digest = hashlib.sha256()\\n149:         self._last = b\\\"\\\"\\n150:         for observation in observations:\\n151:             self._normalized.write(observation)\\n152:             if observation.session_id is not None:\\n153:                 self._session_id = observation.session_id\\n154:         return observations\\n155: \\n156:     def _bind_observations(\\n157:         self, observations: tuple[Observation, ...]\\n158:     ) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\\n159:         if not self._bind_identity:\\n160:             return observations\\n161:         return tuple(\\n162:             replace(\\n163:                 observation,\\n164:                 run_id=self._run_id,\\n165:                 session_id=self._session_id,\\n166:                 payload=(\\n167:                     dict(observation.payload)\\n168:                     | {\\\"source_session_id\\\": observation.session_id}\\n169:                     if observation.type == ObservationType.SESSION_STARTED\\n170:                     and observation.session_id is not None\\n171:                     else observation.payload\\n172:                 ),\\n173:             )\\n174:             for observation in observations\\n175:         )\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"408446\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000001625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":236,\"output\":\"src/ovcaq/drivers/base.py:94:    def decode(self, raw_line: str) -> Iterable[Observation]: ...\\nsrc/ovcaq/events/model.py:77:def has_in