final metrics, stale-owner reconciliation, and explicit one-attempt retry of failed capabilities.\\n15: - **state**: add guarded compound supervisor mutations for pause/resume, progress fingerprints, capability attempts, failure attention, and empty-drain completion.\\n16: - **runtime**: publish one immutable canonical metric row per phase or capability session, reconcile interrupted evidence deterministically, and project versioned metrics through legacy-compatible reports.\\n17: - **config**: resolve provider-neutral build, review, and done routes with validated effort, timeout, model-tier, retry-policy, and literal prompt configuration; drivers now expose the version-two default-prompt contract.\\n18: - **config**: load immutable per-agent argv, tier, environment, and JSON option settings with user/project merging and credential-shaped value rejection.\\n19: - **drivers**: define the immutable provider-neutral launch, health, plugin, and discovery contracts with exact-version, duplicate-name, and fail-closed probe validation.\\n20: - **drivers**: add the shell-free Claude launch adapter with explicit unattended permissions, configured tier and fallback resolution, isolated environment construction, executable health checks, and neutral summary reduction.\\n21: - **drivers**: normalize Claude init, activity, tool, lane, usage, rate-limit, and terminal stream records with bounded replay-safe identity tracking and closed failure classification.\\n22: - **events**: define the immutable version-one observation, usage, failure, summary, redaction, validation, and JSON record contract.\\n23: - **events**: deterministically reduce normalized sessions, fold cumulative usage without double counting, preserve typed completion usage, and synthesize sanitized failure observations.\\n24: - **events**: persist private normalized JSONL and decode bounded newline frames only after exact raw bytes are durably recorded, with observable sanitized fallbacks for oversized or failing frames.\\n25: - **runtime**: resolve secure project, runtime, fleet, and evidence paths with validated limits and stable documented field order; probe required macOS process and durability capabilities; and publish, observe, prune, and conditionally remove identity-pinned fleet records behind inode-stable run locks without launch contention.\\n26: - **runtime**: own shell-free process groups through persistent anchors, preserve descendant ownership and validated cleanup ancestry without mutating substituted paths, escalate timed-out groups from TERM to KILL through serialized bounded watchdogs, map supervisor signals to exit statuses, and durably remove matching ownership records while retaining evidence and lock files.\\n27: - **runtime**: persist complete bounded raw session bytes; publish private metadata and summaries that reject unsafe identifiers, mismatches, non-UTC timestamps, and empty required fields; inventory retained evidence; and apply explicit active-safe purge plans with verified ancestry, locks, bounded malformed-row preservation, and durable deletion.\\n28: - **runtime**: gate launches on durable emergency state-write evidence, preserve concurrent evidence, reject malformed or deeply nested records, revalidate evidence before acknowledgement, archive the exact acknowledged record, and restore the gate after failed acknowledgement.\\n29: - **cli**: expose runtime status, actionable doctor resource checks, retained-log lookup/follow, non-applying purge previews, and explicit purge application; reject conflicting parent log options, omit internal path metadata, and reuse validated state for emergency acknowledgement.\\n30: - Import-only package boundaries and a help-only `ovcaq` command.\\n31: - Versioned v1 state schema/defaults and the exhaustive legacy-field crosswalk.\\n32: - Closed v1 state validation with nested, resource, and cross-field invariants.\\n33: - Locked state-store transactions with canonical publication, raw backups, and restore.\\n34: - Monotonic revisions and locked compare-and-set conflict checks for transactions and restores.\\n35: - Create-only initialization requires an existing runtime directory and repairs failed publications.\\n36: - Pure JSON-path parsing and in-memory get/set/append/delete recovery operations.\\n37: - Atomic StateService task, attempt, metadata, count, and contract-card commands.\\n38: - Parsed-token protection for generic state recovery, with explicit unsafe override.\\n39: - P01-T10 state CLI dispatch, stable errors, root discovery, and parser-derived command documentation.\\n40: \\n41: ### Fixed\\n42: \\n43: - **events**: retain native JSON frames containing invalid Unicode scalars as raw gaps before adapter state can change.\\n44: - **events**: reject surrogate code points in shared observation and summary text before redaction or truncation while preserving valid Unicode scalars.\\n45: - **cli**: reject unhealthy adapters before foreground agent execution using sanitized health diagnostics.\\n46: - **tui**: show bounded normalized tool, message and plan activity alongside selected-session lanes with literal markup.\\n47: \\n48: - **tui**: surface selected-run observation read errors as gaps while preserving ownership checks and process-control exceptions.\\n49: - **runtime**: keep standalone `run_once()` usable without full-loop ownership metadata while preserving supervisor identity across full-run sessions.\\n50: - **runtime**: preserve unknown numeric usage in final metrics while retaining exact fields and strict validation of known values.\\n51: - **tui**: fall back after ordinary interactive-view failures, detach plain viewers on real EOF, and print only changed frames while preserving terminal results.\\n52: - **tui**: persist theme changes from both views, honor trusted XDG aliases, and use private no-follow theme I/O with replacement checks that tolerate concurrent readers.\\n53: - **tui**: sanitize both fleet selectors and show stale/malformed registry counts and empty-fleet status without selecting a run.\\n54: - **launcher**: recognize verified fast completion and attachment cleanup races, preserve bounded private startup diagnostics, honor configured runtime roots, and guide duplicate-owner failures to attach even while the new child is still starting.\\n55: - **cli**: require explicit foreground mode for JSON runs and load viewer dependencies only for interactive commands.\\n56: - **tui**: guard selected-run pause/resume through durable publication, reuse those controls for interactive resume, and honor the injected fleet registry for stop.\\n57: - **runtime**: provide shared ownership exclusion for guarded state mutations, preserving state and backup bytes when a selected owner becomes stale during publication.\\n58: - **tui**: keep controls responsive during observation reads and show elapsed selected-run duration instead of summed session times; terminal duration uses durable end evidence so late polls cannot inflate it.\\n59: - **runtime**: bind terminal observations to the exact supervisor and revalidate evidence reads without competing for the launch lock or discarding ordinary active state progress.\\n60: - **tui**: display normalized lane descriptions when an explicit lane label is absent.\\n61: - **events**: bind normalized observations to the owning supervisor run and session while retaining exact native raw evidence.\\n62: - **tui**: retain selected final state and telemetry after supervisor cleanup, reject replacement evidence, and render terminal outcomes before viewers exit.\\n63: - **tui**: follow active session telemetry across rollover, retain stream damage diagnostics, preserve live usage and numeric costs, show the latest capability attempt's evidence path, and distinguish raw-only content without changing evidence presence flags.\\n64: - **paths**: align workflow, runtime, report, launcher, and test defaults on the\\n65:   `docs/dev/project-management` store tree.\\n66: - **runtime**: keep supervisor session collection within style limits while preserving timeout evidence and classification.\\n67: - **runtime**: honor supplied phase settings on every workflow launch while preserving agent overrides and literal prompts.\\n68: - **workflow**: include canonical phase metrics in reports when usage is missing or malformed while excluding capability attempts from workflow totals.\\n69: - **runtime**: share capability execution and failure evidence across pending runs and retries, honor bounded capability timeout precedence, and defer aggregate publication until completion.\\n70: - **runtime**: persist operator stops until resume and halt state failures behind sanitized durable attention or an emergency restart barrier, preserving existing attention notices.\\n71: - **runtime**: bound unchanged attempts across failure classes while preserving terminal halts, honor committed controls before capabilities and drain completion, and preserve phase-pause reasons on resume.\\n72: - **runtime**: initialize batch identity before sessions, preserve capability failure and retry attention, and archive completed batches using the supervisor clock.\\n73: \\n74: - **events**: normalized evidence redacts `x-api-key`, `apiKey`, and other separator or case variants of API-key names, and raw fallback previews redact before truncating so no secret prefix survives the cut.\\n75: - **events**: redaction stays linear on long unbroken text, and raw fallback previews read a bounded head of the frame, so one bad frame can no longer stall decoding or expose a secret cut at the frame limit.\\n76: - **events**: credential assignments behind sensitive key names longer than 64 characters are redacted again.\\n77: - **events**: raw fallback previews of a cut-off frame with no whitespace come out empty whenever an `sk-` token is in view, and short CRLF frames no longer carry the trailing CR.\\n78: - **drivers**: a dated limit banner whose date does not exist in its year (such as Feb 29 in a