+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T08:56:20.312Z","ordinal":67,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a12506-016b-7cd3-8623-7c626aa9ed07","turn_id":"01a12506-01bd-7992-a4dc-77d940f87b6d","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_055f70855de41c54016ac9fdb382a88191aaa62fb6dfdf94a7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The decoder checks native JSON strings before calling the adapter, so invalid Unicode becomes a raw gap without changing adapter state. Normalized writer failures propagate and trigger child cleanup; I’ll make that distinction explicit.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1791622579558,"completed_at_ms":1791622580312}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T08:56:20.315Z","ordinal":68,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_055f70855de41c54016ac9fdb382a88191aaa62fb6dfdf94a7","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The decoder checks native JSON strings before calling the adapter, so invalid Unicode becomes a raw gap without changing adapter state. Normalized writer failures propagate and trigger child cleanup; I’ll make that distinction explicit.\n"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12506-01bd-7992-a4dc-77d940f87b6d","create_time":1791622579.541224,"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]}},"metadata":{"retained_source":{"id":{"message_id":"msg_055f70855de41c54016ac9fdb382a88191aaa62fb6dfdf94a7","turn_id":"01a12506-01bd-7992-a4dc-77d940f87b6d","role":"assistant"},"revision":"retained_01a12507-085b-78d3-9a3e-e79a0236c931","complete":true},"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":6}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T08:56:33.411Z","ordinal":69,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_055f70855de41c54016ac9fdb481288191b33090580f7e9d4e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_142a30733c614fdf9ff027122a1fa071","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/docs/driver-protocol.md\\n@@\\n `PROTOCOL_VERSION` is exactly `1`. An `Observation` has a validated UTC\\n timestamp and identifiers, an `ObservationType`, and a deeply immutable\\n-payload. Version 1 observation types are:\\n+payload. Observation identifiers, payload strings and keys, and summary\\n+identifiers and failure details reject surrogate code points (`U+D800` through\\n+`U+DFFF`) with `ValueError` before redaction or truncation. `sanitize_json`\\n+performs the same recursive check, including values under sensitive keys;\\n+redaction cannot conceal invalid Unicode. Valid Unicode scalars, including\\n+non-BMP characters, remain accepted. Version 1 observation types are:\\n@@\\n-never reaches the preview. Malformed, oversized, unknown, or decoder-failing\\n-input is handled totally: it becomes a `raw.unknown` observation with a bounded\\n-sanitized preview and SHA-256 evidence instead of crashing the supervisor.\\n+never reaches the preview. Malformed, oversized, unknown, or decoder-failing\\n+frames produce `raw.unknown` observations with bounded sanitized previews and\\n+SHA-256 evidence. The raw-first decoder rejects invalid UTF-8 and checks parsed\\n+native JSON strings and keys recursively for invalid Unicode scalars before\\n+calling the driver. An invalid native string becomes a raw gap before the\\n+driver can mutate thread, usage, item, or lane state. Later valid frames can\\n+still complete the session; a gap alone is not a session failure.\\n+\\n+This recovery boundary covers input and ordinary driver decode exceptions.\\n+Raw evidence write/flush errors, normalized observation publication errors,\\n+and process-control exceptions propagate rather than becoming raw gaps. In\\n+particular, failure to publish a gap remains fatal and triggers cleanup of the\\n+live child; it must not be treated as recoverable input damage.\\n@@\\n File detail summarizes paths and change kinds; MCP and web detail is sanitized\\n and bounded to 4096 characters, rather than retained as wholesale results.\\n+Codex diagnostic details processed by `bounded_detail` remove terminal controls\\n+before credential redaction and the 4096-character bound. This order prevents\\n+controls inside a credential from hiding it from redaction or exposing a secret\\n+prefix at the truncation boundary.\\n*** Update File: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/CHANGELOG.md\\n@@\\n ### Fixed\\n \\n+- **runtime**: continue supervised sessions after native Unicode gaps while propagating normalized gap publication failures and cleaning up the live child.\\n - **drivers**: remove terminal controls before redacting and bounding Codex diagnostic details so split credentials cannot survive normalization.\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a12506-01bd-7992-a4dc-77d940f87b6d","create_time":1791622580.5774856}}}
