+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:41:48.733Z","ordinal":55,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a12530-0b4b-7bc1-bb9f-cbf937ca0337","turn_id":"01a12530-0f18-7dd0-be1b-bc3a1e3e56e4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9678a607-3412-45e5-84bb-a0dc1d3e06ac","process_id":"90870","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; s=json.loads(Path(\"docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json\").read_text()); [print(json.dumps(t,indent=2)) for t in s[\"tasks\"] if t[\"id\"] in s[\"rework_task_ids\"]]' "],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import json; from pathlib import Path; s=json.loads(Path(\"docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/state.json\").read_text()); [print(json.dumps(t,indent=2)) for t in s[\"tasks\"] if t[\"id\"] in s[\"rework_task_ids\"]]' "}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"name\": \"[D1] src/ovcaq/\",\n  \"description\": \"Source review: docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-review-1.md\\n\\nDisposition and bounded acceptance:\\nReview-cycle correction: the transmitted original strip-first recipe lost original regex word boundaries. This is a specification gap, not a capability failure. Preserve original-token redaction AND redact reconstructed tokens after removing the unchanged recognized controls, then cap to 4096. A bounded candidate is sanitize original detail, remove the existing controls, sanitize the full cleaned result, then truncate. Preserve classification/reset extraction from untouched full native text, all existing cap/control/Unicode regressions, and public signatures. Amend the design with a review-1 contract correction citing R5; retain its historical recipe/review evidence rather than erase it. Independently test C0/DEL/lone-ESC boundary destruction for bare tokens and Bearer values through helper and actual native normalized payloads/JSONL, plus original R2 control-split cap cases. Never weaken shared sanitizer boundaries or expand recognized control forms.\\n\\nR4 scan optimization must preserve original full-container scalar validation before redaction, valid non-BMP scalars and subclass handling. Avoid bypassing sanitize_json in a caller not already fully checked. A precompiled surrogate regex is sufficient if eliminating repeated validation risks the contract.\\n\\nR7 needs an independent native-parser reason/adapter-state assertion for a bounded deeply nested JSON frame that raises RecursionError in the preflight. R8 must preserve tolerant validation/decode handling and fatal publication boundaries; helper extraction inside the current catch is acceptable, literal hoisting that widens escaping failures is not.\\n\\nAcceptance: every quoted finding is resolved without scope expansion, all original source R7/R2 regressions remain pinned, and focused events/detail tests pass. Do not add cyclic-container guards or TUI changes. Keep the witnessed out-of-scope limitations in the review ledger.\\n\\n### Findings (verbatim)\\n- \\u26aa src/ovcaq/events/model.py:224: Hot-path scan cost. `_payload` scans the whole payload at line 224, then `sanitize_json` scans it again at line 252, and `_usage_payload` scans again through `sanitize_json`. Each scan uses a per-character Python generator: about 22 ms per MiB, against about 2.5 ms for a precompiled `re.compile(\\\"[\\\\ud800-\\\\udfff]\\\").search`. Every frame also gets re-validated by `replace()` in `_bind_observations` and by `observation_record` in the writer. Behavior-preserving fix: use the regex in the predicate, and call `_sanitize_json` inside `_payload` and `_usage_payload` once the up-front check has passed (found by: ALICE, BOB)\\n- \\ud83d\\udfe0 src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:64: Removing controls before redaction now leaks tokens that the old order caught. When a bare C0 control, DEL or lone ESC sits between a word character and a token, removal glues them together: `\\\"x\\\\x00sk-\\\" + \\\"a\\\"*30` becomes `xsk-aaaa\\u2026` and `\\\"auth\\\\x00Bearer \\\" + \\\"a\\\"*26` becomes `authBearer \\u2026`. `_LIKELY_SECRET` needs `\\\\b` before `sk-`/`Bearer`, so neither `bounded_detail` nor the Observation's second sanitizer redacts them. The old order redacted both, because the control supplied the word boundary. Confirmed by tracing the regex by hand; not executed (read-only sandbox) (found by: BOB)\\n- \\ud83d\\udfe1 src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:119: The preflight's `except (ValueError, RecursionError)` branch, which hands the frame to the driver, has no test. No RawFirstDecoder test feeds a deeply nested frame. Narrowing it to `except ValueError` would still pass the suite: deep frames would then get \\\"driver failed to decode frame\\\" instead of the driver's own native gap, against the contract's \\\"ValueError or RecursionError \\u2192 delegate unchanged\\\" (found by: BOB)\\n- \\ud83d\\udfe1 src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:116: The preflight parse and scan sit inside the tolerant driver catch, so the try blocks nest 4 levels deep (the limit). Hoist the `json.loads` try and the scalar check above it and wrap only `tuple(self._driver.decode(frame))` in `except Exception`. This also matches the contract's \\\"consume decode under the existing tolerant catch\\\" (found by: BOB)\\n\",\n  \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n  \"id\": \"6\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"src/ovcaq/events/model.py\",\n    \"src/ovcaq/events/tail.py\",\n    \"src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py\",\n    \"tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py\",\n    \"tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py\",\n    \"tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py\",\n    \"docs/dev/project-management/designs/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-design.md\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_by\": []\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"[D1] tests/events/\",\n  \"description\": \"Source review: docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-review-1.md\\n\\nDisposition and bounded acceptance:\\nRecord tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py in the design acceptance command beside tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py and tests/events/test_tail.py; do not move tests into a file exceeding 800 lines or rewrite the source PRD. Share the duplicated completion additions table while preserving independent construct/decode test paths and every assertion/case. Acceptance: every quoted finding no longer reproduces; named scalar/frame/tail tests pass and design command runs all relevant boundaries. Coordinate after task 6's design amendment.\\n\\n### Findings (verbatim)\\n- \\ud83d\\udfe1 tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py:1: The raw-first regressions (byte-exact raw output, gap digest/preview, unchanged adapter state, later healthy terminal) live in `tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py`. The PRD's Task 2 acceptance command (`pytest tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py tests/events/test_tail.py`) and its repository structure both name `test_unicode_safety.py`, so the PRD's own command does not run them. The full suite covers them, and the split keeps the file under 800 lines. Fix: record the file in the PRD or design acceptance text (found by: ALICE, BLAKE, BOB)\\n- \\ud83d\\udfe1 tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py:314: Duplicated test tables: the completion construct and record-decode tests repeat the same `additions` dict and body. Hoist it to one module constant or merge them into one test parametrized over construct vs decode (found by: BOB)\\n\",\n  \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n  \"id\": \"7\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"tests/events/test_unicode_safety.py\",\n    \"docs/dev/project-management/designs/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-design.md\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_by\": [\n    6\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"[D1] tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py\",\n  \"description\": \"Source review: docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-review-1.md\\n\\nDisposition and bounded acceptance:\\nReplace receiver-lane self-comparison/cap special casing with independently expected exact payload values; assert token/fragment absence against actual payload detail, not expected constants. Keep existing saved JSONL checks, all synthetic runtime fixture values and task 6's new boundary regressions. Acceptance: every quoted finding no longer reproduces, all helper/native/rate/lane tests pass, packaging scanner remains green; no production edits.\\n\\n### Findings (verbatim)\\n- \\ud83d\\udfe1 tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py:281: The receiver-lane test special-cases the exact cap input with `if detail != CAP_REPRODUCER`. It then calls `assert_safe_details(tmp_path, lanes, lane_detail)`, which compares the lane detail to itself, so the cap case never checks the exact redacted value or that `[REDACTED]` is present. I confirmed the actual lane detail equals the expected `\\\"x\\\"*4080 + \\\" [REDACTED]\\\"`. Simpler and stronger: drop the guard and call `assert_safe_details(tmp_path, lanes, expected)`. Related: `assert TOKEN not in expected` and `assert \\\"sk-abcdefghijkl\\\" not in expected` (lines 87-88) check fixed test data inside the loop. They should check `observation.payload[\\\"detail\\\"]` (found by: ALICE, BOB)\\n\",\n  \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n  \"id\": \"8\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_by\": [\n    6\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"name\": \"[D1] prose\",\n  \"description\": \"Source review: docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-review-1.md\\n\\nDisposition and bounded acceptance:\\nNarrow diagnostic-cleanup prose to the existing recognized ANSI/control forms and reflect task 6's reviewed redaction correction. Fold duplicated runtime continuation/publication wording into the events changelog entry. Keep source R7/R2 historical evidence, synthetic-token scope and genuine fatal-writer semantics. Broader TUI display-time reconstruction is already durably recorded in review-1, its settled ledger and deferred_decisions; do not implement it or widen PRD 00054 here. Acceptance: both quoted in-scope prose findings no longer reproduce; docs match actual behavior and no version/publication/provisioning changes occur.\\n\\n### Findings (verbatim)\\n- \\u26aa docs/driver-protocol.md:224: The same strip-after-redaction pattern survives outside `bounded_detail`. TUI `display_text` drops Cc/Cf characters after the sanitizer has already run. I checked that a NUL-split token in a Codex agent message (`codex_events.py:32`, where controls are never stripped) shows the full token on screen. So do ZWSP- and soft-hyphen-split tokens even in `bounded_detail` output, because format characters are not in its control regex. This is outside this PRD's scope (\\\"no speculative control forms\\\"), but the new doc sentence \\\"prevents controls inside a credential from hiding it from redaction\\\" claims more than the code delivers. Fix: narrow the wording to the recognized C0/DEL/CSI forms and file a follow-up PRD to re-sanitize at the display layer (found by: ALICE)\\n- \\u26aa CHANGELOG.md:43: The `**runtime**` changelog entry claims a runtime fix, but no runtime production code changed (Task 4 added tests only). It repeats the `**events**` gap entry. Fix: fold the continuation and propagation wording into the events entry (found by: ALICE)\\n\",\n  \"model\": \"sonnet\",\n  \"id\": \"9\",\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"files\": [\n    \"docs/driver-protocol.md\",\n    \"CHANGELOG.md\"\n  ],\n  \"blocked_by\": [\n    6\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":1750}},"started_at_ms":1791625308733,"completed_at_ms":1791625308733}}
