+{"timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:42:51.301Z","ordinal":12,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a12531-8f04-7a21-94cd-e7d92e06cb40","turn_id":"01a12531-8f5d-7810-996e-aebfda1b7247","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d707647f-9def-42e4-9fb7-84c2c2bb21a9","process_id":"84976","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-6.txt"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-6.txt","name":"dispatch-tess-6.txt","path":"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-6.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"You are writing tests for a feature. You have NOT seen any implementation and must NOT think about how to implement it.\n\nTask: [D1] src/ovcaq/\n\nDescription:\nTask 6 only. Public behavior: bounded_detail(detail: str) -> str must retain redaction of tokens separated from a preceding word by any recognized C0/DEL/lone ESC control, and redact tokens reconstructed when recognized controls occur inside a token. Test bare sk- credentials and Bearer values independently through helper, native error and turn.failed payloads and saved normalized JSONL. Preserve the original R2 cap input and 4096-character final cap, formatting and original-text classification/reset. RawFirstDecoder must delegate deeply nested native JSON unchanged when preflight json.loads raises RecursionError: assert the native parser gap reason, unchanged adapter state, durable raw bytes and normalized evidence. No expanded control forms, cycles or TUI changes.\nAllowed tests to edit: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/drivers/test_codex_detail_safety.py and /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/tests/events/test_unicode_frames.py. Read these two test files and /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/ovcaq/pyproject.toml only. Do not read production implementation. Reading budget: detail tests around lines 1-110 and 145-285; frame fixture lines 1-125 and delegation lines 275-320. Keep changes focused. Run only changed named tests -q --tb=line; do not commit or change state.\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\nOriginal-boundary and reconstructed-token inputs are redacted exactly; deep JSON preserves native delegation. All original cases remain unchanged.\n\nExisting test patterns (follow these conventions):\nimport json\nfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ovcaq.config import AgentSettings\nfrom ovcaq.drivers.codex import CodexDriver\nfrom ovcaq.drivers.codex_events import bounded_detail\nfrom ovcaq.events.model import Observation\nfrom ovcaq.events.tail import NormalizedEventWriter\n\nTOKEN = \"sk-\" + \"abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\"\nCAP_REPRODUCER = \"x\" * 4080 + \" sk-abc\\x1b[0mdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\"\nSPLIT_DETAILS = [\n    pytest.param(CAP_REPRODUCER, \"x\" * 4080 + \" [REDACTED]\", id=\"exact-cap\"),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Diagnostic sk-abc\\x1b[31mdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\",\n        \"Diagnostic [REDACTED]\",\n        id=\"ansi-split\",\n    ),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Diagnostic sk-abc\\x00defghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789ABCDEF\",\n        \"Diagnostic [REDACTED]\",\n        id=\"nul-split\",\n    ),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Bearer \" + TOKEN,\n        \"Bearer [REDACTED]\",\n        id=\"bearer\",\n    ),\n    pytest.param(\n        \"Diagnostic \\x1b]0;\" + TOKEN + \"\\x07 After\",\n        \"Diagnostic ]0;[REDACTED] After\",\n        id=\"osc-controls\",\n    ),\n    *[\n        pytest.param(\n            \"Before \" + token[:6] + control + token[6:] + \" After\",\n            \"Before [REDACTED] After\",\n            id=f\"alternate-{index}-{control_id}\",\n        )\n        for index, token in enumerate([\"sk-\" + \"Q7\" * 20, \"sk-\" + \"4bcD\" * 12])\n        for control_id, control in [\n            (\"plain\", \"\"),\n            (\"ansi\", \"\\x1b[0m\"),\n            (\"nul\", \"\\x00\"),\n        ]\n    ],\n]\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef driver() -> CodexDriver:\n    return CodexDriver(\n        AgentSettings(\n            name=\"codex\",\n            command=(\"fixture-wrapper\",),\n            tiers={\"standard\": \"fixture-model\"},\n            environment={},\n            options={},\n        ),\n        run_id=\"detail-safety-run\",\n    )\n\n\ndef decode_failure(\n    driver: CodexDriver, kind: str, detail: str\n) -> tuple[Observation, ...]:\n    record = (\n        {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": detail}\n        if kind == \"error\"\n        else {\"type\": \"turn.failed\", \"error\": {\"message\": detail}}\n    )\n    return driver.decode(json.dumps(record))\n\n\ndef assert_safe_details(\n    tmp_path: Path, observations: tuple[Observation, ...], expected: str\n) -> None:\n    assert observations\n    for observation in observations:\n        assert observation.payload[\"detail\"] == expected\n        assert len(observation.payload[\"detail\"]) <= 4096\n        assert \"\\x1b\" not in observation.payload[\"detail\"]\n        assert \"\\x00\" not in observation.payload[\"detail\"]\n        assert TOKEN not in expected\n        assert \"sk-abcdefghijkl\" not in expected\n    path = tmp_path / \"normalized.jsonl\"\n    writer = NormalizedEventWriter(path, max_bytes=1 << 20, min_free_bytes=0)\n    try:\n        for observation in observations:\n            writer.write(observation)\n        writer.flush()\n    finally:\n        writer.close()\n    saved = path.read_bytes()\n    assert TOKEN.encode() not in saved\n    assert b\"sk-abcdefghijkl\" not in saved\n    assert b\"\\\\u001b\" not in saved\n    assert b\"\\\\u0000\" not in saved\n    records = [json.loads(line) for line in saved.splitlines()]\n    assert len(records) == len(observations)\n    assert all(record[\"payload\"][\"detail\"] == expected for record in records)\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"detail\", \"expected\"), SPLIT_DETAILS)\ndef test_bounded