ted. Version 1 observation types are:\n \n - `session.started`, `session.completed`, and `session.failed`;\n - `activity.message`;\n@@ -95,8 +100,18 @@ bounded. A preview of a frame longer than its 512-byte window is cut back to\n the last whitespace; a window with no whitespace previews as empty when it\n contains `sk-` (case-insensitive) and is kept otherwise. A frame's trailing CR\n never reaches the preview. Malformed, oversized, unknown, or decoder-failing\n-input is handled totally: it becomes a `raw.unknown` observation with a bounded\n-sanitized preview and SHA-256 evidence instead of crashing the supervisor.\n+frames produce `raw.unknown` observations with bounded sanitized previews and\n+SHA-256 evidence. The raw-first decoder rejects invalid UTF-8 and checks parsed\n+native JSON strings and keys recursively for invalid Unicode scalars before\n+calling the driver. An invalid native string becomes a raw gap before the\n+driver can mutate thread, usage, item, or lane state. Later valid frames can\n+still complete the session; a gap alone is not a session failure.\n+\n+This recovery boundary covers input and ordinary driver decode exceptions.\n+Raw evidence write/flush errors, normalized observation publication errors,\n+and process-control exceptions propagate rather than becoming raw gaps. In\n+particular, failure to publish a gap remains fatal and triggers cleanup of the\n+live child; it must not be treated as recoverable input damage.\n \n `reduce_session` retains the observations and deterministically produces a\n `Reduction` containing a `SessionSummary`. `summary_record` serializes that\n@@ -206,6 +221,10 @@ Tool failure requires native failure/decline status, explicit native error or\n nonzero command exit. Ordinary command output is not provider-health evidence.\n File detail summarizes paths and change kinds; MCP and web detail is sanitized\n and bounded to 4096 characters, rather than retained as wholesale results.\n+Codex diagnostic details processed by `bounded_detail` remove terminal controls\n+before credential redaction and the 4096-character bound. This order prevents\n+controls inside a credential from hiding it from redaction or exposing a secret\n+prefix at the truncation boundary.\n \n Collaboration requires `agents_states` keys matching native receiver thread\n IDs. Pending/running receivers start or progress a lane, completed receivers","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a3c0b3f-796d-46ef-a146-a96b9508aedd","uuid":"87363b8e-0eac-4027-ad39-1329451b51a2","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:17:37.177Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"commit 9e3953791465ec9ae9b78497a8f3389915964fa0\nAuthor: Tomáš Bouška <tomas@buvis.net>\nDate:   Sat Oct 10 10:57:45 2026 +0200\n\n    docs(drivers): clarify Unicode recovery and publication boundaries\n\ndiff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md\nindex 38067d6..648cc59 100644\n--- a/CHANGELOG.md\n+++ b/CHANGELOG.md\n@@ -40,6 +40,7 @@ The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/).\n \n ### Fixed\n \n+- **runtime**: continue supervised sessions after native Unicode gaps while propagating normalized gap publication failures and cleaning up the live child.\n - **drivers**: remove terminal controls before redacting and bounding Codex diagnostic details so split credentials cannot survive normalization.\n - **events**: retain native JSON frames containing invalid Unicode scalars as raw gaps before adapter state can change.\n - **events**: reject surrogate code points in shared observation and summary text before redaction or truncation while preserving valid Unicode scalars.\ndiff --git a/docs/driver-protocol.md b/docs/driver-protocol.md\nindex 4f3c329..fd4fcb5 100644\n--- a/docs/driver-protocol.md\n+++ b/docs/driver-protocol.md\n@@ -53,7 +53,12 @@ strict: there are no compatibility shims or dual writers.\n \n `PROTOCOL_VERSION` is exactly `1`. An `Observation` has a validated UTC\n timestamp and identifiers, an `ObservationType`