+Source review: docs/dev/project-management/reviews/00051-triage-a-single-valid-codex-record-can-crash-th-v1-review-1.md
+
+Disposition and bounded acceptance:
+Review-cycle correction: the transmitted original strip-first recipe lost original regex word boundaries. This is a specification gap, not a capability failure. Preserve original-token redaction AND redact reconstructed tokens after removing the unchanged recognized controls, then cap to 4096. A bounded candidate is sanitize original detail, remove the existing controls, sanitize the full cleaned result, then truncate. Preserve classification/reset extraction from untouched full native text, all existing cap/control/Unicode regressions, and public signatures. Amend the design with a review-1 contract correction citing R5; retain its historical recipe/review evidence rather than erase it. Independently test C0/DEL/lone-ESC boundary destruction for bare tokens and Bearer values through helper and actual native normalized payloads/JSONL, plus original R2 control-split cap cases. Never weaken shared sanitizer boundaries or expand recognized control forms.
+
+R4 scan optimization must preserve original full-container scalar validation before redaction, valid non-BMP scalars and subclass handling. Avoid bypassing sanitize_json in a caller not already fully checked. A precompiled surrogate regex is sufficient if eliminating repeated validation risks the contract.
+
+R7 needs an independent native-parser reason/adapter-state assertion for a bounded deeply nested JSON frame that raises RecursionError in the preflight. R8 must preserve tolerant validation/decode handling and fatal publication boundaries; helper extraction inside the current catch is acceptable, literal hoisting that widens escaping failures is not.
+
+Acceptance: every quoted finding is resolved without scope expansion, all original source R7/R2 regressions remain pinned, and focused events/detail tests pass. Do not add cyclic-container guards or TUI changes. Keep the witnessed out-of-scope limitations in the review ledger.
+
+### Findings (verbatim)
+- ⚪ src/ovcaq/events/model.py:224: Hot-path scan cost. `_payload` scans the whole payload at line 224, then `sanitize_json` scans it again at line 252, and `_usage_payload` scans again through `sanitize_json`. Each scan uses a per-character Python generator: about 22 ms per MiB, against about 2.5 ms for a precompiled `re.compile("[\ud800-\udfff]").search`. Every frame also gets re-validated by `replace()` in `_bind_observations` and by `observation_record` in the writer. Behavior-preserving fix: use the regex in the predicate, and call `_sanitize_json` inside `_payload` and `_usage_payload` once the up-front check has passed (found by: ALICE, BOB)
+- 🟠 src/ovcaq/drivers/codex_events.py:64: Removing controls before redaction now leaks tokens that the old order caught. When a bare C0 control, DEL or lone ESC sits between a word character and a token, removal glues them together: `"x\x00sk-" + "a"*30` becomes `xsk-aaaa…` and `"auth\x00Bearer " + "a"*26` becomes `authBearer …`. `_LIKELY_SECRET` needs `\b` before `sk-`/`Bearer`, so neither `bounded_detail` nor the Observation's second sanitizer redacts them. The old order redacted both, because the control supplied the word boundary. Confirmed by tracing the regex by hand; not executed (read-only sandbox) (found by: BOB)
+- 🟡 src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:119: The preflight's `except (ValueError, RecursionError)` branch, which hands the frame to the driver, has no test. No RawFirstDecoder test feeds a deeply nested frame. Narrowing it to `except ValueError` would still pass the suite: deep frames would then get "driver failed to decode frame" instead of the driver's own native gap, against the contract's "ValueError or RecursionError → delegate unchanged" (found by: BOB)
+- 🟡 src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:116: The preflight parse and scan sit inside the tolerant driver catch, so the try blocks nest 4 levels deep (the limit). Hoist the `json.loads` try and the scalar check above it and wrap only `tuple(self._driver.decode(frame))` in `except Exception`. This also matches the contract's "consume decode under the existing tolerant catch" (found by: BOB)
