+CLOSURE | resolved | "Hot-path scan cost. `_payload` scans the whole payload at line 224, then `sanitize_json` scans it again at line 252, and `_usage_payload` scans again through `sanitize_json`." | `model.py` now uses `_INVALID_UNICODE_SCALAR.search(current)` in place of the per-character generator, which is the regex swap the task text calls sufficient. The container walk and subclass handling are untouched, and the repeated scans still run so original-container validation stays intact.
+
+CLOSURE | resolved | "Removing controls before redaction now leaks tokens that the old order caught... `"x\x00sk-" + "a"*30` becomes `xsk-aaaa…`" | `bounded_detail` now runs `sanitize_text(protected)` before control removal, so original word boundaries are kept, and `sanitize_text(cleaned)` runs again before `[:4096]`. Lone ESC is masked to NUL so a redaction marker cannot form a new CSI. The new `CONTROL_DETAILS` cases (C0, DEL and ESC, bare and Bearer, at the boundary and inside the token) run through the helper and through native payloads and JSONL, and the recorded run passed.
+
+CLOSURE | resolved | "The preflight's `except (ValueError, RecursionError)` branch, which hands the frame to the driver, has no test." | `test_deep_json_recursion_preserves_native_gap_and_durable_evidence` first asserts `json.loads` raises `RecursionError` on the 100k-deep frame. It then asserts the gap payload equals the driver's own native gap, which carries its own reason, and is not the invalid-scalar reason. It also checks adapter state is unchanged and raw and normalized evidence is saved. Narrowing the catch to `ValueError` would send the frame to the outer "driver failed to decode frame" path and change the payload, so this test would fail.
+
+CLOSURE | resolved | "The preflight parse and scan sit inside the tolerant driver catch, so the try blocks nest 4 levels deep (the limit)." | The inner `try/except` moved into `_has_invalid_json_scalar`, which removes one nesting level. The call stays inside the existing tolerant `try`, which the task text allows ("helper extraction inside the current catch is acceptable"). Publication failures still propagate outside it.
+
+NO FINDINGS
